"site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/commit/ccbeb17107c3cc81352cf4f663a14fcf6ccbba6b","node_id":"C_kwDORN37UdoAKGNjYmViMTcxMDdjM2NjODEzNTJjZjRmNjYzYTE0ZmNmNmNjYmJhNmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/commit/cf7fab44db19582b5da7575d5e376a5f41f55dab","sha":"cf7fab44db19582b5da7575d5e376a5f41f55dab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/commits/cf7fab44db19582b5da7575d5e376a5f41f55dab"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/commit/fd426ae76d9dae017138094b996c5643fe3ae92b","sha":"fd426ae76d9dae017138094b996c5643fe3ae92b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/commits/fd426ae76d9dae017138094b996c5643fe3ae92b"}],"sha":"ccbeb17107c3cc81352cf4f663a14fcf6ccbba6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/commits/ccbeb17107c3cc81352cf4f663a14fcf6ccbba6b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/commits/fd426ae76d9dae017138094b996c5643fe3ae92b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T06:24:15Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T06:24:15Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Tanakh LaMetayel: upload images and publish to Storage, keeping every version\n\nStorage is now enabled on the project, so the two paths that were written to\nstop short of it are finished.\n\nImages: the upload button now opens a file picker and uploads. The file is\ndownscaled to a 1600px long edge and converted to WebP in the browser first,\nso a heavy scan does not become a slow app; a format that cannot be converted\nor a conversion that comes out larger falls back to the original, and a failed\nconversion never blocks the upload. The entry stores the full download URL\nrather than the path, so both the CMS and the app resolve it without knowing\nthe bucket: a src starting with http is remote, anything else is a baked id.\nRemoving an image detaches it without deleting the file, so reverting changes\ncannot leave an entry pointing at a deleted file.\n\nPublish: the pack is uploaded to published/live.json or published/preview.json\nand meta/publish is written. Every live version is also archived to\npublished/archive/live-0007.json, zero padded so sorting by name sorts by\nversion. The archive copy is written before the channel, so a failure midway\nleaves a backup without a channel rather than a channel without a backup. The\npanel lists the saved versions and can restore one to the live channel.\n\nAvailability is now derived from the configured bucket instead of a manual\nVITE_TLM_STORAGE_ENABLED flag, which could otherwise disagree with reality;\nthe flag survives only as an escape hatch to force it off.\n\nRestore is the one path that reads a file from Storage into the browser and so\nthe only one CORS can block. Its failure is reported as the one-time bucket\nsetting it is, with the fix in the docs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011enfES8cCygECGBSr5nsas","tree":{"sha":"dc764e09bf65f667b76d4d8ed5b37e1cd9fac5c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/git/trees/dc764e09bf65f667b76d4d8ed5b37e1cd9fac5c4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/git/commits/fd426ae76d9dae017138094b996c5643fe3ae92b","verification":{"payload":"tree dc764e09bf65f667b76d4d8ed5b37e1cd9fac5c4\nparent cf7fab44db19582b5da7575d5e376a5f41f55dab\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790231055 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790231055 +0000\n\nTanakh LaMetayel: upload images and publish to Storage, keeping every version\n\nStorage is now enabled on the project, so the two paths that were written to\nstop short of it are finished.\n\nImages: the upload button now opens a file picker and uploads. The file is\ndownscaled to a 1600px long edge and converted to WebP in the browser first,\nso a heavy scan does not become a slow app; a format that cannot be converted\nor a conversion that comes out larger falls back to the original, and a failed\nconversion never blocks the upload. The entry stores the full download URL\nrather than the path, so both the CMS and the app resolve it without knowing\nthe bucket: a src starting with http is remote, anything else is a baked id.\nRemoving an image detaches it without deleting the file, so reverting changes\ncannot leave an entry pointing at a deleted file.\n\nPublish: the pack is uploaded to published/live.json or published/preview.json\nand meta/publish is written. Every live version is also archived to\npublished/archive/live-0007.json, zero padded so sorting by name sorts by\nversion. The archive copy is written before the channel, so a failure midway\nleaves a backup without a channel rather than a channel without a backup. The\npanel lists the saved versions and can restore one to the live channel.\n\nAvailability is now derived from the configured bucket instead of a manual\nVITE_TLM_STORAGE_ENABLED flag, which could otherwise disagree with reality;\nthe flag survives only as an escape hatch to force it off.\n\nRestore is the one path that reads a file from Storage into the browser and so\nthe only one CORS can block. Its failure is reported as the one-time bucket\nsetting it is, with the fix in the docs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011enfES8cCygECGBSr5nsas\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMTSfJr4\n6H8lLuy0KL5YAxUVdWtWWc3PfshqeF75sA2v1B7dgesgtvQbIY72twnSMRmujZsY/2gOrIT5li1e\ngQg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T06:24:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"