s_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/commit/062b225181d5a56867837872bbb2b08afde25c56","node_id":"C_kwDORN37UdoAKDA2MmIyMjUxODFkNWE1Njg2NzgzNzg3MmJiYjJiMDhhZmRlMjVjNTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/commit/a06d425d04f9f288dbb175ddd6fdc55b53194ace","sha":"a06d425d04f9f288dbb175ddd6fdc55b53194ace","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/commits/a06d425d04f9f288dbb175ddd6fdc55b53194ace"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/commit/0b50504cbe51e8bf791d8a126df498af006c54ac","sha":"0b50504cbe51e8bf791d8a126df498af006c54ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/commits/0b50504cbe51e8bf791d8a126df498af006c54ac"}],"sha":"062b225181d5a56867837872bbb2b08afde25c56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/commits/062b225181d5a56867837872bbb2b08afde25c56"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/commits/0b50504cbe51e8bf791d8a126df498af006c54ac/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T11:26:52Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T11:26:52Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Tanakh LaMetayel: attach an image that is already in the system\n\nIn the printed guide a redirect entry (\"ראה X\") shares a page with the\nfull entry below it, and the import hung several photos on the redirect\ninstead. Fixing one means moving a photo from one entry to another, and\nthe editor could only remove: upload waits on Storage, and there was no\nway to attach a photo that already exists. e0149 סלעם carries the moth\nthat belongs to e0150 סס, עש; e0499 שריון carries the Sharon coast.\n\nThe library is every image already on an entry — all 650 of them are —\nso nothing new has to be indexed. Search runs over the caption first,\nthen the holding entry''s title, then the file id: whoever is looking\nfor the photo of \"עש הבגדים\" knows what is written under it, not what\nthe file is called. The caption travels with the photo, because it was\nwritten for the photo and not for the entry that happened to hold it.\n\nfindImages lives in the model layer with its own tests — an image on\nseveral entries appears once, one already on this entry is skipped, and\nthe list stops at a length that can still be read at a glance.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013S5f5PMiDgEfYaPY2y9vaj","tree":{"sha":"36884306fcc31ca129791c194f862cdb3b0e1112","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/git/trees/36884306fcc31ca129791c194f862cdb3b0e1112"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/git/commits/0b50504cbe51e8bf791d8a126df498af006c54ac","verification":{"payload":"tree 36884306fcc31ca129791c194f862cdb3b0e1112\nparent a742cad78296be23fd972cbd82046170cbb4d899\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790076412 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790076412 +0000\n\nTanakh LaMetayel: attach an image that is already in the system\n\nIn the printed guide a redirect entry (\"ראה X\") shares a page with the\nfull entry below it, and the import hung several photos on the redirect\ninstead. Fixing one means moving a photo from one entry to another, and\nthe editor could only remove: upload waits on Storage, and there was no\nway to attach a photo that already exists. e0149 סלעם carries the moth\nthat belongs to e0150 סס, עש; e0499 שריון carries the Sharon coast.\n\nThe library is every image already on an entry — all 650 of them are —\nso nothing new has to be indexed. Search runs over the caption first,\nthen the holding entry''s title, then the file id: whoever is looking\nfor the photo of \"עש הבגדים\" knows what is written under it, not what\nthe file is called. The caption travels with the photo, because it was\nwritten for the photo and not for the entry that happened to hold it.\n\nfindImages lives in the model layer with its own tests — an image on\nseveral entries appears once, one already on this entry is skipped, and\nthe list stops at a length that can still be read at a glance.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013S5f5PMiDgEfYaPY2y9vaj\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPYstR/L\nT4AAJTKy2TZcClYNO3edXbsoVes7O3hCUkWN6+EULGTUVnUTApB86ENCJSAehOARPSJ8vBY8Kfns\n3As=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T11:27:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/commit/0b50504cbe51e8bf791d8a126df498af006c54ac","node_id":"C_kwDORN37UdoAKDBiNTA1MDRjYmU1MWU4YmY3OTFkOGExMjZkZjQ5OGFmMDA2YzU0YWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/commit/a742cad78296be23fd972cbd82046170cbb4d899","sha":"a742cad78296be23fd972cbd82046170cbb4d899","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/commits/a742cad78296be23fd972cbd82046170cbb4d899"}],"sha":"0b50504cbe51e8bf791d8a126df498af006c54ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/commits/0b50504cbe51e8bf791d8a126df498af006c54ac"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/commits/a742cad78296be23fd972cbd82046170cbb4d899/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T10:55:32Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T10:55:32Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Tanakh LaMetayel: repair broken references against the Tanakh text\n\nWhat cleanRefs left behind are lines whose book name is right and whose\nnumbers the scan destroyed: \"חבקוק ה, ח\" where Habakkuk has three\nchapters, \"דברי הימים א\" with no chapter at all. Fixing one means\nknowing what the entry is about — and the text itself can be asked.\nThe whole Tanakh is already baked into the app, and the entry''s name is\na word that appears in the verse. \"דרור · ויקרא מט\" resolves to\nויקרא כה, י, because that is where \"וקראתם דרור בארץ\" is written.\n\nTwo kinds of evidence, and only their intersection counts as settled:\nsearching the book for the entry''s name, and reading the damaged\nnumbers structurally (\"מלכים א לח, מה\" is chapter 1 verse 38, not\nchapter 38). Every structural guess is checked against the book before\nit is offered.\n\nTwo rules earn their place by the false positives they caught when the\nfirst version ran over the real content:\n\n  - A term must appear as a word, with at most one prefix letter.\n    Without that, \"ציץ\" matched inside \"מציץ מן החרכים\" and produced a\n    confident proposal for an unrelated verse. Mem is not in the prefix\n    set: every participle opens with it.\n  - A chapter that exists in the book is evidence. When only the verse\n    overflowed, a lone hit in some other chapter drops to review rather\n    than being written.\n\ncertain is not proof, and the script says so: in \"תרצה\" the word stands\nin דברים לג, יא as a verb, not as the place. So the report prints the\nverse beside every proposal, and --write touches only the line itself,\nafter backing up every entry.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013S5f5PMiDgEfYaPY2y9vaj","tree":{"sha":"0e8e3958438b0ac66ba9d0f879d4c9e97f5b695f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/git/trees/0e8e3958438b0ac66ba9d0f879d4c9e97f5b695f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/git/commits/a742cad78296be23fd972cbd82046170cbb4d899","verification":{"payload":"tree 0e8e3958438b0ac66ba9d0f879d4c9e97f5b695f\nparent a06d425d04f9f288dbb175ddd6fdc55b53194ace\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790074532 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790074532 +0000\n\nTanakh LaMetayel: repair broken references against the Tanakh text\n\nWhat cleanRefs left behind are lines whose book name is right and whose\nnumbers the scan destroyed: \"חבקוק ה, ח\" where Habakkuk has three\nchapters, \"דברי הימים א\" with no chapter at all. Fixing one means\nknowing what the entry is about — and the text itself can be asked.\nThe whole Tanakh is already baked into the app, and the entry''s name is\na word that appears in the verse. \"דרור · ויקרא מט\" resolves to\nויקרא כה, י, because that is where \"וקראתם דרור בארץ\" is written.\n\nTwo kinds of evidence, and only their intersection counts as settled:\nsearching the book for the entry''s name, and reading the damaged\nnumbers structurally (\"מלכים א לח, מה\" is chapter 1 verse 38, not\nchapter 38). Every structural guess is checked against the book before\nit is offered.\n\nTwo rules earn their place by the false positives they caught when the\nfirst version ran over the real content:\n\n  - A term must appear as a word, with at most one prefix letter.\n    Without that, \"ציץ\" matched inside \"מציץ מן החרכים\" and produced a\n    confident proposal for an unrelated verse. Mem is not in the prefix\n    set: every participle opens with it.\n  - A chapter that exists in the book is evidence. When only the verse\n    overflowed, a lone hit in some other chapter drops to review rather\n    than being written.\n\ncertain is not proof, and the script says so: in \"תרצה\" the word stands\nin דברים לג, יא as a verb, not as the place. So the report prints the\nverse beside every proposal, and --write touches only the line itself,\nafter backing up every entry.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013S5f5PMiDgEfYaPY2y9vaj\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQD7P8pvT\nNV3OmWGvIq8sM+SvWHWaVqG5UwzB+6hiliOzjOg/6MovULhMAj/DOv/DVhy5+sbIQ7ICRe0OHI4J\nCAU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T10:55:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/oth