,"html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/commits/2d3be782b1b7b2cd3c8aa1a6442013e64c863c2d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T10:43:04Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T10:43:04Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Tanakh LaMetayel: say \"fragment\" when a moved line is one, not \"caption\"\n\nOf the 66 lines the cleanup moves to the notes, 38 are not photo captions at\nall — they are reference fragments: a footnote number and a chapter whose\nbook name stayed on the previous line of the page (\"93 י\", \"308 מח\"), or a\nlone Hebrew numeral (\"יח\"). Moving them is still right, since a line reading\n\"93 י\" is noise in a citation list either way, but calling them captions was\nwrong.\n\nThe reason travels with the line into the entry''s notes and stays there, so\nan editor reading it later needs it to be true. A fragment now says so, and\nthe AI-assisted stage can use that as its worklist.\n\nThe test is a leading digit, or one or two bare Hebrew numerals — not\n\"short\", which would have swept up captions like \"קשת בשמי הארץ\".\n\n28 captions, 38 fragments, 22 from empty redirects.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013S5f5PMiDgEfYaPY2y9vaj","tree":{"sha":"6ba96b8c30909ac121393867585ca72581406715","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/git/trees/6ba96b8c30909ac121393867585ca72581406715"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/git/commits/2d3be782b1b7b2cd3c8aa1a6442013e64c863c2d","verification":{"payload":"tree 6ba96b8c30909ac121393867585ca72581406715\nparent 735dd325e625ddbc214754e74e2c4cc446757177\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789641784 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789641784 +0000\n\nTanakh LaMetayel: say \"fragment\" when a moved line is one, not \"caption\"\n\nOf the 66 lines the cleanup moves to the notes, 38 are not photo captions at\nall — they are reference fragments: a footnote number and a chapter whose\nbook name stayed on the previous line of the page (\"93 י\", \"308 מח\"), or a\nlone Hebrew numeral (\"יח\"). Moving them is still right, since a line reading\n\"93 י\" is noise in a citation list either way, but calling them captions was\nwrong.\n\nThe reason travels with the line into the entry''s notes and stays there, so\nan editor reading it later needs it to be true. A fragment now says so, and\nthe AI-assisted stage can use that as its worklist.\n\nThe test is a leading digit, or one or two bare Hebrew numerals — not\n\"short\", which would have swept up captions like \"קשת בשמי הארץ\".\n\n28 captions, 38 fragments, 22 from empty redirects.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013S5f5PMiDgEfYaPY2y9vaj\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOOnxoE6\nJsT9heqs4rnKnJ4KFmHPaiXT3chQzQoWQmF93ydOrSHGOVuucnndvro73zdcxvJBKZsn7FijS5DW\npg4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T10:43:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}",