n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T09:43:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/commit/0f5ebb779baf2cf5630d261888b1b299c347e487","node_id":"C_kwDORN37UdoAKDBmNWViYjc3OWJhZjJjZjU2MzBkMjYxODg4YjFiMjk5YzM0N2U0ODc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/commit/6dcc201aa31eeca3dc5a0589f70482bb23995ab3","sha":"6dcc201aa31eeca3dc5a0589f70482bb23995ab3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/commits/6dcc201aa31eeca3dc5a0589f70482bb23995ab3"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/commit/ccad724d1f8ddde423fbe0d717dca8717fbc841e","sha":"ccad724d1f8ddde423fbe0d717dca8717fbc841e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/commits/ccad724d1f8ddde423fbe0d717dca8717fbc841e"}],"sha":"0f5ebb779baf2cf5630d261888b1b299c347e487","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/commits/0f5ebb779baf2cf5630d261888b1b299c347e487"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/commits/ccad724d1f8ddde423fbe0d717dca8717fbc841e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T09:24:26Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T09:24:26Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Tanakh LaMetayel: script to clean up scanned reference lists\n\nCitation lists are the hardest thing on the page for OCR — small type,\nHebrew numerals, footnote markers glued on. Of 6,456 references carried over,\n5,919 are clean and 334 are whole-chapter citations (also correct); 91 are\nout of range and 112 have no book name at all.\n\nThe script only touches the two patterns that can be identified with\ncertainty: a line with no book name in it (almost always a photo caption\nthat landed in the wrong column), and references sitting on an empty\nredirect entry. The emptiness test matters — the migration left redirect\nentries that also swallowed a neighbour''s body, and e0063 \"ענף עץ עבות\"\nholds the entire \"עץ\" entry along with its 61 references, which do belong\nto the content inside it.\n\nNothing is deleted. Each moved line goes to the entry''s internal notes,\nwhich are never published, under a fixed header — so it leaves the citation\nlist the reader sees and can still be put back.\n\nEverything else is reported, not touched: an out-of-range chapter, and\nfragments like \"308 מח\" where the book name stayed on the previous line of\nthe page. Fixing those means knowing what the entry is about, and a guess\nthere is worse than leaving it broken; they are for a human or for the\nAI-assisted stage.\n\nWith --write a backup of every entry is written first, and only changed\nentries are saved. Reference and note changes are outside sourceHash, so\nthis does not mark translations stale.\n\nAgainst the current content: 59 entries change, 134 lines move (112 with no\nbook, 22 from 8 empty redirects), and 135 lines in 94 entries are reported\nfor human eyes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013S5f5PMiDgEfYaPY2y9vaj","tree":{"sha":"1819ecdf5aa052c2f2e64406261f9329ca80a491","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/git/trees/1819ecdf5aa052c2f2e64406261f9329ca80a491"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/git/commits/ccad724d1f8ddde423fbe0d717dca8717fbc841e","verification":{"payload":"tree 1819ecdf5aa052c2f2e64406261f9329ca80a491\nparent 6dcc201aa31eeca3dc5a0589f70482bb23995ab3\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789637066 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789637066 +0000\n\nTanakh LaMetayel: script to clean up scanned reference lists\n\nCitation lists are the hardest thing on the page for OCR — small type,\nHebrew numerals, footnote markers glued on. Of 6,456 references carried over,\n5,919 are clean and 334 are whole-chapter citations (also correct); 91 are\nout of range and 112 have no book name at all.\n\nThe script only touches the two patterns that can be identified with\ncertainty: a line with no book name in it (almost always a photo caption\nthat landed in the wrong column), and references sitting on an empty\nredirect entry. The emptiness test matters — the migration left redirect\nentries that also swallowed a neighbour''s body, and e0063 \"ענף עץ עבות\"\nholds the entire \"עץ\" entry along with its 61 references, which do belong\nto the content inside it.\n\nNothing is deleted. Each moved line goes to the entry''s internal notes,\nwhich are never published, under a fixed header — so it leaves the citation\nlist the reader sees and can still be put back.\n\nEverything else is reported, not touched: an out-of-range chapter, and\nfragments like \"308 מח\" where the book name stayed on the previous line of\nthe page. Fixing those means knowing what the entry is about, and a guess\nthere is worse than leaving it broken; they are for a human or for the\nAI-assisted stage.\n\nWith --write a backup of every entry is written first, and only changed\nentries are saved. Reference and note changes are outside sourceHash, so\nthis does not mark translations stale.\n\nAgainst the current content: 59 entries change, 134 lines move (112 with no\nbook, 22 from 8 empty redirects), and 135 lines in 94 entries are reported\nfor human eyes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013S5f5PMiDgEfYaPY2y9vaj\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMNVdeaP\nNGeLlwlJ9X4SKyDzDDxsZu2acNN0KKRu5b3NVw0jGPBpUzzEz8gHvKwVv/QAv125S8EnKdMFVWJw\n+gU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T09:24:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https