\n\nSaving to stage, copying to prod and publishing are three separate steps,\nand none of the text said so. Each message described the mechanism —\nFirestore, the Bagel, sync timestamps — so nothing told the editor the\none thing that decides whether she is done: whether the change has\nreached the people davening.\n\nEvery message in that flow now answers that. The toolbar tooltips number\nthe steps and say what each one does not yet accomplish. The publish\ndialog asks \"publish to the congregation?\" rather than \"publish to the\nBagel of prod\", and its detail line says this is the step that reaches\nreal users.\n\nSpecific corrections:\n\n- The stage save reported \"saved successfully (local)\". It is not local;\n  it goes to the stage server. It now says saved to stage, not yet with\n  the congregation.\n- The prod-is-newer warning ended with \"see the console\", which nobody\n  opens. It now explains that those documents will be left untouched,\n  why that happens, and to stop and check if that is unexpected.\n- The list header now leads with the fact that publishing aligns prod to\n  stage, so everything saved to stage since the last publish goes out —\n  other people''s edits included — and asks for the list to be read.\n- The preview-failed message says the failure is in the preview only, the\n  publish still does its own comparison, and what is lost is seeing it\n  first.\n- Publish success now names what actually happened, including \"nothing\n  needed copying\" rather than staying silent about it.\n\n\"Bagel\" no longer appears in anything the editor reads. It is the\ninternal transport, and the app has moved off it for sync anyway.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XrnJgebU4Wx5yTzPfq3s3W","tree":{"sha":"577188e7f4c56a4473fda9806b2808b722e9b4d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/git/trees/577188e7f4c56a4473fda9806b2808b722e9b4d3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/git/commits/6616f9245d00b88b192eb10139d8fc9f67d6589f","verification":{"payload":"tree 577188e7f4c56a4473fda9806b2808b722e9b4d3\nparent 50b695d0ddd24c3282617880b4be730d144b3c00\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789043487 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789043487 +0000\n\nRewrite the publish and save messages around who sees the change\n\nSaving to stage, copying to prod and publishing are three separate steps,\nand none of the text said so. Each message described the mechanism —\nFirestore, the Bagel, sync timestamps — so nothing told the editor the\none thing that decides whether she is done: whether the change has\nreached the people davening.\n\nEvery message in that flow now answers that. The toolbar tooltips number\nthe steps and say what each one does not yet accomplish. The publish\ndialog asks \"publish to the congregation?\" rather than \"publish to the\nBagel of prod\", and its detail line says this is the step that reaches\nreal users.\n\nSpecific corrections:\n\n- The stage save reported \"saved successfully (local)\". It is not local;\n  it goes to the stage server. It now says saved to stage, not yet with\n  the congregation.\n- The prod-is-newer warning ended with \"see the console\", which nobody\n  opens. It now explains that those documents will be left untouched,\n  why that happens, and to stop and check if that is unexpected.\n- The list header now leads with the fact that publishing aligns prod to\n  stage, so everything saved to stage since the last publish goes out —\n  other people''s edits included — and asks for the list to be read.\n- The preview-failed message says the failure is in the preview only, the\n  publish still does its own comparison, and what is lost is seeing it\n  first.\n- Publish success now names what actually happened, including \"nothing\n  needed copying\" rather than staying silent about it.\n\n\"Bagel\" no longer appears in anything the editor reads. It is the\ninternal transport, and the app has moved off it for sync anyway.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XrnJgebU4Wx5yTzPfq3s3W\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMA3pR0W\nMYSYfBIfjKG/5sRKUrQRz5J6E8yft/gz0V6QupjL3eUO41GjwSh57VJuIG42rkoSGI398NJYE5VP\njg8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-10T12:31:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/commit/6616f9245d00b88b192eb10139d8fc9f67d6589f","node_id":"C_kwDORN37UdoAKDY2MTZmOTI0NWQwMGI4OGIxOTJlYjEwMTM5ZDhmYzlmNjdkNjU4OWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/commit/50b695d0ddd24c3282617880b4be730d144b3c00","sha":"50b695d0ddd24c3282617880b4be730d144b3c00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/commits/50b695d0ddd24c3282617880b4be730d144b3c00"}],"sha":"6616f9245d00b88b192eb10139d8fc9f67d6589f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/commits/6616f9245d00b88b192eb10139d8fc9f67d6589f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/commits/50b695d0ddd24c3282617880b4be730d144b3c00/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T11:59:05Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T11:59:05Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Say plainly why an empty publish is still worth doing\n\nWhen the comparison finds nothing to copy, the dialog said \"prod is\nalready up to date\" and, in small grey text, that publishing would still\nupdate the sync timestamp so devices re-check. Two things were unclear.\n\n\"46 documents scanned\" read as the size of the whole nusach. It is not:\noutside a first run the scan covers only what changed in stage since the\nlast publish. The line now says so, and distinguishes a first full\ncomparison, nothing-changed, and the singular case.\n\nAnd an empty result read as \"nothing to do here\", when publishing is\nexactly what is still missing — copying documents and telling devices are\nseparate steps, and without the second the content sits in prod unread.\nThat is now its own highlighted note rather than a grey footnote, in\nterms of what reaches the people davening.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XrnJgebU4Wx5yTzPfq3s3W","tree":{"sha":"adac0793bab98f32001ecd9673160a969d47b78d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/git/trees/adac0793bab98f32001ecd9673160a969d47b78d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/koren-workspace/AppKorenCMS/git/commits/50b695d0ddd24c3282617880b4be730d144b3c00","verification":{"payload":"tree adac0793bab98f32001ecd9673160a969d47b78d\nparent 217fdd68053faf169e2e061d86648561835368e3\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789041545 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789041545 +0000\n\nSay plainly why an empty publish is still worth doing\n\nWhen the comparison finds nothing to copy, the dialog said \"prod is\nalready up to date\" and, in small grey text, that publishing would still\nupdate the sync timestamp so devices re-check. Two things were unclear.\n\n\"46 documents scanned\" read as the size of the whole nusach. It is not:\noutside a first run the scan covers only what changed in stage since the\nlast publish. The line now says so, and distinguishes a first full\ncomparison, nothing-changed, and the singular case.\n\nAnd an empty result read as \"nothing to do here\", when publishing is\nexactly what is still missing — copying documents and telling devices are\nseparate steps, and without the second the content sits in prod unread.\nThat is now its own highlighted note rather than a grey footnote, in\nterms of what reaches the people davening.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XrnJgebU4Wx5yTzPfq3s3W\n","reason":"valid","signature":"--