ketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/c7d1b5a803a40b50f950dbbd63e1873ccf728545"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/130109357?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-savage/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-savage/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-savage/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-savage/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dylan-savage","id":130109357,"login":"dylan-savage","node_id":"U_kgDOB8FPrQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-savage/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-savage/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-savage/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-savage/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-savage/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-savage","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/b10d8c54976d6fb6e4d5ac6b151808082dc7ccc1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T21:13:48Z","email":"130109357+dylan-savage@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dylan Savage"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T21:13:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(shell): end the dev-preview hold and name unresolvable apps (#2460) (#2506)\n\nAn App Builder preview (framed, ?appid=...&rrdev=1) held its splash until\nthe embedder''s dev registration arrived, with no deadline and for any app\nid, and that hold masked \"App not found\", every load error and the boot\nwatchdog. A wrong app id and a dev build that never arrived both left a\nsilent, endless rocket; unknown ids never even reached the 300s load\ntimeout.\n\n- The hold now covers only the session-locked app and ends 30s after page\n  load (DEV_REMOTE_TIMEOUT_MS), one deadline shared by the layout and the\n  loader. App Builder mounts the preview only once its dev server serves\n  and injects on shell:devReady, so a healthy registration lands within a\n  second or two; a late one still self-corrects.\n- After the hold, the preview says which failure it is: no dev build\n  arrived (with the id to check), or the dev build failed to load. A 404\n  for a listed app no longer claims the app \"isn''t installed\".\n- Every unresolvable id now leaves a console warning, which App Builder\n  mirrors into its Console pane: the not-found surface, a registration for\n  a different id than the locked one, a malformed registration, and a\n  switchApp to an unknown id.\n\nFixes #2460\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"65e9e0b68b4482eef21065919236329cdb547d0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/trees/65e9e0b68b4482eef21065919236329cdb547d0f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/commits/b10d8c54976d6fb6e4d5ac6b151808082dc7ccc1","verification":{"payload":"tree 65e9e0b68b4482eef21065919236329cdb547d0f\nparent ed115cdfebaf7fc121f4de6063f2a1dfcc95107e\nauthor Dylan Savage <130109357+dylan-savage@users.noreply.github.com> 1791148428 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791148428 -0700\n\nfix(shell): end the dev-preview hold and name unresolvable apps (#2460) (#2506)\n\nAn App Builder preview (framed, ?appid=...&rrdev=1) held its splash until\nthe embedder''s dev registration arrived, with no deadline and for any app\nid, and that hold masked \"App not found\", every load error and the boot\nwatchdog. A wrong app id and a dev build that never arrived both left a\nsilent, endless rocket; unknown ids never even reached the 300s load\ntimeout.\n\n- The hold now covers only the session-locked app and ends 30s after page\n  load (DEV_REMOTE_TIMEOUT_MS), one deadline shared by the layout and the\n  loader. App Builder mounts the preview only once its dev server serves\n  and injects on shell:devReady, so a healthy registration lands within a\n  second or two; a late one still self-corrects.\n- After the hold, the preview says which failure it is: no dev build\n  arrived (with the id to check), or the dev build failed to load. A 404\n  for a listed app no longer claims the app \"isn''t installed\".\n- Every unresolvable id now leaves a console warning, which App Builder\n  mirrors into its Console pane: the not-found surface, a registration for\n  a different id than the locked one, a malformed registration, and a\n  switchApp to an unknown id.\n\nFixes #2460\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwsGMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtMEQAIwZ/sK4nCK3M3KJgiBpwzps\nGhcAGQtVmZPBwjn/gEFnAHINV9o4+h0fg3WQwTuj3qFbxzJndHZTdcI0z31Gkz9N\nK2dNdPcTxDETLgwDq1Fes3IaZE7DvALpi1K66FxthC7vxvVPZramo93VGJYQIObn\nKlYyOJ5CdScVx5b21gyQjElPloGU3f3Q0INySGksomQrjMizODmHbOv1TPJiCVrO\nYf/Jt+Jl/CvopeICBon2FwG3GPGATWzXxHD2axNECS4mnc9lm0pYkYg1CmbOggod\nIxQiNqBZNI/4EXBKqa381fk7p7e+FnoYqnss9iOBI8MIJi+E95mVP5JbxSKYO49J\nn1JKRKwtMd1jnC66ZrV1VXAeqRFQuDXqKtOF3i312cE+wyqXLwROUMtRL8cxn/9n\n7fkd1WzNmo3egAPWQ8HpvVgbzQ02qDxuByvyBWwCqOPHen+RkhH02Z6z8fPB/X+k\nCcy/5+oGyYZQ34uCwbcq4BtQMyaw25RbPDzFFzdZmUO5gPwqR8CIDjGHdwA8NJaQ\nEtoMk5IHKG4EhF2ICiW8jtV3h5LFmFIZclMJ3EG109wPXBKZeSt+sSPCY4uSzZ7D\nOBd/NR23B99zA3y5BMpEwiZH/pwOKd4wcZu41Pgnaa5KT5aWObhxMHnVTY7E/fpj\nxZzpg8JMOzNSxHtiHTN3\n=HNJm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T21:13:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commit/b10d8c54976d6fb6e4d5ac6b151808082dc7ccc1","node_id":"C_kwDOROCxS9oAKGIxMGQ4YzU0OTc2ZDZmYjZlNGQ1YWM2YjE1MTgwODA4MmRjN2NjYzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commit/ed115cdfebaf7fc121f4de6063f2a1dfcc95107e","sha":"ed115cdfebaf7fc121f4de6063f2a1dfcc95107e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/ed115cdfebaf7fc121f4de6063f2a1dfcc95107e"}],"sha":"b10d8c54976d6fb6e4d5ac6b151808082dc7ccc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/b10d8c54976d6fb6e4d5ac6b151808082dc7ccc1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184572825?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leela8256/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leela8256/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leela8256/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leela8256/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leela8256","id":184572825,"login":"Leela8256","node_id":"U_kgDOCwBbmQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leela8256/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leela8256/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leela8256/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leela8256/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leela8256/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leela8256","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/ed115cdfebaf7fc121f4de6063f2a1dfcc95107e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T06:24:10Z","email":"leelaprasad.dammalapati@sjsu.edu","name":"Leela8256"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T06:24:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(nodes): say tool_python has no network access where builders look (#2509)\n\nThe Python tool runs in a RestrictedPython sandbox with no network,\nfilesystem or subprocess access by default, but only the node README\nsaid so. State it in the node description the pipeline editor shows and\nin the tool description the LLM reads, and point to tool_http_request\nfor web calls and tool_daytona for code that needs network access or\nextra packages.\n\nAlso drop the \"network scans\" example from the timeout help text, since\nthe sandbox cannot reach the network, and note that Additional Allowed\nModules has no effect on RocketRide Cloud (sandbox.py drops the extra\nmodules under --hosted).\n\nStrings only; no logic changes. The generated Schema table in README.md\ncatches up when nodes:docs-generate next runs on develop.\n\nFixes #2467\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1abf08e49422479fe2d0079d763e88058c128d08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/trees/1abf08e49422479fe2d0079d763e88058c128d08"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/commits/ed115cdfebaf7fc121f4de6063f2a1dfcc95107e","verification":{"payload":"tree 1abf08e49422479fe2d0079d763e88058c128d08\nparent da5ac853e37de34d6e6a486a9fb989748b4e2219\nauthor Leela8256 <leelaprasad.dammalapati@sjsu.edu> 1791095050 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791095050 -0700\n\ndocs(nodes): say tool_python has no network access where builders look (#2509)\n\nThe Python tool runs in a RestrictedPython sandbox with no network,\nfilesystem or subprocess access by default, but only the node README\nsaid so. State it in the node description the pipeline editor shows and\nin the tool description the LLM reads, and point to tool_http_request\nfor web calls and tool_daytona for code that needs network access or\nextra packages.\n\nAlso drop the \"network scans\" example from the timeout help text, since\nthe sandbox cannot reach the network, and note that Additional Allowed\nModules has no effect on RocketRide Cloud (sandbox.py drops the extra\nmodules under --hosted).\n\nStrings only; no logic changes. The generated Schema table in README.md\ncatches up when nodes:docs-generate next runs on develop.\n\nFixes #2467\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwfEKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAt2MQABBJqf0NfI90i4x55T1Xt7yP\nYMQQktyvHtueSFUIMJM5Rqq1M7D+DULj0IlivLv3ff7LFUyZ3eeBVo18kyz7NHWU\nmqBKxV9j5BaDoaBuOsnsEvKTSb9x0cm4Lf4mWDcbQiw8zk+W2CsqdcuJ9g2JYbMB\nXjqM63TrJN5gqHd26omrQWsiQ2yX9/kH9+iwXLhzqluTgOGkaqvAQhx/VtQhQsJ7\nhJ4b77n9dkY+qwhwOJnQi4Lv3gYO8sjIzCBzQnuc5tjg0KDBa91F5Zvd9mErySNt\n32/H2QZgwKMcSfCOGmAa8vPwm/mit7XD2C51dpCwkuukiHAsi3zve/9iJGLqTpS0\nwBBeN5Q1UE3hhd9w38uaWvHedx4DbB+ud0O66t1O1yijktV3MzsKJrt6730HMNa+\n6fh9qtTXd+AAjdNYxGDqL8/wLFnCcaMqkh5hiDKc/KmrD8V5SFnwLPmnB/Z7MgLb\nEZ2q2myMOeWYB/ISMHUN4eEZ4is/wf80sMLcTch6UGgED5iePWbuA1VUfrmsd1u5\neMld3ycBRajqEEfKTdUZBGZWvOjlVvyqqAmbm13nYmpNDxmahLGhV/JKupiRjU2O\nXYxzDetwDpV1NbgNqucET58cNI4ZRZE+LGQZSz25fcHj+ySelaptcphjcEYs9wTy\nR8uzpxHEnfT0fxz805h2\n=bz9i\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T06:24:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commit/ed115cdfebaf7fc121f4de6063f2a1dfcc95107e","node_id":"C_kwDOROCxS9oAKGVkMTE1Y2RmZWJhZjdmYzEyMWY0ZGU2MDYzZjJhMWRmY2M5NTEwN2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commit/da5ac853e37de34d6e6a486a9fb989748b4e2219","sha":"da5ac853e37de34d6e6a486a9fb989748b4e2219","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/da5ac853e37de34d6e6a486a9fb989748b4e2219"}],"sha":"ed115cdfebaf7fc121f4de6063f2a1dfcc95107e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/ed115cdfebaf7fc121f4de6063f2a1dfcc95107e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/130109357?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-savage/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-savage/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-savage/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-savage/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dylan-savage","id":130109357,"login":"dylan-savage","node_id":"U_kgDOB8FPrQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-savage/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-savage/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-savage/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-savage/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-savage/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-savage","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/da5ac853e37de34d6e6a486a9fb989748b4e2219/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T22:22:19Z","email":"130109357+dylan-savage@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dylan Savage"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T22:22:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: remove em dashes from user-facing UI copy (#2505)\n\n* chore(shell): remove em dashes from user-facing copy\n\nEm dashes across the shell UI read as machine-written to external users\n(#2470). Rewrite each one in banners, dialogs, settings and environment\nsubtitles, Monitor tab descriptions, checkout, and data-grid column\ntooltips with the punctuation the sentence needs: a colon after a label,\na period between independent clauses, parentheses for asides. Also fix\nthe one double-hyphen stand-in on the Profile panel.\n\nComments, console logs, developer-only invariant errors and lone \"no\nvalue\" placeholder dashes are unchanged. The session-expired assertions\nin connection.test.ts follow the new wording.\n\nRefs #2470\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(ui): remove em dashes from shared UI components\n\nRewrite the em dashes in user-visible copy across the shared components\n(#2470): deploy and schedule panels, endpoint info modal and its\nintegration examples, canvas configuration snackbars, trace and play-bar\nlabels, and the project status, source and log panes. Includes the\n&mdash; entities and — escapes, which a plain search misses.\n\nLone \"no value\" placeholder dashes in tiles and table cells are kept, as\nare comments and console logs.\n\nRefs #2470\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(appdev): remove em dashes from App Builder views\n\nRewrite the em dashes in the App Builder Dashboard, Deploy, Design,\nPackage, Store and plan views (#2470). Tab subtitles keep their label\nform with a colon (\"Package: everything this app needs ...\"), and lists\nthat already followed a colon move into parentheses so no sentence\ncarries two colons.\n\nRefs #2470\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(appdev): remove em dashes from component gallery docs\n\nThe App Builder component gallery renders each entry''s doc string on\nscreen, so its em dashes are user-facing too (#2470). Definition bullets\nnow use one pattern (\"- **Sidebar**: ...\"), and mid-sentence dashes\nbecome periods, semicolons, commas or parentheses as the sentence needs.\n\nRefs #2470\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(vscode): remove em dashes from extension copy\n\nRewrite the em dashes in VS Code notifications, status-bar tooltips,\nwebview text, App Builder readiness notes and error messages surfaced\nto the user, plus the four retired-setting deprecation messages in\npackage.json (#2470). The checkout description shared by the Project,\nAccount and Cloud panels now reads the same everywhere; two of those\ncopies used a double hyphen in place of the dash.\n\nOutput-channel and App Builder console log lines, and the headers\nwritten into generated service scripts, are unchanged.\n\nRefs #2470\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(apps): remove em dashes from sql-ui, chat widget and bundled apps\n\nRewrite the em dashes in user-visible copy in sql-ui, the chat widget,\nand the hello, test, profiler, explorer and world apps (#2470). The\nsql-ui README quoted two of the changed strings (\"Will run: nothing\n(editor is empty)\" and the \"Generated preview: review, then Run\"\nbanner) and is updated to match.\n\nRefs #2470\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"18e950cd232985b9a56066cf402dd0bfa236f53d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/trees/18e950cd232985b9a56066cf402dd0bfa236f53d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/commits/da5ac853e37de34d6e6a486a9fb989748b4e2219","verification":{"payload":"tree 18e950cd232985b9a56066cf402dd0bfa236f53d\nparent 8f27ea89c0af7f97cdaa81d49fb9ba55f45a8b68\nauthor Dylan Savage <130109357+dylan-savage@users.noreply.github.com> 1790979739 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790979739 +0000\n\nchore: remove em dashes from user-facing UI copy (#2505)\n\n* chore(shell): remove em dashes from user-facing copy\n\nEm dashes across the shell UI read as machine-written to external users\n(#2470). Rewrite each one in banners, dialogs, settings and environment\nsubtitles, Monitor tab descriptions, checkout, and data-grid column\ntooltips with the punctuation the sentence needs: a colon after a label,\na period between independent clauses, parentheses for asides. Also fix\nthe one double-hyphen stand-in on the Profile panel.\n\nComments, console logs, developer-only invariant errors and lone \"no\nvalue\" placeholder dashes are unchanged. The session-expired assertions\nin connection.test.ts follow the new wording.\n\nRefs #2470\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(ui): remove em dashes from shared UI components\n\nRewrite the em dashes in user-visible copy across the shared components\n(#2470): deploy and schedule panels, endpoint info modal and its\nintegration examples, canvas configuration snackbars, trace and play-bar\nlabels, and the project status, source and log panes. Includes the\n&mdash; entities and — escapes, which a plain search misses.\n\nLone \"no value\" placeholder dashes in tiles and table cells are kept, as\nare comments and console logs.\n\nRefs #2470\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(appdev): remove em dashes from App Builder views\n\nRewrite the em dashes in the App Builder Dashboard, Deploy, Design,\nPackage, Store and plan views (#2470). Tab subtitles keep their label\nform with a colon (\"Package: everything this app needs ...\"), and lists\nthat already followed a colon move into parentheses so no sentence\ncarries two colons.\n\nRefs #2470\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(appdev): remove em dashes from component gallery docs\n\nThe App Builder component gallery renders each entry''s doc string on\nscreen, so its em dashes are user-facing too (#2470). Definition bullets\nnow use one pattern (\"- **Sidebar**: ...\"), and mid-sentence dashes\nbecome periods, semicolons, commas or parentheses as the sentence needs.\n\nRefs #2470\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(vscode): remove em dashes from extension copy\n\nRewrite the em dashes in VS Code notifications, status-bar tooltips,\nwebview text, App Builder readiness notes and error messages surfaced\nto the user, plus the four retired-setting deprecation messages in\npackage.json (#2470). The checkout description shared by the Project,\nAccount and Cloud panels now reads the same everywhere; two of those\ncopies used a double hyphen in place of the dash.\n\nOutput-channel and App Builder console log lines, and the headers\nwritten into generated service scripts, are unchanged.\n\nRefs #2470\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(apps): remove em dashes from sql-ui, chat widget and bundled apps\n\nRewrite the em dashes in user-visible copy in sql-ui, the chat widget,\nand the hello, test, profiler, explorer and world apps (#2470). The\nsql-ui README quoted two of the changed strings (\"Will run: nothing\n(editor is empty)\" and the \"Generated preview: review, then Run\"\nbanner) and is updated to match.\n\nRefs #2470\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwC6bCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALxIQAFzzb5iBMCrBUBfiPdmMy7Ka\ncVKVJIiGLboNMt+fjO0oU8xYJP2owmVIim9gAwbSxn644ZBz71ry5ZcBc3M+lOiw\ncjtQpp6gc973482oQco1SYTz4SBG8AQpryTM8AvUi/iqLpWlAC08LlVMaZplLqg3\nlYxs24E/Ac4HMHILmq3gJ3BCsp3O9dqeJW/LJLCQRH8gmNxhG/SlcYL5j6IA0AJx\nfPLeQ6RCne5YXSF53x5GqPtCW0APhiqYinjB6j19hhDg6I25nBIC5AW+C9BNNb3s\nl40TYKy6tVNK2hkrcl3rDusLLmcrFCf7RkOZL9v6UB5+2HFWSVwWswF1J/568rFN\nFPDIjVIqScIcFj0zBJTE4veqF9F/LHiYVD9nVK0oBfGb4KqNSBiCU3FKAe0DkvIb\nRCuiVx33HY82DWz2ZIFbLGaQpBmcaVbVnMblu/XHYZy8pf9gjLZvOlmJcgOYLuHN\nLquOGh8X0+nuO/pOm41HvQSVQ0GnEwwpTIdqww72YeClIJpFAXxgMNA3Jq2CZ0ku\nKnUCzVtulVF57As/19SiqDj4MY/tNgMBySJ7ancvw2CpURu77rlwyRcIdxBuQNV4\nRhSxfECmVaAnDBJcSry0wTQVrrlJUPmVg724oLFFsEaEn1k/iFCixFo8H9YIBA8N\nnd7r+d1QgKdIudjOxvfK\n=M3gD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T22:22:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commit/da5ac853e37de34d6e6a486a9fb989748b4e2219","node_id":"C_kwDOROCxS9oAKGRhNWFjODUzZTM3ZGUzNGQ2ZTZhNDg2YTlmYjk4OTc0OGI0ZTIyMTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commit/8f27ea89c0af7f97cdaa81d49fb9ba55f45a8b68","sha":"8f27ea89c0af7f97cdaa81d49fb9ba55f45a8b68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/8f27ea89c0af7f97cdaa81d49fb9ba55f45a8b68"}],"sha":"da5ac853e37de34d6e6a486a9fb989748b4e2219","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/da5ac853e37de34d6e6a486a9fb989748b4e2219"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/130109357?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-savage/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-savage/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-savage/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-savage/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dylan-savage","id":130109357,"login":"dylan-savage","node_id":"U_kgDOB8FPrQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-savage/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-savage/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-savage/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-savage/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-savage/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-savage","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/8f27ea89c0af7f97cdaa81d49fb9ba55f45a8b68/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T22:16:34Z","email":"130109357+dylan-savage@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dylan Savage"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T22:16:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(clients): reconcile deploy, app-ladder and use() docs with the SDK (#2504)\n\n* docs(clients): reconcile deploy, app-ladder and use() docs with the SDK\n\nThe client docs disagreed with each other and with the SDK, so the API\nreference produced wrong results. Every fact below is taken from the SDK\nsource (deploy.ts, client.ts, deploy.py, mixins/apps.py, execution.py):\n\n- The \"only deploy.add/addApp live on client.deploy\" sentence was wrong\n  (verifyApp and createApp live there too); it now names all four.\n- deploy.createApp / deploy.create_app was undocumented on the site.\n- removeAppPublish / remove_app_publish was missing from the public\n  reference; disableAppPublish / disable_app_publish was documented\n  nowhere.\n- listDeployments omitted buildPhase/buildEndedAt, and the TS reference\n  typed it as RailEntry[] (and whereApp as Pin[]) - neither type exists in\n  the SDK; both now show the real fields.\n- The TS reference hid the teamId scope on deploy.list/deploy.history\n  (the Python reference already showed team_id).\n- pipelines.md (both languages) omitted use()''s token option.\n\nPython moves in lockstep, as the reference parity gate requires, and the\nagent bundle (ROCKETRIDE_*_API.md, ROCKETRIDE_APPS.md) gets the same\ncorrections.\n\nFixes #2475\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(clients): address review on the deploy docs\n\n- Drop the app-ladder method tables from both deploy.md guides. The\n  client-docs schema keeps method tables only in reference.md; the\n  guides now carry the lifecycle as prose and link to the reference\n  (every guide row was already covered by a reference row).\n- buildEndedAt is always present on rail rows (app_deploy.py\n  _rail_entry): epoch seconds, or null until the build ends. Say so in\n  both references and both agent API docs.\n- CreatedApp is TypeScript-only (Python''s create_app returns a dict);\n  give it its own language-specific entry. AppVerifyReport and\n  AppVerifyCheck exist in both SDKs, so the Python types line now lists\n  them too.\n\nRefs #2475\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8c9fe8117ac98fd69997980ae9cf84d28f2ddee7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/trees/8c9fe8117ac98fd69997980ae9cf84d28f2ddee7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/commits/8f27ea89c0af7f97cdaa81d49fb9ba55f45a8b68","verification":{"payload":"tree 8c9fe8117ac98fd69997980ae9cf84d28f2ddee7\nparent 08cc862aa9c0116687f80910d26ceaf3b845b28a\nauthor Dylan Savage <130109357+dylan-savage@users.noreply.github.com> 1790979394 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790979394 -0700\n\ndocs(clients): reconcile deploy, app-ladder and use() docs with the SDK (#2504)\n\n* docs(clients): reconcile deploy, app-ladder and use() docs with the SDK\n\nThe client docs disagreed with each other and with the SDK, so the API\nreference produced wrong results. Every fact below is taken from the SDK\nsource (deploy.ts, client.ts, deploy.py, mixins/apps.py, execution.py):\n\n- The \"only deploy.add/addApp live on client.deploy\" sentence was wrong\n  (verifyApp and createApp live there too); it now names all four.\n- deploy.createApp / deploy.create_app was undocumented on the site.\n- removeAppPublish / remove_app_publish was missing from the public\n  reference; disableAppPublish / disable_app_publish was documented\n  nowhere.\n- listDeployments omitted buildPhase/buildEndedAt, and the TS reference\n  typed it as RailEntry[] (and whereApp as Pin[]) - neither type exists in\n  the SDK; both now show the real fields.\n- The TS reference hid the teamId scope on deploy.list/deploy.history\n  (the Python reference already showed team_id).\n- pipelines.md (both languages) omitted use()''s token option.\n\nPython moves in lockstep, as the reference parity gate requires, and the\nagent bundle (ROCKETRIDE_*_API.md, ROCKETRIDE_APPS.md) gets the same\ncorrections.\n\nFixes #2475\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(clients): address review on the deploy docs\n\n- Drop the app-ladder method tables from both deploy.md guides. The\n  client-docs schema keeps method tables only in reference.md; the\n  guides now carry the lifecycle as prose and link to the reference\n  (every guide row was already covered by a reference row).\n- buildEndedAt is always present on rail rows (app_deploy.py\n  _rail_entry): epoch seconds, or null until the build ends. Say so in\n  both references and both agent API docs.\n- CreatedApp is TypeScript-only (Python''s create_app returns a dict);\n  give it its own language-specific entry. AppVerifyReport and\n  AppVerifyCheck exist in both SDKs, so the Python types line now lists\n  them too.\n\nRefs #2475\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwC1DCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAObQQAGFBNi2zhbpdd5bDSTo99RFU\n4srdU4RHX93NU1y4i7qwSMNVWDr8Zgjjx1sfkFwyXsNs01nnXHGJ+42FNoQpbnfV\nKd0xTrqaOd+IFMaxLMR79vzLGPRQAWu4oWE7wxTasyD9VDDTm+tQuhnUjJsdCxEU\njH32t0iqDzdFY6RKqGmG0IwS+pJxX1gom0iBjJM8ofgI2wttTp6XHdTZXXaQVKCQ\nCmGWU1WYfzENE/tvHjN9a5jiXGVK0FHThQ6mXG8n8jsBvw46oXjDTRFo9Hpxpcaj\nBoieOmf+uQGTVwdoplSBO5tGtHVSwA/uxXcbka2AeVFzh4E1B1s+1DNjAnIytQO2\nuBwOGtldUgeTwDYawotxdzgAoM0vee0H3+iWULPAWHvMPsftQ1wUAf4Amc2wXdzL\nARaimoqS0GA2kWvfpgWrIJffGmptjxmT0LqLYF/ud7fTRUe3vyX8gt/h+SnIuhoI\nM+6zpHUD8isjK5AqM3DzSjyDdzFQ11riIa4FePSgiYlyflR2M/9dHdTn98Hdou93\nniyfURNzaICPYsm5ZckbMJOApDY65FuSEUE2dgr0fM5rVOTGJhu+ZE/edWHMG3fi\nNIlOtb9Um0YleckZi4bO9guGakW0vQrRHG9D69JIW58ADwQ1Ny6x5dDpjfar8AxT\nc3/zjE+KKZptVmYpbER7\n=Fh6O\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T22:16:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commit/8f27ea89c0af7f97cdaa81d49fb9ba55f45a8b68","node_id":"C_kwDOROCxS9oAKDhmMjdlYTg5YzBhZjdmOTdjZGFhODFkNDlmYjliYTU1ZjQ1YThiNjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commit/08cc862aa9c0116687f80910d26ceaf3b845b28a","sha":"08cc862aa9c0116687f80910d26ceaf3b845b28a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/08cc862aa9c0116687f80910d26ceaf3b845b28a"}],"sha":"8f27ea89c0af7f97cdaa81d49fb9ba55f45a8b68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/8f27ea89c0af7f97cdaa81d49fb9ba55f45a8b68"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29624014?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/asclearuc","id":29624014,"login":"asclearuc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NjI0MDE0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/08cc862aa9c0116687f80910d26ceaf3b845b28a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T18:14:09Z","email":"asclearuc@gmail.com","name":"Alexandru Sclearuc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T18:14:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(nodes, ai): stop loading and installing torch in nodes that never use it (#2448)\n\n* fix(nodes): stop loading torch in embedding_image and embedding_video\n\nBoth embed through ai.common.models, which proxies to the model server\nwhen --modelserver is set, and neither node uses torch. The side-effect\nimport in beginGlobal loaded it in both modes, and under --modelserver\nthe GPU import guard refuses that import, so the nodes could not run\nwith a model server at all.\n\nThe wrapper now also refuses before depends() when the guard is\ninstalled, so a future call site fails immediately instead of after\ninstalling the CUDA wheel. A test asserts that no node imports the\nwrapper, which is what stops this being copied into a third one.\n\nFixes #2443\n\n* test(ai): scan node imports with ast, not a regex\n\n`from ai.common import torch` is the same wrapper under another spelling\nand slipped past the regex, and import-like text in a docstring matched\nit. The scan now also covers bare torch imports, which no node has\ntoday, and the detector has cases of its own: the invariant is worth\nonly as much as what backs it.\n\nRaised by CodeRabbit on #2448.\n\n* fix(nodes): stop installing torch through node requirements\n\nembedding_image, embedding_video and preprocessor_langchain declared\naccelerate (and the transformers stack) without using it. accelerate pulls\ntorch, so loading any of them installed a CUDA torch (~5-6 GB with the nvidia\nlibraries) on every run that used it.\n\nembedding_image and embedding_video get their models from\nai.common.models.vision, whose loader installs transformers and torch itself,\nand only on the local path. They now declare no requirements and call no\ndepends(). preprocessor_langchain counts chunk length itself; its NLTK and\nspaCy splitters keep their own requirement files.","tree":{"sha":"283b9be7680f63570f6879dd83a19fda7d078b9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/trees/283b9be7680f63570f6879dd83a19fda7d078b9e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/commits/08cc862aa9c0116687f80910d26ceaf3b845b28a","verification":{"payload":"tree 283b9be7680f63570f6879dd83a19fda7d078b9e\nparent e25e513acd3e5c4957ca94e3cf9a2fa4aea6e2bd\nauthor Alexandru Sclearuc <asclearuc@gmail.com> 1790964849 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790964849 +0000\n\nfix(nodes, ai): stop loading and installing torch in nodes that never use it (#2448)\n\n* fix(nodes): stop loading torch in embedding_image and embedding_video\n\nBoth embed through ai.common.models, which proxies to the model server\nwhen --modelserver is set, and neither node uses torch. The side-effect\nimport in beginGlobal loaded it in both modes, and under --modelserver\nthe GPU import guard refuses that import, so the nodes could not run\nwith a model server at all.\n\nThe wrapper now also refuses before depends() when the guard is\ninstalled, so a future call site fails immediately instead of after\ninstalling the CUDA wheel. A test asserts that no node imports the\nwrapper, which is what stops this being copied into a third one.\n\nFixes #2443\n\n* test(ai): scan node imports with ast, not a regex\n\n`from ai.common import torch` is the same wrapper under another spelling\nand slipped past the regex, and import-like text in a docstring matched\nit. The scan now also covers bare torch imports, which no node has\ntoday, and the detector has cases of its own: the invariant is worth\nonly as much as what backs it.\n\nRaised by CodeRabbit on #2448.\n\n* fix(nodes): stop installing torch through node requirements\n\nembedding_image, embedding_video and preprocessor_langchain declared\naccelerate (and the transformers stack) without using it. accelerate pulls\ntorch, so loading any of them installed a CUDA torch (~5-6 GB with the nvidia\nlibraries) on every run that used it.\n\nembedding_image and embedding_video get their models from\nai.common.models.vision, whose loader installs transformers and torch itself,\nand only on the local path. They now declare no requirements and call no\ndepends(). preprocessor_langchain counts chunk length itself; its NLTK and\nspaCy splitters keep their own requirement files.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv/RxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8nUQAKWATOoOdGRQSNyZCKOKFEtH\ncxFCWwp0aYBDElwyLVowl0tKQdPTP16IL4m7/R98wQ0DQEYujD3eUvQCcCJvaMHN\nVGJv99LHHZnfVIdxIbdm+PdgnlOwTGeFE09uFOp++EJ3qSUYDP5XTx9PRlks0+cL\n90TrCOALi0Z7lI5hwgm3LjtPHTe68Bd3Z/Ecie0kEnmYBuY6eI6dBThc5ctbJbVu\nz7qEVCsBdsY7NzG3Zj0JfoMZiaTmbc6BCucGg2rDppKAq8Q1as+dzztKK3Q1BBr3\nqSWeUbuijp18fZ03OpRZz12FdI/+dLOE7VGoYtriHDBEE2/+ocUQqDy9eDia5l0A\nikD99tqGSbEe/1BV3LQ