pi.github.com/users/asclearuc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/97ba24d1a1fbba3edb1a00bc0e3e941ffc1fe47b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T21:01:16Z","email":"asclearuc@gmail.com","name":"Alexandru Sclearuc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T21:01:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(tools): ignore OpenRouter routing variants during discovery (#2480)\n\n* fix(nodes): deprecate the profiles carrying an OpenRouter routing alias\n\nFifty-three profiles across seven nodes store an ID like gpt-4o:batch or\nmodels/gemini-2.5-flash:batch, which no provider SDK accepts. Each is marked\ndeprecated with a note naming the base model to use instead; four others were\nalready marked, so the catalogues now carry none that is both live and\nunusable.\n\nDeprecated rather than deleted. getNodeConfig raises \"Profile ... is not\ndefined\" for a key it cannot find, so removing them would stop a saved\npipeline from loading, while a deprecated profile loads and the engine prints\nthe migration note. The tool''s own policy agrees: deprecation.grace_period_\nreleases is 2, so removal belongs two releases later.\n\nOnly profiles whose modelSource is openrouter and whose suffix is a routing\nvariant are touched; the local Ollama IDs in llm_deepseek keep working.\n\nRefs #2479\n\n* fix(tools): ignore OpenRouter routing variants during discovery\n\nOpenRouter lists routing variants as entries of their own: author/slug:batch\nand author/slug:free. What follows the colon tells OpenRouter how to route the\nrequest and is no part of the name the vendor answers to, so such an ID is\nnever valid for a native SDK. Discovery passed them through, and a keyless run\nturned them into profiles that fail when the model is called.\n\nOf the 91 variant entries OpenRouter lists today, 86 carry their base model in\nthe same response, so dropping the variants costs the catalogue nothing; the\nremaining five are third-party :free models no node''s filter matches.\n\nThe filter sits in the OpenRouter fetch alone. A colon is not suspicious in\nitself: llm_deepseek stores seven local Ollama IDs (deepseek-r1:7b and the\nrest) that are real names, and Bedrock''s end in :0.\n\nRefs #2479","tree":{"sha":"c6977d5caf7c9661fa460d6ad1d8de644394b502","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/trees/c6977d5caf7c9661fa460d6ad1d8de644394b502"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/commits/97ba24d1a1fbba3edb1a00bc0e3e941ffc1fe47b","verification":{"payload":"tree c6977d5caf7c9661fa460d6ad1d8de644394b502\nparent 209afad2b66c6fa43f38b798b14bb922feaa3680\nauthor Alexandru Sclearuc <asclearuc@gmail.com> 1790888476 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790888476 +0000\n\nfix(tools): ignore OpenRouter routing variants during discovery (#2480)\n\n* fix(nodes): deprecate the profiles carrying an OpenRouter routing alias\n\nFifty-three profiles across seven nodes store an ID like gpt-4o:batch or\nmodels/gemini-2.5-flash:batch, which no provider SDK accepts. Each is marked\ndeprecated with a note naming the base model to use instead; four others were\nalready marked, so the catalogues now carry none that is both live and\nunusable.\n\nDeprecated rather than deleted. getNodeConfig raises \"Profile ... is not\ndefined\" for a key it cannot find, so removing them would stop a saved\npipeline from loading, while a deprecated profile loads and the engine prints\nthe migration note. The tool''s own policy agrees: deprecation.grace_period_\nreleases is 2, so removal belongs two releases later.\n\nOnly profiles whose modelSource is openrouter and whose suffix is a routing\nvariant are touched; the local Ollama IDs in llm_deepseek keep working.\n\nRefs #2479\n\n* fix(tools): ignore OpenRouter routing variants during discovery\n\nOpenRouter lists routing variants as entries of their own: author/slug:batch\nand author/slug:free. What follows the colon tells OpenRouter how to route the\nrequest and is no part of the name the vendor answers to, so such an ID is\nnever valid for a native SDK. Discovery passed them through, and a keyless run\nturned them into profiles that fail when the model is called.\n\nOf the 91 variant entries OpenRouter lists today, 86 carry their base model in\nthe same response, so dropping the variants costs the catalogue nothing; the\nremaining five are third-party :free models no node''s filter matches.\n\nThe filter sits in the OpenRouter fetch alone. A colon is not suspicious in\nitself: llm_deepseek stores seven local Ollama IDs (deepseek-r1:7b and the\nrest) that are real names, and Bedrock''s end in :0.\n\nRefs #2479","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvsocCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAI2AQAHRGZmefhJq/WKTv4jE4YV3J\nbjs4aK1ZY803OHttB/27eNCCOkxT53sPCSdlKoYb1ZiWyDGlDwccfwkffvs1hl1f\nbGYqIVqNXlNmTL5OuO9Id2Q8/S5l/bjT8iZ+Ox5NuQfLvGJqYWl0hj9Qxa3u01qs\n9wiqBEB6TVNLq8ebmP8iM3nBsOsHY7v+9KJ1vjmnLIrVV+QpnLjf3x4d30Jj7WGB\ntLMlrY+E/SAmmiduwxoSDe7bWnTG0rAR7VTmwvUcGbRShGizJp5HEE+6SsFkJijl\nwd8pK80ZWJoxV8I54IJpVrbN9125W4UqndkEDJtkrie1hWnYIgS2dlFvRqRhofnv\nbFKjXwBlYMbXUh87MxGWIuSzi7ZsAGaTuCcuOCj5LiQEcni7YS1k6AUvVNVX4Csh\n5qvPffGIPCA62CY1L2Y6F0FZcrhPAddRWAtswfuJMda0DUo2Xk47vSkBrwKVHtH1\nShqo0KDY/CnPjRrkdujwOTgE92kCDNSY4JN29Q9bG3eJIlOmEXgFnXMbUEyieNfb\n+Fw4M2UFsEASgXRFgiT3BFcxBoj3HNPjCEDMhZrXW/qoSiNX7fPGcwR8tUzATw1a\nTrCTIzA/7ZXKJeWWURfoAdepbZIjY4w4Qy3asOzDHpkuhjk0KnbBSMQqHGuSn4yg\nsD9zwSKr+wKHsQVSKx6L\n=OS8m\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T21:01:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commit/97ba24d1a1fbba3edb1a00bc0e3e941ffc1fe47b","node_id":"C_kwDOROCxS9oAKDk3YmEyNGQxYTFmYmJhM2VkYjFhMDBiYzBlM2U5NDFmZmMxZmU0N2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commit/209afad2b66c6fa43f38b798b14bb922feaa3680","sha":"209afad2b66c6fa43f38b798b14bb922feaa3680","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/209afad2b66c6fa43f38b798b14bb922feaa3680"}],"sha":"97ba24d1a1fbba3edb1a00bc0e3e941ffc1fe47b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/97ba24d1a1fbba3edb1a00bc0e3e941ffc1fe47b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29624014?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/asclearuc","id":29624014,"login":"asclearuc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NjI0MDE0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/209afad2b66c6fa43f38b798b14bb922feaa3680/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T20:17:47Z","email":"asclearuc@gmail.com","name":"Alexandru Sclearuc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T20:17:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(server): report Crashpad dumps at crash time on Linux (#2429)\n\n* fix(server): report Crashpad dumps at crash time on Linux\n\nCrashpad writes dumps out-of-process, so >DUMP only reached the caller on\nthe next task run''s sweep, not when the engine crashed as with Breakpad.\n\n- Linux: register a Crashpad last-chance handler (runs once the dump is\n  written). It wakes a \"Crash Reporter\" thread over a pipe, which moves\n  the process''s own dump and fires crashDumpCreatedCallback; the handler\n  waits up to 10s. The handler itself stays async-signal-safe, since it\n  runs on Crashpad''s ~8KB alternate signal stack.\n- Attribute dumps by the pid and process start time in the dump''s\n  MiscInfo stream: the per-task sweep skips dumps of running processes,\n  treats zombies as dead, and ignores recycled pids.\n- Skip silently when another engine''s sweep already moved the dump.\n- macOS unchanged: Crashpad dumps on EXC_CRASH, so it is still reported\n  on the next task run.\n\nRefs #2428\n\n* fix(server): report Crashpad dumps at crash time on macOS\n\nCrashpad on macOS dumps on EXC_CRASH, once the process is already dying,\nso the dump was only reported on the next task run.\n\n- Catch fatal signals and have Crashpad dump immediately via\n  SimulateCrash(), with the faulting thread''s registers from ucontext.\n- Report it through the shared Crash Reporter thread, then disable\n  EXC_CRASH so Crashpad does not write a second dump.\n- Chain to the previous (engine) signal handler afterwards.\n- Test: the child must report its own dump on every platform, and a\n  crash must leave exactly one dump.\n\nRefs #2428\n\n* fix(server): address review on crash-time dump reporting\n\n- macOS: always re-raise after chaining to the previous handler. SIGSYS\n  and an x86 int3 do not re-fire on return, and Darwin does not fill\n  si_code reliably enough to tell them apart.\n- Linux: one-shot guard in the last-chance handler, since the reporter\n  thread serves a single request (Crashpad already calls it only once).\n\nRefs #2428","tree":{"sha":"f6b2104c7dbc3fe65189550f41debe531e1dac57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/trees/f6b2104c7dbc3fe65189550f41debe531e1dac57"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/commits/209afad2b66c6fa43f38b798b14bb922feaa3680","verification":{"payload":"tree f6b2104c7dbc3fe65189550f41debe531e1dac57\nparent 7bde99c667fd705f494b2b16608b69d36284fc1f\nauthor Alexandru Sclearuc <asclearuc@gmail.com> 1790885867 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790885867 +0300\n\nfix(server): report Crashpad dumps at crash time on Linux (#2429)\n\n* fix(server): report Crashpad dumps at crash time on Linux\n\nCrashpad writes dumps out-of-process, so >DUMP only reached the caller on\nthe next task run''s sweep, not when the engine crashed as with Breakpad.\n\n- Linux: register a Crashpad last-chance handler (runs once the dump is\n  written). It wakes a \"Crash Reporter\" thread over a pipe, which moves\n  the process''s own dump and fires crashDumpCreatedCallback; the handler\n  waits up to 10s. The handler itself stays async-signal-safe, since it\n  runs on Crashpad''s ~8KB alternate signal stack.\n- Attribute dumps by the pid and process start time in the dump''s\n  MiscInfo stream: the per-task sweep skips dumps of running processes,\n  treats zombies as dead, and ignores recycled pids.\n- Skip silently when another engine''s sweep already moved the dump.\n- macOS unchanged: Crashpad dumps on EXC_CRASH, so it is still reported\n  on the next task run.\n\nRefs #2428\n\n* fix(server): report Crashpad dumps at crash time on macOS\n\nCrashpad on macOS dumps on EXC_CRASH, once the process is already dying,\nso the dump was only reported on the next task run.\n\n- Catch fatal signals and have Crashpad dump immediately via\n  SimulateCrash(), with the faulting thread''s registers from ucontext.\n- Report it through the shared Crash Reporter thread, then disable\n  EXC_CRASH so Crashpad does not write a second dump.\n- Chain to the previous (engine) signal handler afterwards.\n- Test: the child must report its own dump on every platform, and a\n  crash must leave exactly one dump.\n\nRefs #2428\n\n* fix(server): address review on crash-time dump reporting\n\n- macOS: always re-raise after chaining to the previous handler. SIGSYS\n  and an x86 int3 do not re-fire on return, and Darwin does not fill\n  si_code reliably enough to tell them apart.\n- Linux: one-shot guard in the last-chance handler, since the reporter\n  thread serves a single request (Crashpad already calls it only once).\n\nRefs #2428","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvr/rCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUuoQAA7+TQmze08YRTMIDu3tBNdC\n0shjywR0JU2wyYEaHZLxMQBcEKchxJkMJKElYz+9yVsRpXF/Duq5dni/Cjs3t3Eg\nMiXZc0AKvlJX1j7fPbbB6GWRzt5oW+TNem9M+Ea4ZVbxpPzGybadvn0Cmh4GRt2N\nXZR6kTFlIO/vloH387iydRLiYnUjppqtcJbjAx8gXv/crcqczOivwrvmEvsce7nX\nPUa5nB2WkaLJjS77x3d3xIkSJCZRxVQZiNJZyQzCZmIXaNZWJr5TA8O7e7Uqi2QO\n/klOnH3qQ8C8tFuI7sotWwwj2wzqxo9WI9cx+rRqrL96a9pt20VurxAmNjWckdcW\n1qQEksOS2bMFbEelAmzUkKsw0I5f+qzYF3halsbO9XLtlDp