up, so the Store stubs are rejected.\n- Without the engine, run the validator''s unit tests when that Python has\n  `pytest`, and skip them otherwise. `docs-schemas.yml` installs `pytest`,\n  so that doc-path gate now runs them instead of always skipping them.\n- Document the interpreter choice in `docs/development/ci-gates.md`.\n\nFixes #2383","tree":{"sha":"c7d03286500d973e04d8b69eeb1b14a86ed69ee4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/trees/c7d03286500d973e04d8b69eeb1b14a86ed69ee4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/commits/5ae09ed7c497b5d103a3e72e8f07a93756e017b9","verification":{"payload":"tree c7d03286500d973e04d8b69eeb1b14a86ed69ee4\nparent 92b19506a96848c6aa8089adc90dc4e688fca99f\nauthor Alexandru Sclearuc <asclearuc@gmail.com> 1790857265 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790857265 +0000\n\nfix(docs): run docs:validate under the engine''s Python (#2384)\n\n- `docs:validate` ran its two schema validators with a bare `python3`. On\n  Windows this is usually the Microsoft Store stub, so the task failed with\n  exit 9009 even when the engine was built.\n- Pick one interpreter for all three phases: the engine in `dist/server`\n  when it is built, else the first of `python3`, `python` that runs and is\n  Python 3.10+. Each candidate is run through `execCommand`, not just\n  looked up, so the Store stubs are rejected.\n- Without the engine, run the validator''s unit tests when that Python has\n  `pytest`, and skip them otherwise. `docs-schemas.yml` installs `pytest`,\n  so that doc-path gate now runs them instead of always skipping them.\n- Document the interpreter choice in `docs/development/ci-gates.md`.\n\nFixes #2383","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvlAxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHKsQAIZxFfp/KI9NXPqGFu/Zm3zK\nS3hDgKIc01akahm+FbWu3NdeGMCFUzWmwW3Qn9SxdywqWcX52YfY4TA4hLi6rgAF\nDoafIb8grjlGIAlBZtj3gQSF8wo5cBWfr8uN+SB8Qn1fyHNFI7wcVuLQyaUFHMHP\nb8