de-org/rocketride-server/commits/92b19506a96848c6aa8089adc90dc4e688fca99f"}],"sha":"5ae09ed7c497b5d103a3e72e8f07a93756e017b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/5ae09ed7c497b5d103a3e72e8f07a93756e017b9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29624014?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/asclearuc","id":29624014,"login":"asclearuc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NjI0MDE0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/92b19506a96848c6aa8089adc90dc4e688fca99f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T12:20:09Z","email":"asclearuc@gmail.com","name":"Alexandru Sclearuc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T12:20:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(nodes): gate heavy-model tests on hardware (`requiresHardware`) (#2314)\n\n* feat(ai): torch-free hardware probe for requiresHardware checks\n\nai.common.utils.hardware predicts the device pick_torch_device() would use\n(NVML, platform, psutil) without importing torch, and parses and checks\nrequiresHardware declarations.\n\nRefs #2313\n\n* feat(nodes): declare requiresHardware for model-loading test groups\n\nEvery test group of the model-loading nodes states where it can run, and\nprompt/question declare false. BiRefNet HR gets its own fulltest group. A\ncontract test requires the declaration for gpu nodes and memory_gb profiles.\n\nRefs #2313\n\n* fix(nodes): keep gmail mock-SDK tests off an already imported real SDK\n\nThe mock tests put nodes/test/mocks first on sys.path, but a real\ngoogle.oauth2 or googleapiclient imported earlier in the same worker still\nwins. Set those modules aside for the test, and restore them and the\ngoogle.oauth2 attribute afterwards.\n\nRefs #2313\n\n* feat(nodes): gate node tests on hardware, add model warmup and skip report\n\n- Skip tests whose requiresHardware isn''t met (fail them with\n  ROCKETRIDE_TEST_HARDWARE_STRICT); wait for free VRAM before heavy CUDA tests.\n- Run heavy tests in hwN xdist lanes (ROCKETRIDE_TEST_HW_LANES); refuse\n  other --dist modes when heavy tests are selected.\n- nodes:test-full pre-downloads the selected tests'' models (--warmup=plan|off).\n- --list-skipped[=category] reports skips without running anything.\n- Install nodes/test/requirements.txt, now listing the node packages tests\n  import directly, before the tests.\n- A missing `requires` env var is a visible skip; group timeouts can raise\n  the suite limit.\n\nRefs #2313\n\n* fix(ai): reject non-finite and MIG parent-GPU memory readings\n\njson.loads accepts NaN and Infinity, and NaN passed every memory\ncomparison, so a malformed value could clear any minimum. A MIG-\nselector resolved to the parent GPU, whose memory is a multiple of the\ninstance''s; resolve the instance by UUID, or report VRAM as unknown.\n\nRefs #2313\n\n* fix(nodes): fail closed in the hardware gate\n\n- An invalid requiresHardware fails before the env/libs skips: a\n  malformed declaration is a repo bug, not a property of this machine.\n- The pre-test VRAM check fails when NVML stops answering, instead of\n  starting a heavy test on an unverified GPU.\n- The contract test requires mps/cpu ramGb to cover memory_gb too.\n- --list-skipped= and --warmup= with an empty value are rejected, not\n  silently ignored.\n\nRefs #2313\n\n* fix(nodes): let a busy GPU fail a test instead of skipping it\n\nrequiresHardware now decides on capacity alone: free VRAM at session start no\nlonger skips a heavy test. The setup preflight already waits for the memory and\nfails naming the holders, so a leftover process on the GPU can no longer turn a\nrun green. The report header says up front when the memory is short.\n\nRefs #2313","tree":{"sha":"f72346735df777f5c213ccfc4eb0d683c3faf361","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/trees/f72346735df777f5c213ccfc4eb0d683c3faf361"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/commits/92b19506a96848c6aa8089adc90dc4e688fca99f","verification":{"payload":"tree f72346735df777f5c213ccfc4eb0d683c3faf361\nparent d6b70b82ec7306d061d7919e1dac8e6a3a6a4cd1\nauthor Alexandru Sclearuc <asclearuc@gmail.com> 1790857209 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790857209 +0200\n\nfeat(nodes): gate heavy-model tests on hardware (`requiresHardware`) (#2314)\n\n* feat(ai): torch-free hardware probe for requiresHardware checks\n\nai.common.utils.hardware predicts the device pick_torch_device() would use\n(NVML, platform, psutil) without importing torch, and parses and checks\nrequiresHardware declarations.\n\nRefs #2313\n\n* feat(nodes): declare requiresHardware for model-loading test groups\n\nEvery test group of the model-loading nodes states where it can run, and\nprompt/question declare false. BiRefNet HR gets its own fulltest group. A\ncontract test requires the declaration for gpu nodes and memory_gb profiles.\n\nRefs #2313\n\n* fix(nodes): keep gmail mock-SDK tests off an already imported real SDK\n\nThe mock tests put nodes/test/mocks first on sys.path, but a real\ngoogle.oauth2 or googleapiclient imported earlier in the same worker still\nwins. Set those modules aside for the test, and restore them and the\ngoogle.oauth2 attribute afterwards.\n\nRefs #2313\n\n* feat(nodes): gate node tests on hardware, add model warmup and skip report\n\n- Skip tests whose requiresHardware isn''t met (fail them with\n  ROCKETRIDE_TEST_HARDWARE_STRICT); wait for free VRAM before heavy CUDA tests.\n- Run heavy tests in hwN xdist lanes (ROCKETRIDE_TEST_HW_LANES); refuse\n  other --dist modes when heavy tests are selected.\n- nodes:test-full pre-downloads the selected tests'' models (--warmup=plan|off).\n- --list-skipped[=category] reports skips without running anything.\n- Install nodes/test/requirements.txt, now listing the node packages tests\n  import directly, before the tests.\n- A missing `requires` env var is a visible skip; group timeouts can raise\n  the suite limit.\n\nRefs #2313\n\n* fix(ai): reject non-finite and MIG parent-GPU memory readings\n\njson.loads accepts NaN and Infinity, and NaN passed every memory\ncomparison, so a malformed value could clear any minimum. A MIG-\nselector resolved to the parent GPU, whose memory is a multiple of the\ninstance''s; resolve the instance by UUID, or report VRAM as unknown.\n\nRefs #2313\n\n* fix(nodes): fail closed in the hardware gate\n\n- An invalid requiresHardware fails before the env/libs skips: a\n  malformed declaration is a repo bug, not a property of this machine.\n- The pre-test VRAM check fails when NVML stops answering, instead of\n  starting a heavy test on an unverified GPU.\n- The contract test requires mps/cpu ramGb to cover memory_gb too.\n- --list-skipped= and --warmup= with an empty value are rejected, not\n  silently ignored.\n\nRefs #2313\n\n* fix(nodes): let a busy GPU fail a test instead of skipping it\n\nrequiresHardware now decides on capacity alone: free VRAM at session start no\nlonger skips a heavy test. The setup preflight already waits for the memory and\nfails naming the holders, so a leftover process on the GPU can no longer turn a\nrun green. The report header says up front when the memory is short.\n\nRefs #2313","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvk/5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyTgQADfEqs4tGQE+McE377ZDJ34X\nRQMw6JE6yjOYU/S15NWtBhBR0f7Nqw3f/90oJwO4JO93T5grGlLMn8XVDQzEu/23\nFW4GSmbb8HYpLkPh2WPWc0VhuiVOG0n5lGKYpKKcydx3PP8P9kR3BWiuXeGicF3o\nsYnbFP5tXWf0WKReY7JVKYkc75Lbcxbm3YTqB8P0exanWlsW7SUHpjh2lD4c8bOx\n0qPqTjSb0r+AxnzBUSBDpBJWod9t27B+rR+3PqQiZkXukG+GD2rrPoPtjSfWvr4b\n6CBUdHvelkGZ+UiYFwrNd+ue/4IEeuN8mhlrX1kCLqvoJR5kIoXc3e4aybr85e7T\njtIhMYgINwkElNN4WLkUn/tqll+GD9uyCc+yi2ShYpsJsRZwy8LcuPH0jT7Kiuzp\nRtlc2Q26Q+b7kICCwd18apwTgQDeznTKNSoXeyEt3KvNLmQt6EpA/SbWmhVeRT0s\nouF+EHXnk7eyS+bTJmz4mGzqFP2EEHfPV8GArtP3Cw0oYSHOq8wKUYQ1XAm5g9Rb\nv6ssrs0C0zkv6p91dBpBUScmvpHjilJUEePvFeI+uQMGGU4k9VieIFzSe4tCQfRq\nBnVQynommLBdleXQGN55ned3pc/RzYruBPFovR2Y2mNIDU3VVshoWP7Wbc5jouwg\n9MusTw9weiEQz5j+vz1W\n=ni+K\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T12:20:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commit/92b19506a96848c6aa8089adc90dc4e688fca99f","node_id":"C_kwDOROCxS9oAKDkyYjE5NTA2YTk2ODQ4YzZhYTgwODlhZGM5MGRjNGU2ODhmY2E5OWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commit/d6b70b82ec7306d061d7919e1dac8e6a3a6a4cd1","sha":"d6b70b82ec7306d061d7919e1dac8e6a3a6a4cd1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/d6b70b82ec7306d061d7919e1dac8e6a3a6a4cd1"}],"sha":"92b19506a96848c6aa8089adc90dc4e688fca99f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/92b19506a96848c6aa8089adc90dc4e688fca99f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29624014?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/asclearuc","id":29624014,"login":"asclearuc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NjI0MDE0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/d6b70b82ec7306d061d7919e1dac8e6a3a6a4cd1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T12:20:00Z","email":"asclearuc@gmail.com","name":"Alexandru Sclearuc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T12:20:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(cli): upload finds files through Windows paths again (#2350)\n\n* fix(cli): upload finds files through Windows paths again\n\nrocketride upload expands wildcards and directories with glob 10, which\nreads a backslash as an escape unless windowsPathsNoEscape is set. On\nWindows every native path is backslash-separated, so a pattern like\ntestdata\\documents\\*.docx, or a whole directory, matched nothing and the\ncommand failed with \"No files found matching the specified patterns\".\nvalidate.ts already sets the option; upload now does the same for both\nof its lookups.\n\nfindFiles is exported for a unit test that builds every path with\npath.join, so on Windows it exercises the native separator; without the\noption four of its six cases fail.\n\n* test(cli): resolve the temp dir before comparing upload paths\n\nOn macOS os.tmpdir() is under /var, a symlink to /private/var. After\nchdir into the work dir, process.cwd() is the resolved path, so\nfindFiles returned /private/var/... while the test compared against\n/var/... and the relative-path case failed. Resolve the work dir once\nso every path is canonical.","tree":{"sha":"f7b9277eeb123a90a463e8f4ffbfc5f65c197089","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/trees/f7b9277eeb123a90a463e8f4ffbfc5f65c197089"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/commits/d6b70b82ec7306d061d7919e1dac8e6a3a6a4cd1","verification":{"payload":"tree f7b9277eeb123a90a463e8f4ffbfc5f65c197089\nparent c5d8c866f67fe604a2f5303f7d92a23f2be29b64\nauthor Alexandru Sclearuc <asclearuc@gmail.com> 1790857200 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790857200 +0200\n\nfix(cli): upload finds files through Windows paths again (#2350)\n\n* fix(cli): upload finds files through Windows paths again\n\nrocketride upload expands wildcards and directories with glob 10, which\nreads a backslash as an escape unless windowsPathsNoEscape is set. On\nWindows every native path is backslash-separated, so a pattern like\ntestdata\\documents\\*.docx, or a whole directory, matched nothing and the\ncommand failed with \"No files found matching the specified patterns\".\nvalidate.ts already sets the option; upload now does the same for both\nof its lookups.\n\nfindFiles is exported for a unit test that builds every path with\npath.join, so on Windows it exercises the native separator; without the\noption four of its six cases fail.\n\n* test(cli): resolve the temp dir before comparing upload paths\n\nOn macOS os.tmpdir() is under /var, a symlink to /private/var. After\nchdir into the work dir, process.cwd() is the resolved path, so\nfindFiles returned /private/var/... while the test compared against\n/var/... and the relative-path case failed. Resolve the work dir once\nso every path is canonical.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvk/wCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1qQQAAONG1H4sBjGiqR/MNwWpoBX\n29TjrHwL/Rb3VwuVfd87siL2qd+7pOmENrPbvGRkhH1vUg6DPZ0wKioDQ3z/VmJW\nxT53t3Ds+NdcQikA6nLuGEaJz80K9dkbifvitkWc0CWWwgBrxuEaZhYn81e0W8gN\n5T083fYaRsZYKGjN85XeBuhm/Jx30MdwbUM57XA5KJNMHEJvtX4fHcxbzoSuTVxT\nzkShmiAJuTpOKrcwCTzOfETTNgIIpRtnd/6MYxtEU+E/HqlD6kDfOqdnIkiZxcfk\nPcQGStmWQU0UVPcVpjL249m9Xf9FSg3DtrRKXKEFt3jMiJXBBc/cCKMI/6vo7iyz\nt3DalB6Dpj4+Bb+55+rLpg0W7ZQFekubIpEQzRO44nif5vcLXNPjEmVIYNemFT+u\nEDIzWW+s0UgODsVC1iodgs2a4Srqrxs6JMptVr2zuuZrS2CGTLzD2FTIvLThFPvi\nc1AjeJD+B0ZQyKlm4uZvklarlV0NmVTOMb2PJt+GJq7+XM9v1OfGfW3AR1KpwJTx\nD9O5VyLJ2J/Pgn475I0PT5EmaGKcYkPQpAoG41YT0sRCFByw3h/bFa+n34iBGnAb\n6lXvh6wMUopDK/++Hf53Vvc+zOaHI5JVufM5Oliw40Y6mQOGkducPHItyqtvgqlP\n/adWIsGsWr9MMRb9Xj9W\n=IliB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T12:20:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commit/d6b70b82ec7306d061d7919e1dac8e6a3a6a4cd1","node_id":"C_kwDOROCxS9oAKGQ2YjcwYjgyZWM3MzA2ZDA2MWQ3OTE5ZTFkYWM4ZTZhM2E2YTRjZDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commit/c5d8c866f67fe604a2f5303f7d92a23f2be29b64","sha":"c5d8c866f67fe604a2f5303f7d92a23f2be29b64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/c5d8c866f67fe604a2f5303f7d92a23f2be29b64"}],"sha":"d6b70b82ec7306d061d7919e1dac8e6a3a6a4cd1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/d6b70b82ec7306d061d7919e1dac8e6a3a6a4cd1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29624014?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/asclearuc","id":29624014,"login":"asclearuc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NjI0MDE0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/c5d8c866f67fe604a2f5303f7d92a23f2be29b64/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T11:06:58Z","email":"asclearuc@gmail.com","name":"Alexandru Sclearuc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T11:06:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(nodes): give the synced Kimi profiles the endpoint the driver needs (#2451)\n\nkimi.py refuses to start a profile whose serverbase is empty, and llm_kimi\ndefines no field for it, so there is no default to fall back on. The five\nhand-written profiles carry the Moonshot endpoint; the seven the model sync\nadded did not, so every one of them failed at pipe start.\n\nAll seven now carry it, and the provider''s extra_profile_fields writes it into\nfuture ones — the endpoint guard in the sync tool''s wiring test enforces that\nfor every provider whose seeded profiles all carry an endpoint.\n\nkimi-k3-batch is a second problem: it stores kimi-k3:batch, an OpenRouter\nrouting alias rather than a Moonshot model ID, so the API has nothing to answer\nwith. It is deprecated with a note pointing at kimi-k3, the way llm_qwen\nhandles the profiles that reached it the same way. It keeps loading for saved\npipelines.\n\nRefs #2449","tree":{"sha":"3d969fa456c06574cf82d9f0376f2f548b944e1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/trees/3d969fa456c06574cf82d9f0376f2f548b944e1c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/commits/c5d8c866f67fe604a2f5303f7d92a23f2be29b64","verification":{"payload":"tree 3d969fa456c06574cf82d9f0376f2f548b944e1c\nparent 43258c42ca0a6eb0a6b91fdf5f66051e6cb4bcf4\nauthor Alexandru Sclearuc <asclearuc@gmail.com> 1790852818 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790852818 +0000\n\nfix(nodes): give the synced Kimi profiles the endpoint the driver needs (#2451)\n\nkimi.py refuses to start a profile whose serverbase is empty, and llm_kimi\ndefines no field for it, so there is no default to fall back on. The five\nhand-written profiles carry the Moonshot endpoint; the seven the model sync\nadded did not, so every one of them failed at pipe start.\n\nAll seven now carry it, and the provider''s extra_profile_fields writes it into\nfuture ones — the endpoint guard in the sync tool''s wiring test enforces that\nfor every provider whose seeded profiles all carry an endpoint.\n\nkimi-k3-batch is a second problem: it stores kimi-k3:batch, an OpenRouter\nrouting alias rather than a Moonshot model ID, so the API has nothing to answer\nwith. It is deprecated with a note pointing at kimi-k3, the way llm_qwen\nhandles the profiles that reached it the same way. It keeps loading for saved\npipelines.\n\nRefs #2449","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvj7SCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7JAQAEZJc1pmTLjhVc0Tsj1Qoohc\nfGSjylNYMcTciMFOpviwJwzCmmd5YMnqntDLpBgyWIxdCm4pQ30UuWkjarq6RSWk\n/xtFOLAr5YFRGV4xne8ZwMSxWIR8Thb3l6taQTUR+hSpuhQJTui8dRwjx3JItqi8\n9u30EmbXkH4INasCE8i16p6uY4c+sujC1a/lLPKS0MxZyn0zA6PrGWBBXFk/ntle\n/7IM93MJYFLo7FOe2MJENQt/CadBUZ/r/cXZJnz6E2fsUKDhr1nMkc4mqC7tftkJ\nGhP3ouiqEMjnQFfsWdLCNaOc354B93hPz2CQOMjDbIHjNmUDYKb+Q3mdUWPkct/M\nwSYu77FJKUJ1BVxSW51qI9evfcgfzuR/u69inmTKVCOLz6G8C/qVj5VLi5IdlPzD\nSgxiGa0N/yu4/zgJ9iSxTMlk1Y3k8+C1JAx4ZAF1eItAGaZfCIHrdxZbzy02J8nb\nTeAoI2IZdG0gHrJFbAJZ38ac1IH6FCGe7p3JwJU27QfC6rr4NtvehMF1lhAr2A8E\nkBLQnlkjLiVkDjuGqOp4e+h2OyqBSGKJZLXccgvKTG4++NOxgbEWHJ0HNcmGVz7f\n0MdquKtCYGkwVHGDSPsLSqHTkj3fM7sX0SqyF/clrqu7M0gmCUatPvoKrQdEo/ys\nKi5q/o2OJx8gMmpdcj1i\n=JQQF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T11:06:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commit/c5d8c866f67fe604a2f5303f7d92a23f2be29b64","node_id":"C_kwDOROCxS9oAKGM1ZDhjODY2ZjY3ZmU2MDRhMmY1MzAzZjdkOTJhMjNmMmJlMjliNjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commit/43258c42ca0a6eb0a6b91fdf5f66051e6cb4bcf4","sha":"43258c42ca0a6eb0a6b91fdf5f66051e6cb4bcf4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/43258c42ca0a6eb0a6b91fdf5f66051e6cb4bcf4"}],"sha":"c5d8c866f67fe604a2f5303f7d92a23f2be29b64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/c5d8c866f67fe604a2f5303f7d92a23f2be29b64"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29624014?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/asclearuc","id":29624014,"login":"asclearuc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NjI0MDE0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/43258c42ca0a6eb0a6b91fdf5f66051e6cb4bcf4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T10:44:00Z","email":"asclearuc@gmail.com","name":"Alexandru Sclearuc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T10:44:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(tools): stamp reasoning for models stored under a prefixed ID (#2447)\n\nThe OpenRouter cache is keyed by the bare vendor ID, so a lookup with an ID a\nnode stores with a prefix never matched: openai/gpt-5.2 on GMI Cloud, or\nmodels/gemini-3-flash-preview on Gemini. Only the family heuristic could stamp\nthose, which is why llm_openai''s gpt-5.2 carries capabilities.reasoning while\nthe same model resold by GMI Cloud carries nothing. Against today''s files that\nis 16 GMI Cloud profiles, 32 Gemini profiles and 1 Nebius profile.\n\n_is_reasoning_model now also tries the name after the last slash, lowercased,\nand the dotted form of each candidate. Whether a model reasons is a property of\nthe model, so its name identifies it whichever host serves it — unlike a\ncontext window, which belongs to one host''s deployment and keeps the stricter\nper-provider mapping.\n\nRefs #2446","tree":{"sha":"6caed1d30cf20200f8705dc232466e2bf7ac488d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/trees/6caed1d30cf20200f8705dc232466e2bf7ac488d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/commits/43258c42ca0a6eb0a6b91fdf5f66051e6cb4bcf4","verification":{"payload":"tree 6caed1d30cf20200f8705dc232466e2bf7ac488d\nparent ce0975e68b83dfd9bce320347b825e400190b41b\nauthor Alexandru Sclearuc <asclearuc@gmail.com> 1790851440 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790851440 +0200\n\nfix(tools): stamp reasoning for models stored under a prefixed ID (#2447)\n\nThe OpenRouter cache is keyed by the bare vendor ID, so a lookup with an ID a\nnode stores with a prefix never matched: openai/gpt-5.2 on GMI Cloud, or\nmodels/gemini-3-flash-preview on Gemini. Only the family heuristic could stamp\nthose, which is why llm_openai''s gpt-5.2 carries capabilities.reasoning while\nthe same model resold by GMI Cloud carries nothing. Against today''s files that\nis 16 GMI Cloud profiles, 32 Gemini profiles and 1 Nebius profile.\n\n_is_reasoning_model now also tries the name after the last slash, lowercased,\nand the dotted form of each candidate. Whether a model reasons is a property of\nthe model, so its name identifies it whichever host serves it — unlike a\ncontext window, which belongs to one host''s deployment and keeps the stricter\nper-provider mapping.\n\nRefs #2446","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvjlwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhc8QALAg83J/F8pAJc8Zrj3bpt8n\njT3lw+k+Xqjz1X8hc2NWx+lNTSboHjGqDUJkOH31P0yEWMKBmH4LfeBRQ2b0Cv8S\nAkPQyrOxrWGyFezuOD6ZvyMuI1NJD9uT7HySLmoXjB5W3n6Vm/FdQhG7h+QTKpPY\nL8oXI7N+UULWIwYyK5MKoIkIvt+Ba6VU0y4x8YE/Z4p7cBjNZxCITvkSvEEpMhya\nmwPLJXR8/fGLsqnDZFpULZ1AEZjcQH9ZfsEOn89YX3XjUybcbEnqWZHdqgZawqOA\nXTgFYB1+oDSg4IJVIdD5Tt15Xogo7pCp0Q9QsPmBdQQ6tTiL5FQ8HQUIoHjlF0VF\nGB/1ATwAF3XsW0zBYoXsWV478B9+bBIFo/hmDI9Z20otISbr+iWvRXQrupU0kyRT\nXazynDm5m9b7HrnOMYuNxuv2ax+QwRaB1LjAnuO99+b+Vnw9DoatuMQt7xbq1O4b\nznhA8JscVHnnYlw5I+vLWMhUbZgn81yEV9zhXoghOpiKm6wdVt+DUp5XO803O9g+\n4XmHQKuCjwKBHUF06gb2c7H2ysPdIftHD5k+kj830OoDBt8uu8eyn36WGKKUI+Qa\nkCEBoFKFmEIM0Uz3KcsxZm2cKampLGqFJV889Fk4153FouB5Btza0EiPYl0h2WMk\n48n3k1HYu5DOAUzezkgY\n=cvDX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T10:44:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commit/43258c42ca0a6eb0a6b91fdf5f66051e6cb4bcf4","node_id":"C_kwDOROCxS9oAKDQzMjU4YzQyY2EwYTZlYjBhNmI5MWZkZjVmNjYwNTFlNmNiNGJjZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commit/ce0975e68b83dfd9bce320347b825e400190b41b","sha":"ce0975e68b83dfd9bce320347b825e400190b41b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/ce0975e68b83dfd9bce320347b825e400190b41b"}],"sha":"43258c42ca0a6eb0a6b91fdf5f66051e6cb4bcf4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/43258c42ca0a6eb0a6b91fdf5f66051e6cb4bcf4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29624014?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/asclearuc","id":29624014,"login":"asclearuc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NjI0MDE0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/ce0975e68b83dfd9bce320347b825e400190b41b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T10:43:32Z","email":"asclearuc@gmail.com","name":"Alexandru Sclearuc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T10:43:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(nodes): report a missing GMI Cloud endpoint while the node is configured (#2452)\n\nDeploy-on-demand profiles ship with an empty serverbase: the user pastes the\nURL their GMI Cloud console gives them. validateConfig returned early for that\ncase, so saving reported nothing and the run failed later at pipe start, far\nfrom the field that is missing. It now warns, naming the console.\n\nbeginGlobal computed \"config.get(''serverbase'') or the shared endpoint\" and then\nhanded Chat the raw config, so that default never reached the driver and Chat\nraised anyway. The default is gone and the check is explicit: an empty endpoint\nstops the start with a message that says what to paste and where. A silent\nfallback to the shared endpoint would be worse — a deploy-on-demand model is\nnot served there, so the run would fail later on the model instead.\n\nThe new test loads the node''s IGlobal against stub SDKs, the way the Baidu\nQianfan test does, so it needs no engine and no key.\n\nRefs #2450","tree":{"sha":"f3788d2a1a213644da7992aafcdfb92eb42fc44f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/trees/f3788d2a1a213644da7992aafcdfb92eb42fc44f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/commits/ce0975e68b83dfd9bce320347b825e400190b41b","verification":{"payload":"tree f3788d2a1a213644da7992aafcdfb92eb42fc44f\nparent 2633bc03bd6950bbb89e80e085042fcbceef9585\nauthor Alexandru Sclearuc <asclearuc@gmail.com> 1790851412 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790851412 +0000\n\nfix(nodes): report a missing GMI Cloud endpoint while the node is configured (#2452)\n\nDeploy-on-demand profiles ship with an empty serverbase: the user pastes the\nURL their GMI Cloud console gives them. validateConfig returned early for that\ncase, so saving reported nothing and the run failed later at pipe start, far\nfrom the field that is missing. It now warns, naming the console.\n\nbeginGlobal computed \"config.get(''serverbase'') or the shared endpoint\" and then\nhanded Chat the raw config, so that default never reached the driver and Chat\nraised anyway. The default is gone and the check is explicit: an empty endpoint\nstops the start with a message that says what to paste and where. A silent\nfallback to the shared endpoint would be worse — a deploy-on-demand model is\nnot served there, so the run would fail later on the model instead.\n\nThe new test loads the node''s IGlobal against stub SDKs, the way the Baidu\nQianfan test does, so it needs no engine and no key.\n\nRefs #2450","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvjlUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQhUQACy9gJxv/ERtDH5xwDcZzarC\nypZwtUhG46zkO90rgjZfOeBCMlmpE4ZDkCt5BfVW7K/LSblB7r2SHOiJ6V4ZebhL\nJau7EFMwruVVHlFaoZ0SlfuricwbSd/mrX3+CFRBAJLpluW1RMpR7//U+UcQNA1x\n5wm+SW2qHevT9RbLR4O+/TFNgv3qbH7t7AanwZfumzgIqgNccUf84n5OZXTtUEyx\nLzD0gYK2cwkbTfzIeABKpjRQuj60yY27UtflAsa/R5ZEjz66ru49o5OGgW/zM2FR\n2mbhqPR5DprEqMJSDz1C3Y6PEo04rVBm9kLky6DskaDPt/8NrYydLucTKeNB3VWJ\nqJrXGnUTIAfrEtMVip3f8SborqiDj9wUz6Bs4bU+PmYlyGvoFfjZ