ype":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commit/2633bc03bd6950bbb89e80e085042fcbceef9585","node_id":"C_kwDOROCxS9oAKDI2MzNiYzAzYmQ2OTUwYmJiODllODBlMDg1MDQyZmNiY2VlZjk1ODU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commit/c76810a2e4cb856051f6181491970d9307b811f4","sha":"c76810a2e4cb856051f6181491970d9307b811f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/c76810a2e4cb856051f6181491970d9307b811f4"}],"sha":"2633bc03bd6950bbb89e80e085042fcbceef9585","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/2633bc03bd6950bbb89e80e085042fcbceef9585"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29624014?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/asclearuc","id":29624014,"login":"asclearuc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NjI0MDE0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/c76810a2e4cb856051f6181491970d9307b811f4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T22:23:19Z","email":"asclearuc@gmail.com","name":"Alexandru Sclearuc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T22:23:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(cli): rocketride profile — profile the server or a pipeline from both CLIs (#2382)\n\n* feat(cli): rocketride profile — profile the server or a pipeline from both CLIs\n\nBoth CLIs gain a profile group over the existing cprofile_* client calls:\nstart, stop, run, status, list, report, threads and tree. --token names\na task and profiles its engine subprocess; without it the server process\nis profiled, so unlike the task commands --token has no ROCKETRIDE_TOKEN\ndefault. Output is text; --json gives the raw DAP response. Errors the\nserver reports in the body (status ''error'', an error field) become exit\n1 and the usual error envelope.\n\nstart and stop need --token. The server ends a session on its own\nprocess when the connection that started it closes, discarding the data\n(task_server.py releases it on disconnect), and every CLI invocation is\nits own connection: a start in one invocation is gone before a stop in\nthe next. A task''s session belongs to the server''s link to the\nsubprocess and outlives the CLI. run covers the server process: start,\nwait for Ctrl+C or --duration, stop, all on one connection. The\nTypeScript shutdown handler now offers the first signal to a command\nwaiting for it; the Python CLI swaps in its own SIGINT/SIGTERM handler\nfor the wait. A second Ctrl+C aborts as before.\n\nlist shows the status of the server process and of every task the caller\ncan see, asking the tasks in parallel with a 10 s timeout each; a task\nthat fails or does not answer is listed below the table instead of\nfailing the command. --active keeps only the processes being profiled.\n\nthreads prints ID, name, tid, time and share of the total; tree draws\nthe server''s call tree in ASCII, pruned on the server by --min-pct and\n--max-depth. The list, threads and tree formats are pinned by identical\nexpected lines in the two test suites, so neither CLI can drift from the\nother. Number options are checked in the command rather than by\nargparse, so both CLIs refuse a bad one with the same message and exit\ncode.\n\n* fix(cli): refuse profile numbers the CLIs cannot hold\n\n--duration took any run of digits, and enough of them overflow to\nInfinity in TypeScript and inf in Python: the value passed the\npositive-duration check and turned the wait into one with no end.\nCounts had the mirror problem, where Python keeps every digit and a\nJavaScript number drops them past 2^53, so the two CLIs would have\nanswered the same input differently.\n\nparseDecimal now requires a finite result on both sides, and parseCount\na value up to Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER, the Python side bounded to the\nsame range on purpose. Both suites check a 400-digit duration and\n9007199254740993 for --max-depth and --thread.\n\n* fix(cli): profile run must not leave a task profiling\n\nA task''s session is owned by the server''s link to the subprocess, not by\nthe CLI''s connection, so a signal that killed the command left the task\nprofiling with nobody to stop it. Ctrl+C between `cprofile_start` and the\nwait did exactly that: the interrupt hook was installed only inside the\nwait, so an earlier signal took the CLI down.\n\nArm the interrupt before the session starts and release it in a finally,\nand print how to end a session left behind when the command is killed\noutright. Both CLIs, same text; the docs now say who owns a task session\nand what a second user''s `stop` does to your `run`.\n\n* docs(cli): say when profile run fails after someone else''s stop\n\nA remote stop takes the session away but does not reach the waiting\n`run`: it waits out Ctrl+C or --duration as before and only then fails\non its own stop, with the server''s \"No active profiling session\".","tree":{"sha":"ebc54c402b7e4c87f650294de9e965b0b37412ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/trees/ebc54c402b7e4c87f650294de9e965b0b37412ed"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/commits/c76810a2e4cb856051f6181491970