e server by --min-pct and\n--max-depth. The list, threads and tree formats are pinned by identical\nexpected lines in the two test suites, so neither CLI can drift from the\nother. Number options are checked in the command rather than by\nargparse, so both CLIs refuse a bad one with the same message and exit\ncode.\n\n* fix(cli): refuse profile numbers the CLIs cannot hold\n\n--duration took any run of digits, and enough of them overflow to\nInfinity in TypeScript and inf in Python: the value passed the\npositive-duration check and turned the wait into one with no end.\nCounts had the mirror problem, where Python keeps every digit and a\nJavaScript number drops them past 2^53, so the two CLIs would have\nanswered the same input differently.\n\nparseDecimal now requires a finite result on both sides, and parseCount\na value up to Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER, the Python side bounded to the\nsame range on purpose. Both suites check a 400-digit duration and\n9007199254740993 for --max-depth and --thread.\n\n* fix(cli): profile run must not leave a task profiling\n\nA task''s session is owned by the server''s link to the subprocess, not by\nthe CLI''s connection, so a signal that killed the command left the task\nprofiling with nobody to stop it. Ctrl+C between `cprofile_start` and the\nwait did exactly that: the interrupt hook was installed only inside the\nwait, so an earlier signal took the CLI down.\n\nArm the interrupt before the session starts and release it in a finally,\nand print how to end a session left behind when the command is killed\noutright. Both CLIs, same text; the docs now say who owns a task session\nand what a second user''s `stop` does to your `run`.\n\n* docs(cli): say when profile run fails after someone else''s stop\n\nA remote stop takes the session away but does not reach the waiting\n`run`: it waits out Ctrl+C or --duration as before and only then fails\non its own stop, with the server''s \"No active profiling session\".","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvYvXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYJwQADYHJ8UcKMOSLrMsF07yyYmH\nlkSKXnDpLwlmf8gEo5D7BvvGDhfq1aN1wGtVTaXBjpiLtkkvt9Azz+Vtex1C6loK\nX0yLTcj6zX3ihg/KfVbxwEq9kgH8m99fhHMAkQVov07vCHGznSJQ1dsxQG9XzruA\nlDVYNe1OlYyExff7PE+A4niArCJ/pxds5VzbqTgJrR6JLjTHOBx+f9UemR+gFMDj\nmZ6mFq/c3MUSFwnaxZFCRSkZOSpgZ5oa6qcTalIFih2zIXswDYqgVMnmh4Z7gMHF\nSN0aPNUuy/HLetd+4/RZUwvB01AJ7RdjqVW8B3Y4JE2TD5R0E6mr6r8YgYi/qdnb\nm+dZF+d6HohbocBLX8r9K5TEqR2J2OkwmifF5t17wG4Uz5uAajSnQMvNeDaUbA2h\nvJy8UqxMkFmGiPWhS+T96hcXUBOKPT2WLErjTUcMOJvRIZh3PQlPQkxsU0xmOZV8\nQ0OmUyGZ3QhSgZXXiOYxJ7PXeC4hij9OV4vi91RAN61xie9j1Lf7JGGioIHjxM5R\nT4XWY9gvi+HRVVIrg6pgi3oULd0eiqZDb4qIJh5JjIE6QYA99sbi57GyZCAMEhDL\nYoBp5G5KoSld/8TQxso2qWdBaXxEkvqiwT6VDnOC7hBgn184Q3YNvWA6IUCHxTtf\nKyO7yZYuM/zupilFWDzb\n=6rDX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T22:23:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commit/c76810a2e4cb856051f6181491970d9307b811f4","node_id":"C_kwDOROCxS9oAKGM3NjgxMGEyZTRjYjg1NjA1MWY2MTgxNDkxOTcwZDkzMDdiODExZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commit/63cbed1450a516693cd65360229ae95f03b11cd1","sha":"63cbed1450a516693cd65360229ae95f03b11cd1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/63cbed1450a516693cd65360229ae95f03b11cd1"}],"sha":"c76810a2e4cb856051f6181491970d9307b811f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/c76810a2e4cb856051f6181491970d9307b811f4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29624014?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/asclearuc","id":29624014,"login":"asclearuc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NjI0MDE0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/63cbed1450a516693cd65360229ae95f03b11cd1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T21:00:54Z","email":"asclearuc@gmail.com","name":"Alexandru Sclearuc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T21:00:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(tools): sync model lists for the vision, GMI Cloud and Nebius nodes (#2317)\n\n* feat(tools): sync model lists for the vision, GMI Cloud and Nebius nodes\n\nThe weekly sync covered 13 nodes. Six more shipped hand-written lists that\nnobody updated: every Gemini model in llm_vision_gemini and\naccessibility_describe is already deprecated in llm_gemini, llm_vision_openai\nstops at GPT-4o, and GMI Cloud''s proxied profiles understate their vendor''s\ncontext window. llm_baidu_qianfan was registered in the tool but missing from\nthe workflow, so CI had never synced it.\n\nRegister all seven, and add the three things they need:\n\n- Capability filter (model_filter.require_capabilities). A vision node takes a\n  new model only when a source reports image support: Mistral''s own\n  capabilities.vision, else OpenRouter input modalities, else LiteLLM\n  supports_vision. Unknown counts as no, so a model too new for the databases\n  waits for a later run. New models are verified with an image rather than a\n  text-only call. Existing profiles are never dropped by this check.\n\n- Key-only providers (require_api_key). Without its key such a provider is\n  skipped, not matched against OpenRouter, which does not list these IDs: 21 of\n  21 GMI Cloud profiles, 3 of 3 Nebius, 2 of 6 vision Mistral. A keyless run\n  would retire working models and, under the workflow''s fallback discovery, add\n  IDs the runtime SDK cannot call.\n\n- Host token data (allowed_sources, vendor_proxy_prefixes). A host chooses the\n  window of a model it runs itself, so only its own list is trusted; LiteLLM\n  answered openai/gpt-4o with 16384 and claude-opus-4.5 with 64000. For models\n  GMI Cloud resells, the vendor''s limits apply and are looked up under the\n  vendor''s ID, so those profiles track llm_openai, llm_anthropic and llm_gemini.\n\nA new profile''s form now inherits the properties every sibling model form shows\n(a vision node''s prompt fields); a property only some models carry, such as\ntemperature on part of OpenAI''s catalogue, stays per model. Per-provider\nextra_profile_fields give new Nebius profiles their base URL and key reference.\n\nllm_baidu_qianfan joins the workflow, and a test fails when a registered\nprovider is missing from it, from scripts/tasks.js, or from its config.\n\nThe tool README explains why these providers refuse to run without a key, and\neach node README says what maintains its profiles.\n\nRefs #2316\n\n* fix(tools): guard non-dict profiles and prove the vision live test with an image\n\n_shared_properties() called .get(''model'') on whatever a profile key held, but\n_normalize_profile() deliberately preserves non-dict profile values, so a form\nobject pointing at one raised AttributeError while a new model was being added.\nIt now checks the type first, as the rest of the file does.\n\nThe llm_vision_mistral live test claimed its profiles accept images while only\nrejecting model cards whose capabilities.vision is false: a missing or wrong\ncard value passed even when the model refuses image input. It now calls each\nprofile the way the sync calls a new one, with a small PNG attached, and\nignores a transient failure.\n\nBoth vision node READMEs said the sync asks OpenRouter and LiteLLM and adds a\nmodel when one of them reports vision support. lookup_capability() returns the\nfirst answer it gets, so a \"no\" from OpenRouter settles it without asking\nLiteLLM. The wording now says that.\n\nRefs #2316\n\n* fix(tools): sync Baidu Qianfan only through its own API\n\nThis branch adds llm_baidu_qianfan to the weekly workflow for the first time.\nNo provider key is configured in CI, so that placed it in the fallback group,\nwhere OpenRouter is the model source. OpenRouter carries a single ERNIE entry,\nernie-4.5-vl-424b-a47b, and none of the three models this node serves. Such a\nrun could not enrich or deprecate anything; it could only add that\nvision-language ID to a text-only node, the way llm_qwen collected the dead\nprofiles its README documents.\n\nrequire_api_key now skips the provider when its key is missing, as it does for\nthe model hosts and the vision nodes, and \"vl\" joins the exclude list so the\nVL family stays out once the key exists.\n\nRefs #2316\n\n* fix(tools): give new host profiles the endpoint their driver needs\n\nA synced profile carries only what the tool puts in it, so a node that demands\nan endpoint gets a profile it refuses to start. gmi_cloud.py raises \"GMI Cloud\nserverbase is required.\", the gmi_cloud.serverbase field has no default, and\nIGlobal''s own fallback never reaches the driver because it hands Chat the raw\nconfig. The form of a new profile does not carry the field either, so the value\ncould not even be typed in.\n\nllm_gmi_cloud now writes the shared endpoint into every new profile. That is\nthe honest value: discovery smoke-tests each new model against that endpoint,\nso a model which reaches the catalogue is one that answers there. A\ndeploy-on-demand model still needs its console URL, entered per pipeline.\n\nA new wiring test states the rule for every provider — when all seeded profiles\ncarry serverbase or base_url, extra_profile_fields must write it into new ones.\nIt found llm_glm and llm_baidu_qianfan in the same shape. Their drivers fall\nback to a default, so nothing was broken there, but new profiles would have\ndiffered from the seeded ones; both now pin their endpoint.\n\nFound in review.\n\nRefs #2316","tree":{"sha":"7e7c5767bdcc3317c95e66133fbc6bb883d13806","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/trees/7e7c5767bdcc3317c95e66133fbc6bb883d13806"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/commits/63cbed1450a516693cd65360229ae95f03b11cd1","verification":{"payload":"tree 7e7c5767bdcc3317c95e66133fbc6bb883d13806\nparent ca5ab4152f21ccc2cfbcf4bc51d429205da2c92e\nauthor Alexandru Sclearuc <asclearuc@gmail.com> 1790802054 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790802054 +0300\n\nfeat(tools): sync model lists for the vision, GMI Cloud and Nebius nodes (#2317)\n\n* feat(tools): sync model lists for the vision, GMI Cloud and Nebius nodes\n\nThe weekly sync covered 13 nodes. Six more shipped hand-written lists that\nnobody updated: every Gemini model in llm_vision_gemini and\naccessibility_describe is already deprecated in llm_gemini, llm_vision_openai\nstops at GPT-4o, and GMI Cloud''s proxied profiles understate their vendor''s\ncontext window. llm_baidu_qianfan was registered in the tool but missing from\nthe workflow, so CI had never synced it.\n\nRegister all seven, and add the three things they need:\n\n- Capability filter (model_filter.require_capabilities). A vision node takes a\n  new model only when a source reports image support: Mistral''s own\n  capabilities.vision, else OpenRouter input modalities, else LiteLLM\n  supports_vision. Unknown counts as no, so a model too new for the databases\n  waits for a later run. New models are verified with an image rather than a\n  text-only call. Existing profiles are never dropped by this check.\n\n- Key-only providers (require_api_key). Without its key such a provider is\n  skipped, not matched against OpenRouter, which does not list these IDs: 21 of\n  21 GMI Cloud profiles, 3 of 3 Nebius, 2 of 6 vision Mistral. A keyless run\n  would retire working models and, under the workflow''s fallback discovery, add\n  IDs the runtime SDK cannot call.\n\n- Host token data (allowed_sources, vendor_proxy_prefixes). A host chooses the\n  window of a model it runs itself, so only its own list is trusted; LiteLLM\n  answered openai/gpt-4o with 16384 and claude-opus-4.5 with 64000. For models\n  GMI Cloud resells, the vendor''s limits apply and are looked up under the\n  vendor''s ID, so those profiles track llm_openai, llm_anthropic and llm_gemini.\n\nA new profile''s form now inherits the properties every sibling model form shows\n(a vision node''s prompt fields); a property only some models carry, such as\ntemperature on part of OpenAI''s catalogue, stays per model. Per-provider\nextra_profile_fields give new Nebius profiles their base URL and key reference.\n\nllm_baidu_qianfan joins the workflow, and a test fails when a registered\nprovider is missing from it, from scripts/tasks.js, or from its config.\n\nThe tool README explains why these providers refuse to run without a key, and\neach node README says what maintains its profiles.\n\nRefs #2316\n\n* fix(tools): guard non-dict profiles and prove the vision live test with an image\n\n_shared_properties() called .get(''model'') on whatever a profile key held, but\n_normalize_profile() deliberately preserves non-dict profile values, so a form\nobject pointing at one raised AttributeError while a new model was being added.\nIt now checks the type first, as the rest of the file does.\n\nThe llm_vision_mistral live test claimed its profiles accept images while only\nrejecting model cards whose capabilities.vision is false: a missing or wrong\ncard value passed even when the model refuses image input. It now calls each\nprofile the way the sync calls a new one, with a small PNG attached, and\nignores a transient failure.\n\nBoth vision node READMEs said the sync asks OpenRouter and LiteLLM and adds a\nmodel when one of them reports vision support. lookup_capability() returns the\nfirst answer it gets, so a \"no\" from OpenRouter settles it without asking\nLiteLLM. The wording now says that.\n\nRefs #2316\n\n* fix(tools): sync Baidu Qianfan only through its own API\n\nThis branch adds llm_baidu_qianfan to the weekly workflow for the first time.\nNo provider key is configured in CI, so that placed it in the fallback group,\nwhere OpenRouter is the model source. OpenRouter carries a single ERNIE entry,\nernie-4.5-vl-424b-a47b, and none of the three models this node serves. Such a\nrun could not enrich or deprecate anything; it could only add that\nvision-language ID to a text-only node, the way llm_qwen collected the dead\nprofiles its README documents.\n\nrequire_api_key now skips the provider when its key is missing, as it does for\nthe model hosts and the vision nodes, and \"vl\" joins the exclude list so the\nVL family stays out once the key exists.\n\nRefs #2316\n\n* fix(tools): give new host profiles the endpoint their driver needs\n\nA synced profile carries only what the tool puts in it, so a node that demands\nan endpoint gets a profile it refuses to start. gmi_cloud.py raises \"GMI Cloud\nserverbase is required.\", the gmi_cloud.serverbase field has no default, and\nIGlobal''s own fallback never reaches the driver because it hands Chat the raw\nconfig. The form of a new profile does not carry the field either, so the value\ncould not even be typed in.\n\nllm_gmi_cloud now writes the shared endpoint into every new profile. That is\nthe honest value: discovery smoke-tests each new model against that endpoint,\nso a model which reaches the catalogue is one that answers there. A\ndeploy-on-demand model still needs its console URL, entered per pipeline.\n\nA new wiring test states the rule for every provider — when all seeded profiles\ncarry serverbase or base_url, extra_profile_fields must write it into new ones.\nIt found llm_glm and llm_baidu_qianfan in the same shape. Their drivers fall\nback to a default, so nothing was broken there, but new profiles would have\ndiffered from the seeded ones; both now pin their endpoint.\n\nFound in review.\n\nRefs #2316","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvXiGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZIAQAAk3/yhYLrsONoTcE0KsPA8m\nlAvZspP4UrlVmfUg81VgDVsStG8xMdKW5P5sMMzE+wMzqgCghDJucYGYx2tsDj/S\no8yftB1HmM5AY6eXZ6rki4jVSx2d/KQN5Ww9IMcc9UPgfJPwKQ8nHZQQbnnv4Q90\nFjr08gv2XCQyXLbdXhzms8GWKZ3FtiHK/EVlx5gXtVnFx1coPO5tyIIoDF/UvSfG\nCEkFoZNied4UDErOej4kTtvdVed9riu8FQMoKbAbcPrhfqifFHVWm/km5WGNYlYX\nIW3WPaTg5cmL5bFi5YN0aME2fFS4Fu2vi2qqmH03osPtrtGJXVTosfSNhnp5Lk+y\n+z7OfTGX2/PwWcwLUgyGRQX/H33RAa4yha6DPQpAnvIwatNxLDX0R6pV8qcvWgR9\n8TLov4WiSgzzNbKy3HSMSlyz3Kl5BwWCBCjA7A/QwVf9jpIoXO21SrIzQl88NFNc\nWuVJWJbSKxdT/BQrkb3/W0lO+raFalDPPH1nZmxaGnlmdAy57Op8I/WSXzljijwX\nOaD6WIlkKwY8l0gpC6Q1gljSOIMdUuQfhpI96/Z/