ments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/9d8203429d1a9a074672ce2d379fe5c3906c72b2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T19:43:18Z","email":"dmitrii.kataraev@rocketride.ai","name":"dk-rocketride"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T19:43:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(shell): 404 on missing /shell/static/* assets instead of SPA HTML (#2225)\n\n* fix(shell): 404 on missing /shell/static/* assets instead of SPA HTML\n\nshell_static() fell back to index.html for ANY unmatched path, including\nmissing content-hashed build assets under /shell/static/*. Behind the\nstaging CloudFront the /shell/static/* behavior is edge-cached with an\nimmutable Cache-Control, so a 200 index.html served under a .js/.css URL\ngets cached (edge + browser) as HTML-under-a-JS-URL and poisons every\nviewer — the app then fails to boot until the cache expires.\n\nReturn a real 404 for a missing asset under /shell/static/; keep the SPA\nindex.html fallback only for genuine navigation routes. This makes the\nmissing chunk uncacheable as a valid asset and lets the client recover.\napps_static() already 404s correctly; this brings the shell path in line.\n\nAdds regression tests: missing /shell/static/* -> 404, and a non-static\n/shell/* navigation route still serves index.html.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015nTVr6jfSFYm1GppxbjghP\n\n* fix(shell): decide the /shell/static/* 404 on the resolved path, before serving\n\nReview on #2225 found the guard was unreachable for a traversal: it ran\nafter the serve step, and _resolve_safe answers a traversal with index.html,\nwhich exists, so /shell/static/js/%2e%2e/%2e%2e/%2e%2e/x.js still returned\n200 index.html under a .js URL. That is the exact response this PR exists\nto prevent.\n\nThe check now runs before serving and on the resolved path: a\n/shell/static/* request is served only when it resolves to a real file\ninside static/, otherwise 404. Same rule apps_static already follows.\n\nTests, per the review: a present bundle is still served (so a guard that\nrejected everything cannot pass), and a percent-encoded traversal 404s\n(literal ../ is resolved by httpx before sending and proves nothing). The\nshared setup moves into a _shell_client() helper. The docstring and the\ncomment now describe the scope actually taken.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015nTVr6jfSFYm1GppxbjghP\n\n* fix(shell): trigger the /shell/static/* 404 on the stripped path, keep the 503\n\nReview on #2225: the guard read the raw URL, so ''/shell//static/x.js'' and\n''/shell/%2e/static/x.js'' skipped it and got index.html. Both reach the\norigin and get the immutable cache on staging today. The trigger now looks\nat the stripped path two ways: its leading segment (catches static/../..\nwalking out) and its normalized form (catches a/../static walking in).\n\nWith the shell unbuilt, answer the 503 that names the build command before\nany path handling, as apps_static does. Docstring lists the 404.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015nTVr6jfSFYm1GppxbjghP\n\n* fix(shell): early 503 keys on index.html, so a partial build is not a 404\n\nCodeRabbit on #2225: with the shell dir present but index.html missing, an\nasset miss answered 404 before the build-instruction 503 could run.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015nTVr6jfSFYm1GppxbjghP\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"283bb1333805e13795fbcec77c7605ad4521c3d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/trees/283bb1333805e13795fbcec77c7605ad4521c3d5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/commits/9d8203429d1a9a074672ce2d379fe5c3906c72b2","verification":{"payload":"tree 283bb1333805e13795fbcec77c7605ad4521c3d5\nparent 96164a564e8f783506452d576a594429b5664e2a\nauthor dk-rocketride <dmitrii.kataraev@rocketride.ai> 1790278998 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790278998 -0700\n\nfix(shell): 404 on missing /shell/static/* assets instead of SPA HTML (#2225)\n\n* fix(shell): 404 on missing /shell/static/* assets instead of SPA HTML\n\nshell_static() fell back to index.html for ANY unmatched path, including\nmissing content-hashed build assets under /shell/static/*. Behind the\nstaging CloudFront the /shell/static/* behavior is edge-cached with an\nimmutable Cache-Control, so a 200 index.html served under a .js/.css URL\ngets cached (edge + browser) as HTML-under-a-JS-URL and poisons every\nviewer — the app then fails to boot until the cache expires.\n\nReturn a real 404 for a missing asset under /shell/static/; keep the SPA\nindex.html fallback only for genuine navigation routes. This makes the\nmissing chunk uncacheable as a valid asset and lets the client recover.\napps_static() already 404s correctly; this brings the shell path in line.\n\nAdds regression tests: missing /shell/static/* -> 404, and a non-static\n/shell/* navigation route still serves index.html.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015nTVr6jfSFYm1GppxbjghP\n\n* fix(shell): decide the /shell/static/* 404 on the resolved path, before serving\n\nReview on #2225 found the guard was unreachable for a traversal: it ran\nafter the serve step, and _resolve_safe answers a traversal with index.html,\nwhich exists, so /shell/static/js/%2e%2e/%2e%2e/%2e%2e/x.js still returned\n200 index.html under a .js URL. That is the exact response this PR exists\nto prevent.\n\nThe check now runs before serving and on the resolved path: a\n/shell/static/* request is served only when it resolves to a real file\ninside static/, otherwise 404. Same rule apps_static already follows.\n\nTests, per the review: a present bundle is still served (so a guard that\nrejected everything cannot pass), and a percent-encoded traversal 404s\n(literal ../ is resolved by httpx before sending and proves nothing). The\nshared setup moves into a _shell_client() helper. The docstring and the\ncomment now describe the scope actually taken.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015nTVr6jfSFYm1GppxbjghP\n\n* fix(shell): trigger the /shell/static/* 404 on the stripped path, keep the 503\n\nReview on #2225: the guard read the raw URL, so ''/shell//static/x.js'' and\n''/shell/%2e/static/x.js'' skipped it and got index.html. Both reach the\norigin and get the immutable cache on staging today. The trigger now looks\nat the stripped path two ways: its leading segment (catches static/../..\nwalking out) and its normalized form (catches a/../static walking in).\n\nWith the shell unbuilt, answer the 503 that names the build command before\nany path handling, as apps_static does. Docstring lists the 404.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015nTVr6jfSFYm1GppxbjghP\n\n* fix(shell): early 503 keys on index.html, so a partial build is not a 404\n\nCodeRabbit on #2225: with the shell dir present but index.html missing, an\nasset miss answered 404 before the build-instruction 503 could run.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015nTVr6jfSFYm1GppxbjghP\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtX1WCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAk/gQAEwC7FDZz5Oy+T/NtSVuXZ27\nOAEquXfMogZ6rCJoASjKKOn9GFmdr2iYRPamO/afo9HzlHp/WqDx8zgKX6oyUP3C\nH7UTgAS0UNTvJ3iAlQE6OLmshb1L5zrTjh