64a564e8f783506452d576a594429b5664e2a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/181051779?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krishhgg/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krishhgg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krishhgg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krishhgg/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/krishhgg","id":181051779,"login":"krishhgg","node_id":"U_kgDOCsqhgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krishhgg/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krishhgg/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krishhgg/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krishhgg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krishhgg/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/krishhgg","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/aebb8aa92a56e433b6a8f41de0211021b5f45a45/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T18:25:05Z","email":"kgarg@chapman.edu","name":"Krish Garg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T18:25:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ai): make engine and task processes non-dumpable on hosted engines (#2414)\n\nHosted engines and their tasks clear the dumpable flag at startup with prctl(PR_SET_DUMPABLE, 0), so their /proc entries (environment, memory, open files) are root-only rather than readable by other processes of the same user. eaas.py does it after .env loads and before serving (--saas or RR_PROC_PRIVATE=1; a failure is logged and the engine keeps serving). node.py does it before any pipeline code loads (--hosted or RR_PROC_PRIVATE=1; a task that cannot exits 1). RR_PROC_PRIVATE joins the task env allowlist.\n\nTask exit recording: a task that exits without an >EXIT event now records its process exit code (1 if it cannot be read) and ends CANCELLED rather than COMPLETED; a process that outlives its closed output is killed after the cancel timeout; requested stops keep exit code 0; a restart clears the previous run''s process. The remaining exit-0 case is #2416.\n\nDocs: \"Pipeline process isolation\" in operate/security.md (task env allowlist, RR_SUBPROCESS_ENV, RR_PROC_PRIVATE, limits).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a49a539318b014d6ff523e87e79aab54129c2df0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/trees/a49a539318b014d6ff523e87e79aab54129c2df0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/commits/aebb8aa92a56e433b6a8f41de0211021b5f45a45","verification":{"payload":"tree a49a539318b014d6ff523e87e79aab54129c2df0\nparent 0391071cbc88b26182aff89dd0b1a51e4e55c729\nauthor Krish Garg <kgarg@chapman.edu> 1790274305 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790274305 -0700\n\nfix(ai): make engine and task processes non-dumpable on hosted engines (#2414)\n\nHosted engines and their tasks clear the dumpable flag at startup with prctl(PR_SET_DUMPABLE, 0), so their /proc entries (environment, memory, open files) are root-only rather than readable by other processes of the same user. eaas.py does it after .env loads and before serving (--saas or RR_PROC_PRIVATE=1; a failure is logged and the engine keeps serving). node.py does it before any pipeline code loads (--hosted or RR_PROC_PRIVATE=1; a task that cannot exits 1). RR_PROC_PRIVATE joins the task env allowlist.\n\nTask exit recording: a task that exits without an >EXIT event now records its process exit code (1 if it cannot be read) and ends CANCELLED rather than COMPLETED; a process that outlives its closed output is killed after the cancel timeout; requested stops keep exit code 0; a restart clears the previous run''s process. The remaining exit-0 case is #2416.\n\nDocs: \"Pipeline process isolation\" in operate/security.md (task env allowlist, RR_SUBPROCESS_ENV, RR_PROC_PRIVATE, limits).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtWsBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaZ4QADf+NV7SWal1CHhe1v+ZfMB0\nkCyHgUvJ0fjnysQSr4HxJvv7PH8XS1YFzjEfAHFuBPF2O2/iuGLCqtm0yD+nC+FS\n+vSkhAQFRosEjxBYMba8gMJagpZ0yaeMisusLVuYPriry5gcvHtbjVSvZhoGh85Z\nk+C4Sd4wByxUUq8zqbMuNqJONHL5OGpLyn7EWGL+/duEH4Ivy79QQ1jUaBtlX63F\nNI6TzkcJOweWeXKpPsWnQ2amw7vCvOOunFS0Cx7TsR9VQkJmoS0RbPyfEizBdCf3\nX2r7rJFlI2Q53LNkLHy7ML+UkcTf85O8hvmmggKbXAgV+qGu+XsJ2N8B/KKFVid2\ne2fXErQdyZcpyIiAM7KLS/qe6BCRX3L4Fcfozs47UHZ7Gs40YI4s6W/XM7LdK3S7\nSeSStSg5bysSxiVWw4HjpVyHVjS7lsWaoEde5iQUN3+/zwuyr4C0kOKPwTZZPnC3\nHBhMW4vikZ73wMJap4JYSfcCR1wc9gUlca1to7Yd0003XOmHQLHdpB9HXKtKpIKb\nYA6flqVSjyn5g9cSr6njg8+++j6+RojUBsOvUUXMRnXXR/+sYi+D7f0MN1/wbk4x\nhyHSAHxe+Gc/FQAor4ND5UPsLZGKmnrzvXSKya78oSL9qoiawBx1aZ8fUdXxAcKJ\ndI0Jq75WLsiL+N1Hc5KB\n=U0Fd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T18:25:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commit/aebb8aa92a56e433b6a8f41de0211021b5f45a45","node_id":"C_kwDOROCxS9oAKGFlYmI4YWE5MmE1NmU0MzNiNmE4ZjQxZGUwMjExMDIxYjVmNDVhNDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commit/0391071cbc88b26182aff89dd0b1a51e4e55c729","sha":"0391071cbc88b26182aff89dd0b1a51e4e55c729","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/0391071cbc88b26182aff89dd0b1a51e4e55c729"}],"sha":"aebb8aa92a56e433b6a8f41de0211021b5f45a45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/aebb8aa92a56e433b6a8f41de0211021b5f45a45"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/322872359?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dk-rocketride/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dk-rocketride/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dk-rocketride/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dk-rocketride/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dk-rocketride","id":322872359,"login":"dk-rocketride","node_id":"U_kgDOEz6kJw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dk-rocketride/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dk-rocketride/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dk-rocketride/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dk-rocketride/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dk-rocketride/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dk-rocketride","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/0391071cbc88b26182aff89dd0b1a51e4e55c729/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T22:14:16Z","email":"dmitrii.kataraev@rocketride.ai","name":"dk-rocketride"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T22:14:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ai): hosted engines refuse nosaas nodes and stdio MCP before launch (#2412)\n\n* fix(ai): hosted engines refuse nosaas nodes and stdio MCP before launch\n\nThe canvas hides nosaas services, but a pipeline can reach the engine\nwithout the canvas, and nothing on the engine side checked. A hosted\nengine now refuses, in _check_pipeline before anything launches:\n\n- any component whose service carries the nosaas capability\n- the MCP client in stdio mode, which launches a command inside the\n  engine''s container. The transport is resolved the way the node\n  resolves it (the default profile is itself stdio), and anything that\n  cannot be resolved is refused. HTTP transports are unaffected.\n\n\"Hosted\" = the engine''s own --saas flag or the account provider''s saas\ncapability. Local installs are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015nTVr6jfSFYm1GppxbjghP\n\n* fix(ai): match the MCP client by node, and refuse stdio in the node too\n\nReview on #2412 found two ways past the gate: tool_butterbase is built on\nthe same node and can be switched to stdio, and provider lookup is\ncase-insensitive, so MCP_Client resolved to the MCP node but did not match\nthe exact name. The gate now matches the service''s node module\n(nodes.tool_mcp_client), whatever the provider is called.\n\nSecond layer: a hosted engine starts its tasks with --hosted. Pipeline\nargs can add flags but not remove one. McpStdioClient.start() refuses\nwhen the flag is present, before anything launches.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015nTVr6jfSFYm1GppxbjghP\n\n* fix(ai): the Python sandbox allows only default modules on a hosted engine\n\ntool_python lets a pipeline add modules to the sandbox allowlist, and a\nmissing one is pip-installed on the spot. Under a hosted engine either\nruns with the container''s own access (its files, its cloud role), not\nthe user''s. With --hosted, the sandbox ignores extra modules and never\ninstalls, and tool_python stops offering them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015nTVr6jfSFYm1GppxbjghP\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"df3b3c2c26b9b261ad79bdeaea2aa583a910a957","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/trees/df3b3c2c26b9b261ad79bdeaea2aa583a910a957"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/commits/0391071cbc88b26182aff89dd0b1a51e4e55c729","verification":{"payload":"tree df3b3c2c26b9b261ad79bdeaea2aa583a910a957\nparent 6e47387b1b4b09f375aad50b0c12faee047965bb\nauthor dk-rocketride <dmitrii.kataraev@rocketride.ai> 1790201656 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790201656 -0700\n\nfix(ai): hosted engines refuse nosaas nodes and stdio MCP before launch (#2412)\n\n* fix(ai): hosted engines refuse nosaas nodes and stdio MCP before launch\n\nThe canvas hides nosaas services, but a pipeline can reach the engine\nwithout the canvas, and nothing on the engine side checked. A hosted\nengine now refuses, in _check_pipeline before anything launches:\n\n- any component whose service carries the nosaas capability\n- the MCP client in stdio mode, which launches a command inside the\n  engine''s container. The transport is resolved the way the node\n  resolves it (the default profile is itself stdio), and anything that\n  cannot be resolved is refused. HTTP transports are unaffected.\n\n\"Hosted\" = the engine''s own --saas flag or the account provider''s saas\ncapability. Local installs are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015nTVr6jfSFYm1GppxbjghP\n\n* fix(ai): match the MCP client by node, and refuse stdio in the node too\n\nReview on #2412 found two ways past the gate: tool_butterbase is built on\nthe same node and can be switched to stdio, and provider lookup is\ncase-insensitive, so MCP_Client resolved to the MCP node but did not match\nthe exact name. The gate now matches the service''s node module\n(nodes.tool_mcp_client), whatever the provider is called.\n\nSecond layer: a hosted engine starts its tasks with --hosted. Pipeline\nargs can add flags but not remove one. McpStdioClient.start() refuses\nwhen the flag is present, before anything launches.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015nTVr6jfSFYm1GppxbjghP\n\n* fix(ai): the Python sandbox allows only default modules on a hosted engine\n\ntool_python lets a pipeline add modules to the sandbox allowlist, and a\nmissing one is pip-installed on the spot. Under a hosted engine either\nruns with the container''s own access (its files, its cloud role), not\nthe user''s. With --hosted, the sandbox ignores extra modules and never\ninstalls, and tool_python stops offering them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015nTVr6jfSFYm1GppxbjghP\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtE84CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0kcQAJUf9QB2YNSV6X9HauAsCF7N\nnpoa9Z1IVziGRP4nuY5kCBeiTq4JHvutMEpuY0qxVZtNEdfWr/9jgXWbMwOZPftw\nGFNFEOAt+z9IjmfO1UfK4OJ/n2mZO22zIWLCQ4yKjo056nNAoa6CvZBP34/MNKLO\nQ4s1/iyYfcMQ0q+T1M4ohwlkirDzzM14UWjglznuStXhCOZJaP3XpVa35kkHsfvm\n+mIr1TjFfKrMDIEODkIB0ilTvZblTDywyo5PUmVSkU1gS0mUxFv5MV0HH/1QlN/R\n4kA4djIrU53evoT3NdcRH4sjv8CVjyX310ctk7UE72bQ37ChbDzO+XmdBGh8EtXR\n2p3lXoOCB6Yr01lQ7d2dzcXYL5qsLhvVoPS8oAFANdlwpmnFKVgDjs/vcGo0kYam\n/tNmRbf5mdtQZ3ywNadZa+whY6KKH7+W871XXfJWVZ3X+nBmiRNNC3veYDrbCO+t\nZ7PkBa2ste8VitlpWV2e