/krishhgg/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/krishhgg","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/593bd5838e4020784d81a4f12e590abbd562a435/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T20:06:46Z","email":"kgarg@chapman.edu","name":"Krish Garg"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T20:06:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ai): give the task subprocess an env allowlist instead of a copy of the engine env (#2410)\n\nThe task subprocess (which runs pipeline code and anything a pipeline launches) inherited os.environ.copy() minus four ROCKETRIDE_DB_* names. It now gets an allowlist (filter_subprocess_env): the process-runtime baseline, the pipeline-facing ROCKETRIDE_* namespace, interpreter/ML-runtime prefixes, the services the child reaches itself (RR_STORE_*, RR_BASE_URL, RR_SIGNING_KEY, RR_CORS_ORIGINS, RR_OAUTH_BROKER_URL, AWS_*), MEDIA_TOOLKIT_FFMPEG, and README-documented node key fallbacks. Operators extend it with RR_SUBPROCESS_ENV (operator-only tier; a bare ''*'' restores full inheritance). The subprocess''s shared WebServer no longer re-reads the engine''s .env.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"30f721d6012953e194491d845a4f2391919d27cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/trees/30f721d6012953e194491d845a4f2391919d27cc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/commits/593bd5838e4020784d81a4f12e590abbd562a435","verification":{"payload":"tree 30f721d6012953e194491d845a4f2391919d27cc\nparent d18367ff165b25ab3620a325462761370cec4d8e\nauthor Krish Garg <kgarg@chapman.edu> 1790194006 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790194006 -0700\n\nfix(ai): give the task subprocess an env allowlist instead of a copy of the engine env (#2410)\n\nThe task subprocess (which runs pipeline code and anything a pipeline launches) inherited os.environ.copy() minus four ROCKETRIDE_DB_* names. It now gets an allowlist (filter_subprocess_env): the process-runtime baseline, the pipeline-facing ROCKETRIDE_* namespace, interpreter/ML-runtime prefixes, the services the child reaches itself (RR_STORE_*, RR_BASE_URL, RR_SIGNING_KEY, RR_CORS_ORIGINS, RR_OAUTH_BROKER_URL, AWS_*), MEDIA_TOOLKIT_FFMPEG, and README-documented node key fallbacks. Operators extend it with RR_SUBPROCESS_ENV (operator-only tier; a bare ''*'' restores full inheritance). The subprocess''s shared WebServer no longer re-reads the engine''s .env.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtDFWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYQUQAC6cpAggS4lQhjmVhVsluNq5\nUN5agyMVWJlOAFhTCyKvVD2r8Mq2O+6s+0qxDRb71Fp8i5niB+q73rmUJtMKsJx9\n3/dHtEq+4oTRSyOphgLkZZAvECvap9pwLjuZHzI2d2HD7SWlI+B1PJw15EP1q2fO\nIWn3ubx81c7uHbvVNlToOxRB/R1wMRlsJY7YW1KnYgNmYqMs95zj/W6NpSW+BXiE\nmNupPMhRTJiLFDLOwuvH0OC0XTR2ZyFgtr5gaN4UTeA1H8jrV8l7Ia+dA7JT2ibE\n5VCkrecyBqxndkDiXPPy/8POMo1TlGKiya/vBv6ljfbyB/8NvZsMBr9EFGYRVFph\njBMPzuz88iZDmeemnwsnaoYi8q+w/sMWKn/V81yO8S/PT/+vmsH32bGFLHi2E6Lo\n5m4DsrLc+Nmu0yZkB+aPAWgfUGX5dGNl3bj+AMuS0TkGxcRx+xceuyMvmchzWpZf\n24PpS02j8RQJBllaxkXizJqdc/XHpAjQpu5MsXFjA4tV6nidBwbhQn+X3HhJlb3p\nPUxc+EPH3432zu2wT63lty6luVy8bUD1rfNeQ6b6coOL2U8h8BoyigD1Z2xSmfwd\nVBrXLWAjEw94xnokznZjPcTzNNrKMpPP/0K3P19oJUKhEIbgPOePfpwEMDb8o+3H\nWRKDC+xtpe4M9zBGiASM\n=TdS6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T20:06:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/w