d close to, reached the engine without a thread\ncontext. The engine made one named \"External\", and the first call back\ninto Python (setupDebug) copied that over the thread''s Python name, so\nthe profiler listed every such thread as \"External\" and engine logs\ncould not be matched to Python ones.\n\nsyncThreadName() now settles one name per thread on both sides: a\nthread Python started keeps its name and the engine takes it; a thread\nPython knows only as a _DummyThread takes the engine''s name, as before.\nIt runs where Python enters the engine (UnlockPython, which now holds\ngil_scoped_release as a member initialized after the name sync, so the\nGIL is still held) and where the engine enters Python (setupDebug). The\nplaceholder becomes ThreadApi::ExternalName.\n\nNew engtest cases cover a Python-started thread, the same with a context\nmade before UnlockPython, an engine thread and a foreign thread; the\nfirst two failed before this change (\"External\" == \"rr-py-thread\").\n\n* test(engine): keep the thread-name workers from outliving their state\n\nThe Python worker was not a daemon, so a hang in a GIL path would have\nleft it alive and Py_FinalizeEx() at the end of the run waits for such a\nthread: the process would hang after reporting the failure. The engine\nand foreign workers kept their Names and Done on the Catch2 thread''s\nstack, which a worker abandoned on timeout writes into after Catch2 has\nunwound the case. Both now share one State through a shared_ptr the\nworker holds a copy of.","tree":{"sha":"b133d7526e25bf275d4779eed6dff865add31c95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/trees/b133d7526e25bf275d4779eed6dff865add31c95"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/commits/31cc9bfa2be9b9af7eeac298f9bde3eefa917e74","verification":{"payload":"tree b133d7526e25bf275d4779eed6dff865add31c95\nparent 274402fce3e1f8bcaa50bfe79e147b5fb9258bbb\nauthor Alexandru Sclearuc <asclearuc@gmail.com> 1790091203 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790091203 +0300\n\nfix(engine): keep a Python thread''s own name in the engine and in Python (#2369)\n\n* fix(engine): keep a Python thread''s own name in the engine and in Python\n\nA thread Python starts, such as the asyncio workers the data path hands\nevery pipe open, write and close to, reached the engine without a thread\ncontext. The engine made one named \"External\", and the first call back\ninto Python (setupDebug) copied that over the thread''s Python name, so\nthe profiler listed every such thread as \"External\" and engine logs\ncould not be matched to Python ones.\n\nsyncThreadName() now settles one name per thread on both sides: a\nthread Python started keeps its name and the engine takes it; a thread\nPython knows only as a _DummyThread takes the engine''s name, as before.\nIt runs where Python enters the engine (UnlockPython, which now holds\ngil_scoped_release as a member initialized after the name sync, so the\nGIL is still held) and where the engine enters Python (setupDebug). The\nplaceholder becomes ThreadApi::ExternalName.\n\nNew engtest cases cover a Python-started thread, the same with a context\nmade before UnlockPython, an engine thread and a foreign thread; the\nfirst two failed before this change (\"External\" == \"rr-py-thread\").\n\n* test(engine): keep the thread-name workers from outliving their state\n\nThe Python worker was not a daemon, so a hang in a GIL path would have\nleft it alive and Py_FinalizeEx() at the end of the run waits for such a\nthread: the process would hang after reporting the failure. The engine\nand foreign workers kept their Names and Done on the Catch2 thread''s\nstack, which a worker abandoned on timeout writes into after Catch2 has\nunwound the case. Both now share one State through a shared_ptr the\nworker holds a copy of.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsp/DCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdGQQADRg9KlF1UdwHT2/58fe43HH\nK8scrIKDEwMVSaA17etw70T+T4+PC745H5EGlD8AYTg6S3eGk7YQ5NlrrEzJ27kp\nm7jziu1x7+/o7jMADjtJRY6g8cp2n+a17CWNtqQ46qfccuB0tGiJIvkBwQ8vPvvG\nOBDnUExpK9uwFMLmLgNUZ0F8ha5kJD8pkGImRlODi2iYkELoIaliAEndTM8NhUsi\n6vwuvyzfY28a/sRcJBWHt8akefbsXa7WbUzhlz8uRf9Kb7uMSxCPUeQjUbj6Y3pM\n9OYnQqAjGblHvMvNpfRwjwvtEepi/4VS6UFFn41GDXfl/sKjAIyFwff56k0bsGZT\nYo8wkpqT2EdoGZaxMCmuXJ8OHvz88SnSC+X5WSAJrBR2rCe4yrwtWHQDhUChd3iZ\nrVM+W8WUK3SlCM/uBvR4j/TbZXiwQGoyZBAgxaacyN9/6GOeGsKzNP6uoy+pDRU1\nykdmIvxBvDlEI2Eg8J5LREw8xC6TQT30hc5eMEhzkdjTozWvjqluGYULssymqEfL\njN0T60gG7gJufh9Bx0qVz0fJyOE9u/O3W7hw3n2aCV9FDKBvkuB4wDpD86DWcZMs\ntpqiXhadx58Dfsk5ZAaJNLiKR5Dhi8Fsgod1+U5cafGf7bzdK6cJGokIHEHIUfL1\nFdomJYDtykc8H1ZTBu38\n=HkI9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T15:33:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commit/31cc9bfa2be9b9af7eeac298f9bde3eefa917e74","node_id":"C_kwDOROCxS9oAKDMxY2M5YmZhMmJlOWI5YWY3ZWVhYzI5OGY5YmRlM2VlZmE5MTdlNzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commit/274402fce3e1f8bcaa50bfe79e147b5fb9258bbb","sha":"274402fce3e1f8bcaa50bfe79e147b5fb9258bbb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/274402fce3e1f8bcaa50bfe79e147b5fb9258bbb"}],"sha":"31cc9bfa2be9b9af7eeac298f9bde3eefa917e74","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/31cc9bfa2be9b9af7eeac298f9bde3eefa917e74"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98939082?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rod-Christensen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rod-Christensen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rod-Christensen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rod-Christensen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Rod-Christensen","id":98939082,"login":"Rod-Christensen","node_id":"U_kgDOBeWwyg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rod-Christensen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rod-Christensen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rod-Christensen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rod-Christensen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rod-Christensen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rod-Christensen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/274402fce3e1f8bcaa50bfe79e147b5fb9258bbb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T00:27:02Z","email":"98939082+Rod-Christensen@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Rod-Christensen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T00:27:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(appdev): debug in the developer''s default browser, fix breakpoint binding, drop the scaffolded launch.json (#2386)\n\nF5 app debugging had three defects:\n\n- Breakpoints never bound: the app bundles'' sourcemaps carry sources\n  relative to the build root''s parent (the workspace root), so after the\n  browser clamps the leading \"../\"s js-debug sees\n  \"<origin>/apps/<name>/src/*.tsx\". With webRoot set to the APP folder the\n  mapped path doubled (\"…/apps/home-ui/apps/home-ui/…\") and never matched a\n  real file. webRoot is now the workspace root and the stale\n  sourceMapPathOverrides (written for webpack:/// URLs the bundles do not\n  emit) are gone.\n\n- The debug session was hardwired to Edge. New browser.ts resolves the\n  developer''s OS default browser onto a js-debug CDP target: Chrome/Edge map\n  to their native types, other Chromiums (Brave, Vivaldi, Opera, Arc) launch\n  through the ''chrome'' type with the registry-resolved runtimeExecutable,\n  and a non-Chromium default falls back to Edge with a log line explaining\n  why. Resolved once per session.\n\n- The scaffolder wrote a static launch.json entry that could not ensure the\n  watch session, so F5 from it opened a preview with no dev bundle served.\n  The entry (and ensureLaunchConfig) are removed: rocketride.app.debug is\n  the single debug entry point and builds its config in-memory.\n\nSupporting fixes:\n\n- appLoader.isDevPreviewPage() now returns false for TOP-LEVEL pages: only\n  framed pages (App Builder panel) receive the rrdev:registerRemote\n  postMessage injection. An F5 external-browser tab with rrdev=1 has no\n  embedder, and its dev entry is already in the server manifest (resolved\n  via the ?rrsession= nonce) — holding for a message that can never come\n  left the tab blank.\n\n- DesignView: the DEV watch-target badge is now a link that launches the\n  same debug session as the gear menu''s Debug (F5) row.\n\n- AGENTS.md: correct the ''./builder build'' description (global command,\n  builds every module, not server-only). README touch-ups: pin tiktoken\n  <1.0.0 in context_optimizer docs; regenerate core README wording.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8668cec9bd14996d10feaac5c6a624131b94d75f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/trees/8668cec9bd14996d10feaac5c6a624131b94d75f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/commits/274402fce3e1f8bcaa50bfe79e147b5fb9258bbb","verification":{"payload":"tree 8668cec9bd14996d10feaac5c6a624131b94d75f\nparent 51345baa5f8226f93a8ce77340a7ae0e3143d554\nauthor Rod-Christensen <98939082+Rod-Christensen@users.noreply.github.com> 1790036822 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790036822 -0700\n\nfix(appdev): debug in the developer''s default browser, fix breakpoint binding, drop the scaffolded launch.json (#2386)\n\nF5 app debugging had three defects:\n\n- Breakpoints never bound: the app bundles'' sourcemaps carry sources\n  relative to the build root''s parent (the workspace root), so after the\n  browser clamps the leading \"../\"s js-debug sees\n  \"<origin>/apps/<name>/src/*.tsx\". With webRoot set to the APP folder the\n  mapped path doubled (\"…/apps/home-ui/apps/home-ui/…\") and never matched a\n  real file. webRoot is now the workspace root and the stale\n  sourceMapPathOverrides (written for webpack:/// URLs the bundles do not\n  emit) are gone.\n\n- The debug session was hardwired to Edge. New browser.ts resolves the\n  developer''s OS default browser onto a js-debug CDP target: Chrome/Edge map\n  to their native types, other Chromiums (Brave, Vivaldi, Opera, Arc) launch\n  through the ''chrome'' type with the registry-resolved runtimeExecutable,\n  and a non-Chromium default falls back to Edge with a log line explaining\n  why. Resolved once per session.\n\n- The scaffolder wrote a static launch.json entry that could not ensure the\n  watch session, so F5 from it opened a preview with no dev bundle served.\n  The entry (and ensureLaunchConfig) are removed: rocketride.app.debug is\n  the single debug entry point and builds its config in-memory.\n\nSupporting fixes:\n\n- appLoader.isDevPreviewPage() now returns false for TOP-LEVEL pages: only\n  framed pages (App Builder panel) receive the rrdev:registerRemote\n  postMessage injection. An F5 external-browser tab with rrdev=1 has no\n  embedder, and its dev entry is already in the server manifest (resolved\n  via the ?rrsession= nonce) — holding for a message that can never come\n  left the tab blank.\n\n- DesignView: the DEV watch-target badge is now a link that launches the\n  same debug session as the gear menu''s Debug (F5) row.\n\n- AGENTS.md: correct the ''./builder build'' description (global command,\n  builds every module, not server-only). README touch-ups: pin tiktoken\n  <1.0.0 in context_optimizer docs; regenerate core README wording.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsctWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA79YQAGI/vmsHQU90k/MCBGT56c8x\n5vCIg0qJS8LIKq9/LT6omQX65VlPTFNsKisFagJ/t6YJnSGTiOHz8YKqYpS0P6jN\npyrKrTpuLzlNc+/hrn36c14Ysi/BUzc9ujl08mUX2z6ipgd9qj5AXjjLXBFTbvfg\noWZkbXmK2MQbMrqOSmsqvMQ/SLsKeVhzhvZdZ17oGx/2QxJ6Rxy6ZZgS7e+/iITN\nNRvFsZC/Llqv009PSPqaW5k4nb/xinejfJgr/h+8yIO+xKQiMemjpb7zbObEVvIS\nbG7uiEueMpmiX0fkRZVUqajwoRpbkxrjQzYiZX8EpxWfvNmYoVgZl8zsq2NmBcnu\n6QHWOdk5hhXFAGUbzQqmh3Qsigq6raD5FAmQyKHyHrnYltRyDiYeA0RIojK0sPWQ\nx4lJxKWLm1+cP1eUiX3lcXyFAiMYRBnScVlZkn+g0dqg2Z+SzZ12zH4uxE1/Eszm\nbrn8csXLtfEAoDd3cFkP/3pRXpopCMUnFf6beW4ej4gqqy5hOwgGmWgKG0syUthY\nEVEYb05ixKYSfqpV53BTAZbdSytTrxs+uzYhM/x7DPFqul0shqn4UuSiltLaHxlv\n1TKe6s5hk4vkRRIYINXWJWwDCBXd9I5zo5aK+U4jeq6I3XaXBpg4yr1w6GcyUiV2\nPf55A2aGlqgDcL5vxK1l\n=nl8f\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T00:27:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commit/274402fce3e1f8bcaa50bfe79e147b5fb9258bbb","node_id":"C_kwDOROCxS9oAKDI3NDQwMmZjZTNlMWY4YmNhYTUwYmZlNzllMTQ3YjVmYjkyNThiYmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commit/51345baa5f8226f93a8ce77340a7ae0e3143d554","sha":"51345baa5f8226f93a8ce77340a7ae0e3143d554","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/51345baa5f8226f93a8ce77340a7ae0e3143d554"}],"sha":"274402fce3e1f8bcaa50bfe79e147b5fb9258bbb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/274402fce3e1f8bcaa50bfe79e147b5fb9258bbb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184572825?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leela8256/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leela8256/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leela8256/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leela8256/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Leela8256","id":184572825,"login":"Leela8256","node_id":"U_kgDOCwBbmQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leela8256/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leela8256/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leela8256/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leela8256/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leela8256/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leela8256","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/51345baa5f8226f93a8ce77340a7ae0e3143d554/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T17:06:51Z","email":"leelaprasad.dammalapati@sjsu.edu","name":"Leela8256"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T17:06:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(db_hotdata): match the live Hotdata API result contract (#2372)\n\n* fix(db_hotdata): match the live Hotdata API result contract\n\nThree defects, all traced to the node disagreeing with what the API\nactually returns. Verified against api.hotdata.dev.\n\nResult rows never got their column names. /v1/query and /v1/results both\nanswer with `columns` (the names) and `rows` (lists of *values*), never\nwith objects:\n\n    {\"columns\": [\"city\",\"units\"], \"rows\": [[\"Reno\",200],[\"Austin\",120]]}\n\n_run_sql passed `rows` straight through, so everything downstream saw\npositional lists. _rows_to_markdown fell through its isinstance(dict)\ncheck to str(row) and emitted Python list reprs - \"[''Reno'', 200]\" - on\nthe answers, table and text lanes instead of a Markdown table. The same\ncause silently emptied _schema_via_sql, whose `if not isinstance(row,\ndict): continue` dropped every row, so natural-language SQL was\ngenerated against no schema at all. Names are now attached once, at the\n_run_sql boundary, with repeated and empty column names disambiguated so\n`SELECT city, city` cannot collapse to one value.\n\nget_result and get_query_run never sent X-Database-Id. Both endpoints\nare database-scoped and answer 400 \"this endpoint is scoped to a\ndatabase\" without it, so the whole deferred-query path - every truncated\nresult and every async run poll - failed 100% of the time.\n\nget_data retried failures no rewrite could fix. A bare `except\nException` fed anything back to the generator, so a bad workspace (HTTP\n404 workspace_not_found) spent three LLM calls and ~100s before\nreporting \"could not answer after 3 attempts\", with the real cause\nburied in the tail. Retries are now limited to what a different\nstatement could plausibly fix: HTTP 400, plus a deferred run that failed\nserver-side (SqlStatementError, which carries no HTTP status). Auth,\nworkspace, database and transport failures raise as-is, keeping the\nserver''s own wording. Same case now fails in ~8s naming the 404.\n\nAlso floors async_after_ms at 1000; the API rejects anything lower, so a\npipeline configured below it failed every query.\n\nFive existing tests changed: their mocks returned `rows` as dicts and\nraised SQL errors as bare RuntimeError, neither of which the live API\ndoes. That unfaithful mocking is why the row-naming bug shipped green.\nMocks now fail the way the client actually fails, and 13 new tests pin\nthe behaviour (162 collected, up from 149).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db_hotdata): stop a generated column key overwriting a real one\n\nReview catch. Both cases drop a value silently, which is the exact\nfailure the naming helper exists to prevent.\n\n_name_columns checked a generated name against the base it was derived\nfrom, not against the names already taken. `SELECT city, city, city_1`\nrenamed the second `city` to `city_1` and collided with the real third\ncolumn, so the dict kept two values out of three.\n\nThe same hole sat in the wider-than-header tail: `column_3` is a legal\ncolumn name, so for columns [''a'', ''column_3''] a three-value row parked\nits third value on the key already holding the second.\n\nBoth now allocate through _free_name, which suffixes until the key is\nunclaimed and reserves it. Two regression tests, which fail on the\nprevious code with ''city_1'' twice and [1, 3] respectively.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db_hotdata): retry on the statement-error contract, not a bare 400\n\nReview catch. _run_sql drives four endpoints - create_database, query,\nget_query_run, get_result - and `status_code == 400` treated a failure\nfrom any of them as SQL the model could rewrite. A bad ttl, a malformed\nlimit or a missing scoping header would each burn every LLM attempt and\nthen be replaced by \"could not answer after N attempts\", which is the\nexact masking this branch set out to remove.\n\nThe server distinguishes the two itself: it answers with a query_run_id\nonly once it has created a run and executed the statement. Verified\nagainst the live API - missing table, parse error and unknown function\nall return 400 with a run id; bad ttl and out-of-range limit return 400\nwithout one.\n\nHotdataError now carries query_run_id off the error body, and\n_is_sql_fixable requires it. SqlStatementError still covers the deferred\npath, where a terminal run failure is reported in the poll body with no\nHTTP status to read.\n\nFour tests: the client lifts the run id when present and leaves it empty\nwhen absent, and get_data retries the first while raising the second\nas-is without spending a second LLM call.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db_hotdata): close out the review - signature, schema, docs, rendering\n\nReview catch, plus a full pass over the branch for the same class of\nproblem so they land together rather than one per round.\n\nget_result kept `offset` and `limit` in their original positions.\nDatabase scoping had been inserted ahead of them, so a positional\nget_result(result_id, offset, limit) written against the old signature\nwould have sent its offset as the X-Database-Id header. `database_id` is\nnow keyword-only and last.\n\nservices.json advertised `minimum: 0` for async_after_ms while the node\nfloors it at 1000, so the form accepted a value the node then silently\noverrode. Both now read 1000 - the smallest the API accepts - and a test\nties the schema to the constant so they cannot drift apart.\n\nA cancelled run is no longer classified as a statement failure. A\nrewritten query cannot un-cancel a run, so it must not earn an LLM turn.\n\nTwo rendering bugs that only became reachable once rows were objects:\nheader cells were not escaped, so an alias such as \"a|b\" split its\ncolumn in two, and SQL NULL rendered as the Python word \"None\". Headers\ngo through _cell like body cells, and NULL is an empty cell.\n\nREADME: get_data retries a rejected statement, not any failure, and the\ntroubleshooting table says why a 401/404 surfaces on the first attempt.\n\nCorrects a claim made earlier on this branch. The docstrings cited\n`SELECT city, city` as the source of repeated column names; the planner\nrejects that outright. Verified against the live API, the real source is\na join - `SELECT a.city, b.city` answers [''city'', ''city''] and `SELECT *`\nover a self-join answers [''city'', ''units'', ''city'', ''units'']. The naming\nhelper is needed for exactly that, and a test now pins the live shape.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db_hotdata): feed the real failure reason back for a deferred run\n\nFound by driving the deferred path against the live API, which no test\nhad done: every earlier live query was small enough to return inline.\n\nA run that fails after deferring reports its cause as `error_message`:\n\n    {\"status\": \"failed\",\n     \"error_message\": \"query execution failed: Arrow error: Divide by zero error\"}\n\n_await_run read `error` or `message`, found neither, and fell back to the\nstatus, so the exception read \"query failed: failed\". That text is what\nthe model is handed for its corrective attempt, so every deferred\nfailure was being retried blind. The jobs poller in the same file\nalready reads `error_message`; this was the one place with guessed keys,\ncovered by a mock that encoded the guess.\n\n_run_failure_text reads `error_message` first, then `error` as text or\nas the {\"message\": ...} object the query endpoint uses, then `message`.\n\nVerified live with a 20M-row window query that divides by zero on its\nlast row: the run deferred, polled four times, failed, and the caller\nnow receives the Arrow error. The same session confirmed the deferred\nsuccess path (query -> 4x get_query_run -> get_result) and the truncated\npath (query truncated=true -> get_result) end to end for the first time.\n\nAlso adds docstrings to the functions this branch touches; coverage on\ntouched functions goes from 66% to 90%.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db_hotdata): wait for the run before reading a truncated result\n\nAddresses the review on #2372, read against the published contract at\nhttps://www.hotdata.dev/openapi.yaml.\n\nA result that was still being saved came back as an empty answer. A\ntruncated /v1/query response always carries a result_id, so the old\n`result_id is None` test never waited for it - and per QueryResponse\nthat id \"is issued while the save is still in flight, so on its own it\ndoes not mean the result can be retrieved\". Reading it early answers 202\n{status, result_id} with no rows; _request only raises from 400 up, so\n_run_sql returned zero rows for a result large enough to be truncated.\nReproduced live with an 8M-row query: 200 truncated, then 202\n\"processing\", then 200 once the run had succeeded. _run_sql now waits on\nthe run whenever the server deferred or truncated, and get_result raises\non a pending/processing body instead of letting it read as empty.\n\n`interrupted` is a documented terminal run status the poll loop did not\nknow, so it was polled until job_timeout_secs ran out and reported as a\ntimeout that never happened. It is now terminal and raised as a plain\nRuntimeError, not SqlStatementError: a rewritten statement cannot\nun-interrupt a run. `cancelled`/`canceled` were never seen live; the\ncomment on the set says so.\n\n_query_run_id reads inside the `error` object as well as beside it, the\nway _error_code does, since the documented error body is\n{\"error\": {code, message}}.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Update nodes/src/nodes/db_hotdata/IInstance.py\n\nCo-authored-by: Alexandru Sclearuc <asclearuc@gmail.com>\n\n* fix(db_hotdata): run an interrupted query once more, as the contract says\n\nAddresses the three notes left with the approval on #2372.\n\n`interrupted` was classified correctly - terminal, not the statement''s\nfault, never SqlStatementError - but nothing acted on the other half of\nthe contract, which calls it \"terminal, and safe to retry\". The caller\nlost a whole tool call because Hotdata replaced a server, and so did\n`execute` and `get_schema`, which share the path.\n\n_run_sql now runs the same statement once more when the run comes back\ninterrupted. It is bounded at one re-run, so a run interrupted every\ntime still ends; it sends the same SQL, so it costs no LLM turn; and it\nis safe to send twice because only read-only statements reach it.\n_await_run signals the case with its own RunInterrupted type, a\nRuntimeError, so `cancelled` and failed statements are never re-run and\neverything that already treats it as \"not the SQL''s fault\" still does.\n\nPins the suggestion applied in e5fa0d8f: a run that reaches a\nterminal-OK status without a result_id still reads the id the query\nanswered with, instead of falling through to an empty result. The test\nfails on c6282753 and passes from e5fa0d8f.\n\nSettles the result_id handed out on the inline fast path. It is issued\nwhile the save is still in flight, and it is safe to hand out anyway:\nthe loads endpoint documents 409 \"the result is still being computed\"\nrather than loading part of a result, and three loads issued right\nbehind a 9,500-row query each returned all 9,500 rows. The code says so\nwhere the id is returned.\n\nThe re-run is covered by mocks only - a server replacement cannot be\nprovoked from outside - so it rests on the spec''s wording.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db_hotdata): a run is finished when its status says so\n\nAddresses the review on #2372 at 1c67cd9e.\n\nBlocking: _await_run returned as soon as a run named a result_id, even\nwhile it was still `running`. The spec''s `running` covers \"still\nexecuting, or still being saved\", so that id names a result that is not\nready; a read against it answers 202, which raises and fails the whole\nquestion. Truncated results have come through this path since c6282753,\nwhich is what made it reachable. It now returns on the status alone.\n\nA run that ends succeeded with no result_id \"saved nothing\", so the id on\nthe query body names a result that was never saved. e5fa0d8f fell back\nto reading that id, which answers 404 or 202. The statement did succeed,\nand a truncated response carries a preview of its rows, so that preview\nis returned instead, cut to the limit, and no result_id is offered. A\ndeferred query has nothing inline, so it raises with the run''s\nwarning_message rather than report an empty result.\n\nNot changed, deliberately: a `failed` run behind a truncated preview is\nstill handed to the model as a statement failure. The preview is\nstreamed before the statement finishes, so it can fail on a later row.\nChecked live - an 8M-row query whose last row divides by zero answered\n200 truncated with 10,000 rows in 0.3s, and its run then ended failed\nwith \"query execution failed: Arrow error: Divide by zero error\". A\nrewrite fixes that. `failed` also covers a failed save, but only\nerror_message tells the two apart, and that is prose, not contract. The\ncode and a test now record this.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Alexandru Sclearuc <asclearuc@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"0704b603c9dcb078c0da2b5c42b041deba5436c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/trees/0704b603c9dcb078c0da2b5c42b041deba5436c5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/commits/51345baa5f8226f93a8ce77340a7ae0e3143d554","verification":{"payload":"tree 0704b603c9dcb078c0da2b5c42b041deba5436c5\nparent 9e902c1c5fccdcdeb3be969f3e80cd6b2002a991\nauthor Leela8256 <leelaprasad.dammalapati@sjsu.edu> 1790010411 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790010411 -0700\n\nfix(db_hotdata): match the live Hotdata API result contract (#2372)\n\n* fix(db_hotdata): match the live Hotdata API result contract\n\nThree defects, all traced to the node disagreeing with what the API\nactually returns. Verified against api.hotdata.dev.\n\nResult rows never got their column names. /v1/query and /v1/results both\nanswer with `columns` (the names) and `rows` (lists of *values*), never\nwith objects:\n\n    {\"columns\": [\"city\",\"units\"], \"rows\": [[\"Reno\",200],[\"Austin\",120]]}\n\n_run_sql passed `rows` straight through, so everything downstream saw\npositional lists. _rows_to_markdown fell through its isinstance(dict)\ncheck to str(row) and emitted Python list reprs - \"[''Reno'', 200]\" - on\nthe answers, table and text lanes instead of a Markdown table. The same\ncause silently emptied _schema_via_sql, whose `if not isinstance(row,\ndict): continue` dropped every row, so natural-language SQL was\ngenerated against no schema at all. Names are now attached once, at the\n_run_sql boundary, with repeated and empty column names disambiguated so\n`SELECT city, city` cannot collapse to one value.\n\nget_result and get_query_run never sent X-Database-Id. Both endpoints\nare database-scoped and answer 400 \"this endpoint is scoped to a\ndatabase\" without it, so the whole deferred-query 