tps://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commit/7fb23a224abc94c2c768fb421c5ffda4862b1505","node_id":"C_kwDOROCxS9oAKDdmYjIzYTIyNGFiYzk0YzJjNzY4ZmI0MjFjNWZmZGE0ODYyYjE1MDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commit/e0033a207a3aa075a3c8c684660c8f835cbc320c","sha":"e0033a207a3aa075a3c8c684660c8f835cbc320c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/e0033a207a3aa075a3c8c684660c8f835cbc320c"}],"sha":"7fb23a224abc94c2c768fb421c5ffda4862b1505","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/7fb23a224abc94c2c768fb421c5ffda4862b1505"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29624014?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/asclearuc","id":29624014,"login":"asclearuc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NjI0MDE0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/asclearuc","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/e0033a207a3aa075a3c8c684660c8f835cbc320c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T14:53:14Z","email":"asclearuc@gmail.com","name":"Alexandru Sclearuc"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T14:53:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(audio_player): accept stop()''s leftover sentinel in the drain test (#2306)\n\n`stop()` queues its own `None` sentinel when it starts waiting before the audio callback has reached the decoder''s. The callback stops at the first `None`, so the second one stays in the queue. `test_begin_write_end_still_drains_normally` still required an empty queue, so it failed whenever `stop()` won that race, which happens on a loaded CI runner.\n\n- The drain test now accepts `[]` or `[None]` as the leftover. Unplayed audio still fails it.\n- New `test_stop_waiting_before_the_callback_leaves_only_its_own_sentinel` forces the `stop()`-first order. It requires exactly `[None]` to be left, all audio played, and `stop()` returned.\n- The shared setup moved into `_player_with_queued_audio()` and `_start_simulated_hardware()`.","tree":{"sha":"cdf784c44c8456b4ad535473d6120bd5481665e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/trees/cdf784c44c8456b4ad535473d6120bd5481665e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/commits/e0033a207a3aa075a3c8c684660c8f835cbc320c","verification":{"payload":"tree cdf784c44c8456b4ad535473d6120bd5481665e0\nparent 668dbc1e6669fb82c86418a6e0b92e037d5593e3\nauthor Alexandru Sclearuc <asclearuc@gmail.com> 1789656794 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789656794 +0000\n\nfix(audio_player): accept stop()''s leftover sentinel in the drain test (#2306)\n\n`stop()` queues its own `None` sentinel when it starts waiting before the audio callback has reached the decoder''s. The callback stops at the first `None`, so the second one stays in the queue. `test_begin_write_end_still_drains_normally` still required an empty queue, so it failed whenever `stop()` won that race, which happens on a loaded CI runner.\n\n- The drain test now accepts `[]` or `[None]` as the leftover. Unplayed audio still fails it.\n- New `test_stop_waiting_before_the_callback_leaves_only_its_own_sentinel` forces the `stop()`-first order. It requires exactly `[None]` to be left, all audio played, and `stop()` returned.\n- The shared setup moved into `_player_with_queued_audio()` and `_start_simulated_hardware()`.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqq/7aCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzfIQAGZoIcIhMVwx+ZV+rGXVeNQJ\nffS0HlDOitm8ahGWNdQ300rzW6WgFXWaW7L2kMg9R0vNQe/ZlsOS1CYmDW9PFeLW\nsPdA/NktjXuMJrmjGxF0Iz0r/9jP84mcAD7bUILtIcnKIGNWwHfbMDI4og6tNemz\nqg0+1f1+sfMKgKgEuNDV2AgAZQw01H9s30oRzVfX7sM5lc1cEYYeVCc4s/CtsYpd\nu6am3dgGCsKIKUYsYmcFZYv6ZH1whuVqrLCkcz7okA15Eog99miTYkLviZstIjD7\nSb2fw7et4wuQRM91YX1wgSBwzF1ao5Z+PunalKo+PWDjbueeWXLq2SBTaXpWMduZ\nLTWqpk+IabTwOKFao6N75U+VzOsoyvr4A8wQtpdAmnqhmo7yeJZu9W97JOa9t7S9\nKZBT3mPcFF/+D+ruIsMMvFkayt7jZyI/6GWOvw0o9dbdLtFXPeMY3K8oB9gv8gi3\nG6GI/2spVYroRqcJi2YyexMSvvNRhwzr8yePsat2UQY3QLRCAcB1sewgimXbnXh5\nRn41Bwknf7SBBz99Z1TqC1gr2qQXL07vWGH9VcdHBJdQPgv9R106LBGqTit+pvZ2\nENqsF74EXTpTSgI26INTkQsvJWkTapVL2KIACi+RyssBpUrI7dsIx/8GN9lABqDv\ns0hMinwIXuu4Edgl9xT0\n=sqHr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T14:53:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commit/e0033a207a3aa075a3c8c684660c8f835cbc320c","node_id":"C_kwDOROCxS9oAKGUwMDMzYTIwN2EzYWEwNzVhM2M4YzY4NDY2MGM4ZjgzNWNiYzMyMGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commit/668dbc1e6669fb82c86418a6e0b92e037d5593e3","sha":"668dbc1e6669fb82c86418a6e0b92e037d5593e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/668dbc1e6669fb82c86418a6e0b92e037d5593e3"}],"sha":"e0033a207a3aa075a3c8c684660c8f835cbc320c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/e0033a207a3aa075a3c8c684660c8f835cbc320c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86812966?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PianoFanatic13/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PianoFanatic13/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PianoFanatic13/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PianoFanatic13/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PianoFanatic13","id":86812966,"login":"PianoFanatic13","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2ODEyOTY2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PianoFanatic13/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PianoFanatic13/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PianoFanatic13/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PianoFanatic13/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PianoFanatic13/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PianoFanatic13","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/commits/668dbc1e6669fb82c86418a6e0b92e037d5593e3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T14:20:01Z","email":"86812966+PianoFanatic13@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Abdul-Raqib Islam"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T14:20:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(memory_persistent): prevent double-forward of questions and answers (#1682)\n\n* fix(memory_persistent): prevent double-forward of questions and answers\n\n* test(memory_persistent): assert preventDefault is called on explicit forwards\n\n* docs(memory_persistent): note preventDefault() unreachability and test stub caveat\n\n* fix(memory_persistent): cover all six exits with delivery-count tests\n\n- Every exit of `writeQuestions` and `writeAnswers` now ends in `return self.preventDefault()`. The separate `return` after `preventDefault()` could never run, because `preventDefault()` raises.\n- `test_node.py`: two tests for the invalid `session_id` paths, which no test reached before. Removing `preventDefault()` from either path now fails a test.\n- `test_lane_forward_once_nodes.py`: six delivery-count cases, one per exit (no store, invalid session, normal path), under the engine''s forward rule. On the normal path, only the enriched or stored copy reaches downstream, never the original.\n- Docstrings in `IInstance.py` now document their arguments.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Alexandru Sclearuc <asclearuc@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"5d10fb6233880a5543973b66202ba1fdbab52ef4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/trees/5d10fb6233880a5543973b66202ba1fdbab52ef4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/git/commits/668dbc1e6669fb82c86418a6e0b92e037d5593e3","verification":{"payload":"tree 5d10fb6233880a5543973b66202ba1fdbab52ef4\nparent 97bb71c55c656830cb9fbd2fc7f1ccda2014118a\nauthor Abdul-Raqib Islam <86812966+PianoFanatic13@users.noreply.github.com> 1789654801 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789654801 +0300\n\nfix(memory_persistent): prevent double-forward of questions and answers (#1682)\n\n* fix(memory_persistent): prevent double-forward of questions and answers\n\n* test(memory_persistent): assert preventDefault is called on explicit forwards\n\n* docs(memory_persistent): note preventDefault() unreachability and test stub caveat\n\n* fix(memory_persistent): cover all six exits with delivery-count tests\n\n- Every exit of `writeQuestions` and `writeAnswers` now ends in `return self.preventDefault()`. The separate `return` after `preventDefault()` could never run, because `preventDefault()` raises.\n- `test_node.py`: two tests for the invalid `session_id` paths, which no test reached before. Removing `preventDefault()` from either path now fails a test.\n- `test_lane_forward_once_nodes.py`: six delivery-count cases, one per exit (no store, invalid session, normal path), under the engine''s forward rule. On the normal path, only the enriched or stored copy reaches downstream, never the original.\n- Docstrings in `IInstance.py` now document their arguments.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Alexandru Sclearuc <asclearuc@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqq/cRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOJcQAKpVEiV2xmn24Aa5s4/qTfvM\nC+BxwEtqoY+WH4mTwAvaiXVrxkNslVgIsrYv9gylODJx4l80AYT1Sq6AOnx9Z8Wk\ngBxoBCBizeSXZrQKds8xnSxJhQgmH5RB2e8Pu9EXwZIy054k/322xtKv4l1Eq7zY\nWdytHq9UwFMnlQLHKBS8riQVbEQwKAU17+Kd7+C1BcIW9QZ6wnS/9wSvrzVeaiTo\nH+36lUjI8eT2sLjBOwT/17GX3lpnOSlg/TCBG7xjJO7dpaJA9VASNzgx0/SYU10Z\nQOk8lEn9tgPf5gHjfWI/eRbrie8i6Mhu85JwMDDQHsdd925M/DPCqi+LazpHznPC\nWfUmfvxsMI96Y9Vj0O9DCTB0NQjjZ4lUVzLz4IJgagLG1qbFD6Ucci9ZkEwljsLk\nx8N8qW92SMx7PI8kJgVblPKg1fspsAAqcJ4v/xBrSVgd+Q0XqB/8f88cGzY5ODsa\nuCtZGWS8Db5u4KF96zk9G3GaNxcPWRUplsd602dLH/9gaH6qbskw12Qe5XMPvT6C\njoQg/cOFP7QFveN9vk/FnlfOC/R11bLdbM5CWtS8MGmeDlaNMM8ETOGCWdsgvANX\nNhLl0FJOD2FNCFtcVrfYRx8l3dPL7WRz8ipgmaKUD0H2MP/I4jCpqu7OGXJnRWFU\n1UEiAeSTQAD0FS2oFCk6\n=fMM4\n-----END PGP 