{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RogeMateos","id":2786311,"login":"RogeMateos","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3ODYzMTE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RogeMateos/JuniorToSenior/commits/b412a9f3d0be30c676391456c5796032357cae5e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-20T13:58:46Z","email":"rogemateos@hotmail.com","name":"Roge"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-20T13:58:46Z","email":"rogemateos@hotmail.com","name":"Roge"},"message":"Add Infrastructure as Code with Terraform tutorial (4.0)\n\n- Create tutorial: \"🌍 4.0 Infrastructure as Code with Terraform\"\n- Covers IaC fundamentals, Terraform concepts, production workflows\n\nContent includes:\n- The real problem (manual infrastructure chaos at scale)\n- Why IaC exists (40 microservices, 3 environments, 15 developers scenario)\n- Solution: declarative infrastructure as code\n- Imperative vs Declarative approach (bash scripts vs Terraform)\n- What Terraform really is (comparison engine, state manager, change executor)\n- The STATE file (most important concept):\n  - What it contains (resources, IDs, relationships)\n  - Real problem: simultaneous terraform apply\n  - Remote State solution (S3 + DynamoDB locking)\n- Professional real workflow (PR-based, not local):\n  - Dev creates branch\n  - terraform fmt, validate, plan in pipeline\n  - Review plan before applying\n  - Infrastructure as code reviewed by PR\n- Project structure (main.tf, variables.tf, outputs.tf, providers.tf)\n- Practical minimal example (Security Group with provider, variables, main, outputs)\n- Basic commands (init, fmt, validate, plan, apply, destroy)\n- Variables and environments (dev/staging/prod with separate state)\n- Security (no hardcoding, Secrets Manager, IAM roles, env vars in CI)\n- Terraform vs CloudFormation vs CDK comparison\n- Advanced concepts:\n  - Drift detection (manual AWS changes)\n  - Import (bringing existing infrastructure to state)\n  - Modules (preventing code duplication)\n- When to use/not use Terraform (scale considerations)\n- Final mental model (\"Git for infrastructure\")\n- When to choose what (when to use Terraform vs when overkill)\n- Key takeaways on state, locking, idempotency, secrets\n\nFiles created:\n- softwarecycle/en/terraform-iac.html\n- softwarecycle/es/terraform-iac.html\n\nNavigation:\n- Added bilingual link to Section 7 (Software Lifecycle)\n- New major category 4.0 (Infrastructure as Code)\n- Updated app.js with proper language-aware routing\n\nResources:\n- Added Dragos ChatGPT Infrastructure as Code with Terraform guide link\n\nThemes:\n- From manual to automated infrastructure\n- State management fundamentals\n- Team collaboration and safety\n- Security in IaC (secrets, IAM)\n- Professional workflows with Git and CI/CD\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"edeb99da571a0f0a746fc7ee24dd968eb7965c15","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RogeMateos/JuniorToSenior/git/trees/edeb99da571a0f0a746fc7ee24dd968eb7965c15"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RogeMateos/JuniorToSenior/git/commits/b412a9f3d0be30c676391456c5796032357cae5e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2786311?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RogeMateos","id":2786311,"login":"RogeMateos","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3ODYzMTE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/RogeMateos/JuniorToSenior/commit/b412a9f3d0be30c676391456c5796032357cae5e","node_id":"C_kwDORO5BhtoAKGI0MTJhOWYzZDBiZTMwYzY3NjM5MTQ1NmM1Nzk2MDMyMzU3Y2FlNWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/RogeMateos/JuniorToSenior/commit/63a1aab25306221d87e768b6b0ac5763e29fa046","sha":"63a1aab25306221d87e768b6b0ac5763e29fa046","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RogeMateos/JuniorToSenior/commits/63a1aab25306221d87e768b6b0ac5763e29fa046"}],"sha":"b412a9f3d0be30c676391456c5796032357cae5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RogeMateos/JuniorToSenior/commits/b412a9f3d0be30c676391456c5796032357cae5e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2786311?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RogeMateos","id":2786311,"login":"RogeMateos","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3ODYzMTE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RogeMateos/JuniorToSenior/commits/63a1aab25306221d87e768b6b0ac5763e29fa046/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-20T13:56:50Z","email":"rogemateos@hotmail.com","name":"Roge"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-20T13:56:50Z","email":"rogemateos@hotmail.com","name":"Roge"},"message":"Add Lambda Cold Start deep dive tutorial (3.1)\n\n- Create tutorial: \"❄️ 3.1 Lambda Cold Start\"\n- Covers cold start mechanics, real-world impact, mitigation strategies\n\nContent includes:\n- Minimum serverless architecture (API Gateway → Lambda → Database)\n- What a cold start really is (5-step process, not just code download)\n- Components: API Gateway (routing, auth, rate limiting), Lambda, Database options\n- Why cold starts matter (p95/p99 latency, user experience, timeouts)\n- What makes cold starts worse (junior mistakes):\n  - Huge bundles (5-10MB)\n  - Code outside handler\n  - Poor DB connection management\n  - Lambda in VPC without need\n  - Heavy libraries\n  - Poor JWT validation\n- How to mitigate:\n  - Make functions lightweight (esbuild, lazy loading, minimal globals)\n  - EventBridge warmup (hack, not clean architecture)\n  - Provisioned Concurrency (official solution with cost trade-off)\n- Real cost vs marketing (when Lambda is ideal, when it''s not)\n- Anti-pattern vs right pattern examples\n- Observability (Init Duration, p95/p99, X-Ray, CloudWatch)\n- Final engineering checklist (8-point production readiness)\n- Senior decision-making table (Lambda vs juniors'' approach)\n- Truth about serverless (not magic, not always cheaper/better)\n- When to choose what (scenario-based decision table)\n- Key takeaway: Never optimize what you don''t measure\n\nFiles created:\n- softwarecycle/en/lambda-cold-start.html\n- softwarecycle/es/lambda-cold-start.html\n\nNavigation:\n- Added bilingual link to Section 7 (Software Lifecycle)\n- Positioned as 3.1 (deep dive into Lambda, following 3.0)\n- Updated app.js with proper language-aware routing\n\nResources:\n- Added Dragos ChatGPT Lambda Cold Start architecture guide link\n\nThemes:\n- Real engineering vs marketing hype\n- Measurement-driven optimization\n- Senior decision-making frameworks\n- Trade-offs in architecture\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8faaed9c528d3a362a252b918c74dfe7657ada1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RogeMateos/JuniorToSenior/git/trees/8faaed9c528d3a362a252b918c74dfe7657ada1a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RogeMateos/JuniorToSenior/git/commits/63a1aab25306221d87e768b6b0ac5763e29fa046","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2786311?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RogeMateos","id":2786311,"login":"RogeMateos","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3ODYzMTE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/RogeMateos/JuniorToSenior/commit/63a1aab25306221d87e768b6b0ac5763e29fa046","node_id":"C_kwDORO5BhtoAKDYzYTFhYWIyNTMwNjIyMWQ4N2U3NjhiNmIwYWM1NzYzZTI5ZmEwNDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/RogeMateos/JuniorToSenior/commit/3855eb940e5da7bf5df8ad0b00097f8230a92bcd","sha":"3855eb940e5da7bf5df8ad0b00097f8230a92bcd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RogeMateos/JuniorToSenior/commits/3855eb940e5da7bf5df8ad0b00097f8230a92bcd"}],"sha":"63a1aab25306221d87e768b6b0ac5763e29fa046","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RogeMateos/JuniorToSenior/commits/63a1aab25306221d87e768b6b0ac5763e29fa046"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2786311?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RogeMateos","id":2786311,"login":"RogeMateos","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3ODYzMTE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RogeMateos/JuniorToSenior/commits/3855eb940e5da7bf5df8ad0b00097f8230a92bcd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-20T13:44:13Z","email":"rogemateos@hotmail.com","name":"Roge"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-20T13:44:13Z","email":"rogemateos@hotmail.com","name":"Roge"},"message":"Add Serverless with AWS Lambda tutorial (3.0)\n\n- Create tutorial: \"⚡️ 3.0 Serverless with AWS Lambda\"\n- Covers serverless fundamentals, cost models, real-world patterns\n\nContent includes:\n- What serverless really means (no server management, not no servers)\n- Mental model: Build → Cold Start → Invocation → Warm Reuse\n- When to use Lambda (irregular traffic, MVPs, event-driven, async)\n- When NOT to use Lambda (long processes, persistent WebSockets)\n- Typical production architecture (API Gateway → Lambda → RDS Proxy → RDS)\n- First Lambda HTTP handler in Node.js\n- Understanding event and context objects\n- Cost model (invocations, execution time, GB-seconds memory)\n- Memory optimization (more memory = more CPU = faster execution)\n- Real problem: Concurrency and database connections\n- Professional solutions (RDS Proxy, SQS buffering, reserved concurrency)\n- Security: Principle of Least Privilege in IAM\n- Observability without SSH (CloudWatch, structured logs, X-Ray)\n- Event-driven architecture (S3, SQS, EventBridge, Cron, DynamoDB)\n- Cold starts and when they matter\n- Avoiding logic fragmentation (too many small Lambda functions)\n- Lambda vs EC2 comparison table\n- Practical exercises (health endpoint, S3 events, peak control)\n- What seniors understand vs juniors\n- Professional architecture rule (Lambda scales free, DB doesn''t)\n- Designing for backpressure, retry, idempotency, concurrency\n\nFiles created:\n- softwarecycle/en/serverless-lambda.html\n- softwarecycle/es/serverless-lambda.html\n\nNavigation:\n- Added bilingual link to Section 7 (Software Lifecycle)\n- Positioned as new category 3.0 (after containers 2.0-2.1)\n- Updated app.js with proper language-aware routing\n\nResources:\n- Added Dragos ChatGPT Serverless with Lambda guide link\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":