m/users/RogeMateos/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RogeMateos","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RogeMateos/JuniorToSenior/commits/32d41168318ffeba9970babe03ea41dbf5dc699c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-20T13:13:23Z","email":"rogemateos@hotmail.com","name":"Roge"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-20T13:13:23Z","email":"rogemateos@hotmail.com","name":"Roge"},"message":"Update Network Security Fundamentals in AWS tutorial with extended content\n\n- Enhanced network security tutorial with comprehensive coverage\n- 16 detailed sections covering VPC, subnets, Security Groups, NACLs\n- Real-world examples: Backend + RDS architecture, debugging timeouts\n- Senior mindset: security as architecture, least privilege principle\n- Updated navigation link with \"1.7\" numbering in app.js\n- Added Dragos ChatGPT resource link\n\nTopics covered:\n- VPC mental model (your mini virtual data center)\n- Public vs private subnets and what makes something truly public\n- Security Groups as per-resource firewalls (stateful)\n- NACL vs Security Group comparison\n- Least Privilege principle and Security Group referencing\n- NAT Gateway for private subnet internet egress\n- Production checklist and debugging guide (timeout vs auth errors)\n- Egress security and data exfiltration prevention\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"13b9cf24ace006fe82b7d93c037e0331b057c0d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RogeMateos/JuniorToSenior/git/trees/13b9cf24ace006fe82b7d93c037e0331b057c0d9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RogeMateos/JuniorToSenior/git/commits/32