"parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/508f1ac336f4f759fb54b2af373b3508a7ba38fa","sha":"508f1ac336f4f759fb54b2af373b3508a7ba38fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/508f1ac336f4f759fb54b2af373b3508a7ba38fa"}],"sha":"d319872b791f044706e3d3a75263f18f6bb5286e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/d319872b791f044706e3d3a75263f18f6bb5286e"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/508f1ac336f4f759fb54b2af373b3508a7ba38fa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T00:29:12Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T00:29:12Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"message":"Shoreline Geology: Shoreforms — seven color groups instead of twelve classes\n\nPer Tina Whitman: all feeder bluffs one sediment-supply red, estuaries and\nlagoons one embayment cyan, and pocket beaches (blue), transport zones\n(amber), barrier / accretion beaches (yellow), rocky shoreline (grey) and\nartificial (near-black) kept separate. Map, legend and sourcing modal use the\ngroups; the popup still titles the exact class with its group in the subtitle.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"317d27c08f694c2b6146c7bc292f1a34e79e5897","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/trees/317d27c08f694c2b6146c7bc292f1a34e79e5897"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/commits/508f1ac336f4f759fb54b2af373b3508a7ba38fa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/508f1ac336f4f759fb54b2af373b3508a7ba38fa","node_id":"C_kwDORPBA8toAKDUwOGYxYWMzMzZmNGY3NTlmYjU0YjJhZjM3M2IzNTA4YTdiYTM4ZmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/f12f684e917ac7b51fd1c0c7abd4be9d201e17f8","sha":"f12f684e917ac7b51fd1c0c7abd4be9d201e17f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/f12f684e917ac7b51fd1c0c7abd4be9d201e17f8"}],"sha":"508f1ac336f4f759fb54b2af373b3508a7ba38fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/508f1ac336f4f759fb54b2af373b3508a7ba38fa"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/f12f684e917ac7b51fd1c0c7abd4be9d201e17f8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T23:30:09Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T23:30:09Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"message":"Shoreline legibility: \"What''s here\" chooser, hover labels, and a stacking rule\n\n- Chooser: a click on a stacked shoreline gathers every visible feature within\n  12 px (services/hitTest.ts, screen-pixel distance with cached bboxes) plus\n  the property under the point from the parcel tiles, and opens a \"What''s\n  here\" list when there is more than one; each row opens its popup. Pins open\n  directly. Parcel clicks with a line nearby get the same list.\n- Hover (desktop): the line under the cursor brightens and a small label\n  names the layer and feature; hit layers forward hover to the visible line.\n- Stacking: zIndex on shore layers (herring fill low … armor high), the forage\n  bands narrow from zoom 15 to 18, and parcel edges go hairline from zoom 17.\n- _popup-test.html?hit=lat,lng&z=&l= renders the chooser for a point.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dbd46a611275c8e713ea43d40dcde50dcc709db1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/trees/dbd46a611275c8e713ea43d40dcde50dcc709db1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/commits/f12f684e917ac7b51fd1c0c7abd4be9d201e17f8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/f12f684e917ac7b51fd1c0c7abd4be9d201e17f8","node_id":"C_kwDORPBA8toAKGYxMmY2ODRlOTE3YWM3YjUxZmQxYzBjN2FiZDRiZTlkMjAxZTE3Zjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/14e89ddfab90307de6a570c2e8cebf8371ec5f95","sha":"14e89ddfab90307de6a570c2e8cebf8371ec5f95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/14e89ddfab90307de6a570c2e8cebf8371ec5f95"}],"sha":"f12f684e917ac7b51fd1c0c7abd4be9d201e17f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/f12f684e917ac7b51fd1c0c7abd4be9d201e17f8"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/14e89ddfab90307de6a570c2e8cebf8371ec5f95/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T23:18:40Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T23:18:40Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"message":"Rename the Friends'' Projects layer to \"Friends habitat restoration projects\"\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c219139d8ef88034129016a4103cf6b8be37385e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/trees/c219139d8ef88034129016a4103cf6b8be37385e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/commits/14e89ddfab90307de6a570c2e8cebf8371ec5f95","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/14e89ddfab90307de6a570c2e8cebf8371ec5f95","node_id":"C_kwDORPBA8toAKDE0ZTg5ZGRmYWI5MDMwN2RlNmE1NzBjMmU4Y2ViZjgzNzFlYzVmOTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/4eec6628e6f17fc9faafa975d1356593058f7e4c","sha":"4eec6628e6f17fc9faafa975d1356593058f7e4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/4eec6628e6f17fc9faafa975d1356593058f7e4c"}],"sha":"14e89ddfab90307de6a570c2e8cebf8371ec5f95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/14e89ddfab90307de6a570c2e8cebf8371ec5f95"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/4eec6628e6f17fc9faafa975d1356593058f7e4c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T23:17:52Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T23:17:52Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"message":"Forage fish beaches: soft band with a drifting school instead of a hard line\n\nDocumented and potential spawning beaches draw as wide translucent bands\n(raspberry / pink), and a KelpOverlay ''beach'' style paints two to five small\nwhite fish per beach that drift slowly along it from zoom 13: solid for\ndocumented, outlined for potential. The band stays the click target.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1301f7e9e95444890e9d2fecc80c9e6a5f109cb1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/trees/1301f7e9e95444890e9d2fecc80c9e6a5f109cb1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/commits/4eec6628e6f17fc9faafa975d1356593058f7e4c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/4eec6628e6f17fc9faafa975d1356593058f7e4c","node_id":"C_kwDORPBA8toAKDRlZWM2NjI4ZTZmMTdmYzlmYWFmYTk3NWQxMzU2NTkzMDU4ZjdlNGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/dfd8f2ad3e2bed3457848470db7c104227863da6","sha":"dfd8f2ad3e2bed3457848470db7c104227863da6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/dfd8f2ad3e2bed3457848470db7c104227863da6"}],"sha":"4eec6628e6f17fc9faafa975d1356593058f7e4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/4eec6628e6f17fc9faafa975d1356593058f7e4c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/dfd8f2ad3e2bed3457848470db7c104227863da6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T23:05:46Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T23:05:46Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"message":"Kelp pins sit inside their patch: widest interior span on the patch''s mid-line, hole-aware\n\nThe vertex centroid of a crescent-shaped bed wrapped around a headland landed\non the rock; 218 of 855 pins were outside their patch. Now 0 are.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"419362c5a88d64182521439b44dd46801b78cb86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/trees/419362c5a88d64182521439b44dd46801b78cb86"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/commits/dfd8f2ad3e2bed3457848470db7c104227863da6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/dfd8f2ad3e2bed3457848470db7c104227863da6","node_id":"C_kwDORPBA8toAKGRmZDhmMmFkM2UyYmVkMzQ1Nzg0ODQ3MGRiN2MxMDQyMjc4NjNkYTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/ee45ec974a4baf5a0366018ba2f43eeb5540a19a","sha":"ee45ec974a4baf5a0366018ba2f43eeb5540a19a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/ee45ec974a4baf5a0366018ba2f43eeb5540a19a"}],"sha":"dfd8f2ad3e2bed3457848470db7c104227863da6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/dfd8f2ad3e2bed3457848470db7c104227863da6"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/ee45ec974a4baf5a0366018ba2f43eeb5540a19a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T23:03:13Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T23:03:13Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"message":"Kelp pins only on patches of 0.05 ac or more; tiny patches show canopy area in sq ft\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3e76d83e602263ec1334fc7b5eb846bd52b10af0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/trees/3e76d83e602263ec1334fc7b5eb846bd52b10af0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/commits/ee45ec974a4baf5a0366018ba2f43eeb5540a19a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/ee45ec974a4baf5a0366018ba2f43eeb5540a19a","node_id":"C_kwDORPBA8toAKGVlNDVlYzk3NGE0YmFmNWEwMzY2MDE4YmEyZjQzZWViNTU0MGExOWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/a79e9215c6f5f7f45677a089f255b2a457cb8240","sha":"a79e9215c6f5f7f45677a089f255b2a457cb8240","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/a79e9215c6f5f7f45677a089f255b2a457cb8240"}],"sha":"ee45ec974a4baf5a0366018ba2f43eeb5540a19a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/ee45ec974a4baf5a0366018ba2f43eeb5540a19a"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/a79e9215c6f5f7f45677a089f255b2a457cb8240/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T22:38:30Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T22:38:30Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"message":"Bull kelp: clickable squiggle pins on the larger patches, thinned by zoom like the eelgrass pins\n\nPolygon layers with a markerIcon now get one marker per patch at its centroid,\nranked by area for the zoom-grid thinning. The kelp pin reuses the legend''s\nnautical squiggle on a goldenrod disc; the squiggle fill stays as it was.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d87e06e0b008d4ccbd05af8e6ce08b78f336ba96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/trees/d87e06e0b008d4ccbd05af8e6ce08b78f336ba96"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/commits/a79e9215c6f5f7f45677a089f255b2a457cb8240","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/a79e9215c6f5f7f45677a089f255b2a457cb8240","node_id":"C_kwDORPBA8toAKGE3OWU5MjE1YzZmNWY3ZjQ1Njc3YTA4OWYyNTViMmE0NTdjYjgyNDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/61bdf0358d623ec2640e867a695953c272ae46e4","sha":"61bdf0358d623ec2640e867a695953c272ae46e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/61bdf0358d623ec2640e867a695953c272ae46e4"}],"sha":"a79e9215c6f5f7f45677a089f255b2a457cb8240","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/a79e9215c6f5f7f45677a089f255b2a457cb8240"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/61bdf0358d623ec2640e867a695953c272ae46e4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T21:22:08Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T21:22:08Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"message":"Popups: \"Why it matters\" only in Friends'' own words, with the source cited\n\n- New LayerConfig.whyItMatters (text + source) on 26 layers: verbatim\n  sentences from Living with the Shoreline, the kelp handout, or sanjuans.org\n  pages; a credit line renders under the block. Layers without sourced text\n  (Properties, Buildings, Lingcod & Greenling, Groins, Boat Ramps, Marine\n  Railways, eBird Hotspots) show no story block.\n- Friends'' Projects and the Related-content rows use the articles'' own\n  WordPress excerpts instead of enrichment summaries (excerpt added to the\n  content index).\n- Parcel Fish tab habitat notes, the Vegetation card note, and the inland\n  Upland stewardship text now quote the handout with the same credit.\n- Geology popup: shoreform definition credited to Friends'' mapping, then the\n  handout''s feeder-bluff text.\n- public/_popup-test.html renders popups without a map for checking.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"54304271d487dab53172a50b5f1d3d877330f5d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/trees/54304271d487dab53172a50b5f1d3d877330f5d5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/commits/61bdf0358d623ec2640e867a695953c272ae46e4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/61bdf0358d623ec2640e867a695953c272ae46e4","node_id":"C_kwDORPBA8toAKDYxYmRmMDM1OGQ2MjNlYzI2NDBlODY3YTY5NTk1M2MyNzJhZTQ2ZTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/e977694ecf62f4159ce03fc4f9ed28a65a3261e0","sha":"e977694ecf62f4159ce03fc4f9ed28a65a3261e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/e977694ecf62f4159ce03fc4f9ed28a65a3261e0"}],"sha":"61bdf0358d623ec2640e867a695953c272ae46e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/61bdf0358d623ec2640e867a695953c272ae46e4"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/e977694ecf62f4159ce03fc4f9ed28a65a3261e0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T21:07:14Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T21:07:14Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"message":"Armor popups: \"Why it matters\" in Friends'' own words from Living with the Shoreline\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2bb2ba9aaeee1fe56fbb197777d7415614ed91ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/trees/2bb2ba9aaeee1fe56fbb197777d7415614ed91ab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/commits/e977694ecf62f4159ce03fc4f9ed28a65a3261e0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/e977694ecf62f4159ce03fc4f9ed28a65a3261e0","node_id":"C_kwDORPBA8toAKGU5Nzc2OTRlY2Y2MmY0MTU5Y2UwM2ZjNGY5ZWQyOGE2NWEzMjYxZTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/65eb657fb53068dcc4bb8bcf74e609f21c8b6cdf","sha":"65eb657fb53068dcc4bb8bcf74e609f21c8b6cdf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/65eb657fb53068dcc4bb8bcf74e609f21c8b6cdf"}],"sha":"e977694ecf62f4159ce03fc4f9ed28a65a3261e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/e977694ecf62f4159ce03fc4f9ed28a65a3261e0"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/65eb657fb53068dcc4bb8bcf74e609f21c8b6cdf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T21:03:57Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T21:03:57Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"message":"Armor popups: \"Why it matters\" explains why armor matters; change status becomes a chip\n\nBoth armor layers'' story text now describes what hard armor does to a beach.\nThe 2009→2019 status (new / enlarged / removed / unchanged, or mapped in\n2009) is a chip under the title; the two-color key stays in the legend.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"07a0582f16dea0da5f5c0dd6c9c561a839f5ec7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/trees/07a0582f16dea0da5f5c0dd6c9c561a839f5ec7d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/commits/65eb657fb53068dcc4bb8bcf74e609f21c8b6cdf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/65eb657fb53068dcc4bb8bcf74e609f21c8b6cdf","node_id":"C_kwDORPBA8toAKDY1ZWI2NTdmYjUzMDY4ZGNjNGJiOGJjZjc0ZTYwOWYyMWM4YjZjZGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/0c252cb87083b9ddfd8ba57af3b5fc77df5fdff7","sha":"0c252cb87083b9ddfd8ba57af3b5fc77df5fdff7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/0c252cb87083b9ddfd8ba57af3b5fc77df5fdff7"}],"sha":"65eb657fb53068dcc4bb8bcf74e609f21c8b6cdf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/65eb657fb53068dcc4bb8bcf74e609f21c8b6cdf"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/0c252cb87083b9ddfd8ba57af3b5fc77df5fdff7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T21:02:35Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T21:02:35Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"message":"Popups: chips sit directly under the title; armor-change popup is item-specific\n\nChips are the facts that distinguish a feature, so they now come before the\nkey numbers and the story block in every popup. The Armor Change popup is\ntitled by its origin year, grades condition as chips (OK / functional but\nfailing / derelict), flags a toe below the high water line, and its story\ndescribes this segment instead of the layer''s color key.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1cbba39fbce1ebfaef529432f6505b600f2dd805","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/trees/1cbba39fbce1ebfaef529432f6505b600f2dd805"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/commits/0c252cb87083b9ddfd8ba57af3b5fc77df5fdff7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/0c252cb87083b9ddfd8ba57af3b5fc77df5fdff7","node_id":"C_kwDORPBA8toAKDBjMjUyY2I4NzA4M2I5ZGRmZDhiYTU3YWYzYjVmYzc3ZGY1ZmRmZjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/ff117834f253e983d670e18ee3d2a318c636ee7c","sha":"ff117834f253e983d670e18ee3d2a318c636ee7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/ff117834f253e983d670e18ee3d2a318c636ee7c"}],"sha":"0c252cb87083b9ddfd8ba57af3b5fc77df5fdff7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/0c252cb87083b9ddfd8ba57af3b5fc77df5fdff7"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/ff117834f253e983d670e18ee3d2a318c636ee7c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T20:56:37Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T20:56:37Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"message":"Popups: related-article block reads \"Related content from Friends of the San Juans\"\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e8a2f712f93679ca0f369395dde2ef1056def5af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/trees/e8a2f712f93679ca0f369395dde2ef1056def5af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/commits/ff117834f253e983d670e18ee3d2a318c636ee7c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/ff117834f253e983d670e18ee3d2a318c636ee7c","node_id":"C_kwDORPBA8toAKGZmMTE3ODM0ZjI1M2U5ODNkNjcwZTE4ZWUzZDJhMzE4YzYzNmVlN2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/dc84cea22fbfa09223ad87e447212f9875db854d","sha":"dc84cea22fbfa09223ad87e447212f9875db854d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/dc84cea22fbfa09223ad87e447212f9875db854d"}],"sha":"ff117834f253e983d670e18ee3d2a318c636ee7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/ff117834f253e983d670e18ee3d2a318c636ee7c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/dc84cea22fbfa09223ad87e447212f9875db854d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T20:54:47Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T20:54:47Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"message":"Shoreline armor: drop the duplicate 2019 layer, popup led by material and what it protects\n\n\"Shoreline Armor\" and \"Shoreline Armor (2019)\" were the same 1,006-segment\nfile; the survivor is \"Shoreline Armor (2019 survey)\". Its popup now titles\nby material and structure (\"Rock bulkhead\", \"Concrete seawall\"), subtitles\nisland · length · condition, chips what the armor protects with warnings\nfor a toe below the high tide line, feeder bluffs, spawning beaches and\ncreosote, and tells the 2009→2019 change story. The duplicate id is also\nremoved from the category trees (seed + live GCS config).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"21ba51b3512da460fb8e0f5680f79a3ed677d58e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/trees/21ba51b3512da460fb8e0f5680f79a3ed677d58e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/commits/dc84cea22fbfa09223ad87e447212f9875db854d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/dc84cea22fbfa09223ad87e447212f9875db854d","node_id":"C_kwDORPBA8toAKGRjODRjZWEyMmZiZmEwOTIyM2FkODdlNDQ3MjEyZjk4NzVkYjg1NGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/55d98610bd591039606d99c05378f65b5d9a5fad","sha":"55d98610bd591039606d99c05378f65b5d9a5fad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/55d98610bd591039606d99c05378f65b5d9a5fad"}],"sha":"dc84cea22fbfa09223ad87e447212f9875db854d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/dc84cea22fbfa09223ad87e447212f9875db854d"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/55d98610bd591039606d99c05378f65b5d9a5fad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T20:25:07Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T20:25:07Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"message":"Recompute per-parcel NDVI classes in Earth Engine with breaks calibrated to the October 2023 scene\n\nscripts/ee-ndvi-parcel-stats.py rebuilds public/data/ndvi_parcel_stats.json\n(reduceRegions over the NAIP 2023 mosaic at 2 m, ~3 min). Breaks come from\nsampling NDVI inside NLCD 2021 classes: water < -0.10, bare -0.10–0.08,\ngrass 0.08–0.20, shrubs 0.20–0.29, tree canopy 0.29–0.35, dense forest\n> 0.35. Means are unchanged (max diff 0.009); the class bar now splits\ncanopy from shrub instead of lumping all forest into \"shrubs\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cab348319c1c93554cf558c7eadc9e18c7cde486","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/trees/cab348319c1c93554cf558c7eadc9e18c7cde486"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/commits/55d98610bd591039606d99c05378f65b5d9a5fad","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/55d98610bd591039606d99c05378f65b5d9a5fad","node_id":"C_kwDORPBA8toAKDU1ZDk4NjEwYmQ1OTEwMzk2MDZkOTljMDUzNzhmNjViNWQ5YTVmYWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/a6d59563592d3bf0fae4177ef4b3d03b3a51e3d5","sha":"a6d59563592d3bf0fae4177ef4b3d03b3a51e3d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/a6d59563592d3bf0fae4177ef4b3d03b3a51e3d5"}],"sha":"55d98610bd591039606d99c05378f65b5d9a5fad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/55d98610bd591039606d99c05378f65b5d9a5fad"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/a6d59563592d3bf0fae4177ef4b3d03b3a51e3d5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T20:13:31Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T20:13:31Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"message":"Vegetation: land-cover labels calibrated to the October 2023 NAIP scene\n\nMature conifer canopy reads NDVI ~0.3–0.45 in this scene (county parcel\nmaximum 0.41), so the fixed 0.5 / 0.7 \"Trees\" / \"Dense Forest\" bands never\noccurred and every forest parcel was labeled \"Shrubs / Garden\". The bar now\nshows Tree canopy / forest (> 0.3) and Grass, shrubs, open woodland\n(0.15–0.3); the data-reference modal explains the calibration.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5b2f92aaba90cdb909742221b69ed6cf53a47eb5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/trees/5b2f92aaba90cdb909742221b69ed6cf53a47eb5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/commits/a6d59563592d3bf0fae4177ef4b3d03b3a51e3d5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/a6d59563592d3bf0fae4177ef4b3d03b3a51e3d5","node_id":"C_kwDORPBA8toAKGE2ZDU5NTYzNTkyZDNiZjBmYWU0MTc3ZWY0YjNkMDNiM2E1MWUzZDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/e6921be2cde74a5d65ee869ea3ac1ccba7eacae5","sha":"e6921be2cde74a5d65ee869ea3ac1ccba7eacae5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/e6921be2cde74a5d65ee869ea3ac1ccba7eacae5"}],"sha":"a6d59563592d3bf0fae4177ef4b3d03b3a51e3d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/a6d59563592d3bf0fae4177ef4b3d03b3a51e3d5"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/e6921be2cde74a5d65ee869ea3ac1ccba7eacae5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T20:02:14Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T20:02:14Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"message":"Shoreline Geology on by default from zoom 13, with a wide invisible click target\n\nThin line layers can declare hitStrokeWeight: an invisible 14 px line is\ndrawn beneath and its clicks are re-dispatched to the visible layer, so a\nnear miss still opens the segment popup.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"146cfb9799edb82f2bbba92970e08ef7098b6243","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/trees/146cfb9799edb82f2bbba92970e08ef7098b6243"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/commits/e6921be2cde74a5d65ee869ea3ac1ccba7eacae5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/e6921be2cde74a5d65ee869ea3ac1ccba7eacae5","node_id":"C_kwDORPBA8toAKGU2OTIxYmUyY2RlNzRhNWQ2NWVlODY5ZWEzYWMxY2NiYTdlYWNhZTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/4f7a736f0ce45bb64f3d6104ae5a42171e52ed06","sha":"4f7a736f0ce45bb64f3d6104ae5a42171e52ed06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/4f7a736f0ce45bb64f3d6104ae5a42171e52ed06"}],"sha":"e6921be2cde74a5d65ee869ea3ac1ccba7eacae5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/e6921be2cde74a5d65ee869ea3ac1ccba7eacae5"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/4f7a736f0ce45bb64f3d6104ae5a42171e52ed06/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T19:53:48Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T19:53:48Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"message":"Forage fish: one family of layer names, potential habitat never on bedrock, \"why it is here\" reasons\n\n- Layers renamed: \"Forage Fish Spawning: Herring\", \"Forage Fish Beach Spawning:\n  Smelt & Sand Lance (documented / potential)\"\n- Precompute: potential beach habitat counts only where it fronts the parcel\n  (25 ft) and never when the parcel''s own shoreform is Rocky Shoreline;\n  documented beaches keep 200 ft. Records carry the matched shoreform and\n  distance, and herring carries its distance\n- Fish tab: herring first, then beach spawners, each with the distance and\n  shoreform that put it there; species codes rendered as plain names\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"215dbfc4e0fbcd9d8f51ebe185f2df73cf83382f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/trees/215dbfc4e0fbcd9d8f51ebe185f2df73cf83382f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/commits/4f7a736f0ce45bb64f3d6104ae5a42171e52ed06","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/4f7a736f0ce45bb64f3d6104ae5a42171e52ed06","node_id":"C_kwDORPBA8toAKDRmN2E3MzZmMGNlNDViYjY0ZjNkNjEwNGFlNWE0MjE3MWU1MmVkMDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/7201db9e67771a354ace46d4b2c05e3abe380c0e","sha":"7201db9e67771a354ace46d4b2c05e3abe380c0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/7201db9e67771a354ace46d4b2c05e3abe380c0e"}],"sha":"4f7a736f0ce45bb64f3d6104ae5a42171e52ed06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/4f7a736f0ce45bb64f3d6104ae5a42171e52ed06"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/7201db9e67771a354ace46d4b2c05e3abe380c0e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T05:08:03Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T05:08:03Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"message":"Load data layers only when they are on; cut phone canvas and deck memory\n\nEvery vector dataset was fetched at startup whether shown or not, which was\nenough to crash the WebKit process behind Chrome on iPhone. Layers now load\nthe first time they are switched on (toggleLayer / setAllVisible /\nURL `l=`), the sidebar switch is enabled before load, and on phones the\nkelp and herring overlay bitmaps drop to 1× with a quarter-viewport pad\nand deck.gl renders at 1×.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d887c5c0555eb6849ef6359e9250f5684efa784d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/trees/d887c5c0555eb6849ef6359e9250f5684efa784d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/commits/7201db9e67771a354ace46d4b2c05e3abe380c0e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/7201db9e67771a354ace46d4b2c05e3abe380c0e","node_id":"C_kwDORPBA8toAKDcyMDFkYjllNjc3NzFhMzU0YWNlNDZkNGIyYzA1ZTNhYmUzODBjMGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/73d7303c6cb0598d911c495e9dfd4becd9105ba6","sha":"73d7303c6cb0598d911c495e9dfd4becd9105ba6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/73d7303c6cb0598d911c495e9dfd4becd9105ba6"}],"sha":"7201db9e67771a354ace46d4b2c05e3abe380c0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/7201db9e67771a354ace46d4b2c05e3abe380c0e"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/73d7303c6cb0598d911c495e9dfd4becd9105ba6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T04:35:06Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T04:35:06Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"message":"Phone layout, herring school animation, buoys/docks on by default, real structure photos\n\n- Phone (<640 px): 64 px header with wordmark and a ⋮ menu for Share and\n  Resources; legend as a \"Layers\" pill + bottom sheet with persistent state;\n  popups as a bottom sheet (popupSheet.ts) with the same events as the\n  InfoWindow; no zoom/fullscreen/rotate/camera controls, basemap picker\n  bottom-left; footer is copyright + logo; welcome card uses pinch wording;\n  full-width sidebar; _mobile-test.html harness\n- Herring Spawning Grounds: drifting school of fish painted over the fill\n  from zoom 13 (KelpOverlay ''school'' style)\n- Mooring Buoys & Floats and Docks on by default from zoom 16\n- Boat Ramps marker uses Scott de Jonge''s boat-ramp glyph (CC BY 4.0)\n- Mooring buoy and dock popups use Friends'' own photos\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"55f8d40f8a2badddb39350542fc96d7b940e299f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/trees/55f8d40f8a2badddb39350542fc96d7b940e299f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/commits/73d7303c6cb0598d911c495e9dfd4becd9105ba6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/73d7303c6cb0598d911c495e9dfd4becd9105ba6","node_id":"C_kwDORPBA8toAKDczZDczMDNjNmNiMDU5OGQ5MTFjNDk1ZTlkZmQ0YmVjZDkxMDViYTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/9ce2f1ac2c1e7da12ae625adb9e6abaa1f17e6aa","sha":"9ce2f1ac2c1e7da12ae625adb9e6abaa1f17e6aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/9ce2f1ac2c1e7da12ae625adb9e6abaa1f17e6aa"}],"sha":"73d7303c6cb0598d911c495e9dfd4becd9105ba6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/73d7303c6cb0598d911c495e9dfd4becd9105ba6"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/9ce2f1ac2c1e7da12ae625adb9e6abaa1f17e6aa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T03:27:10Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T03:27:10Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"message":"Properties: rename layer, draw from zoom 13.5, inland Summary cards, no dollar values\n\n- \"Tax Parcels\" is now \"Properties\"; boundaries draw from zoom 13.5 (deck tile\n  extent set so z13 tiles load below the rounding threshold)\n- Inland parcels (nothing within the nearshore distances) drop the Shoreline,\n  Fish and Modifications tabs and get: distance to the nearest shoreline by\n  name, greenery card with a note on how tree cover helps beaches and\n  nearshore water (from Friends'' vegetation/restoration pages), Friends''\n  projects on the same island, and an upland stewardship card with Friends\n  articles from a new upland-property content bucket\n- Precompute adds nearest-shoreline distance for every parcel\n- Summary tab no longer shows assessed value or last sale\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1dcc2ba508d0c147677d4118b8ac65d6fb98ba2f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/trees/1dcc2ba508d0c147677d4118b8ac65d6fb98ba2f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/commits/9ce2f1ac2c1e7da12ae625adb9e6abaa1f17e6aa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/9ce2f1ac2c1e7da12ae625adb9e6abaa1f17e6aa","node_id":"C_kwDORPBA8toAKDljZTJmMWFjMmMxZTdkYTEyYWU2MjVhZGI5ZTZhYmFhMWYxN2U2YWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/b8ff7b15d4cbfca8007aa627d6094f405ed81559","sha":"b8ff7b15d4cbfca8007aa627d6094f405ed81559","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/b8ff7b15d4cbfca8007aa627d6094f405ed81559"}],"sha":"9ce2f1ac2c1e7da12ae625adb9e6abaa1f17e6aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/9ce2f1ac2c1e7da12ae625adb9e6abaa1f17e6aa"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/b8ff7b15d4cbfca8007aa627d6094f405ed81559/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T21:29:35Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T21:29:35Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"message":"Popups: subject-matched photos, per-feature article ranking, sticky close; report pages match app chrome\n\n- Photos chosen by caption subject per layer (PHOTO_SUBJECTS), curated\n  handout photo first; projects keep their own before/after images\n- From Friends ranked per feature by island and place names, listed\n  newest first; no blank thumbnails for articles without images\n- Popup close button is sticky and translucent while scrolling\n- Report pages: slate header without the globe, grouped Resources menu,\n  matching footer\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6723cac382245ae96abc55aad4072fa729cad10f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/trees/6723cac382245ae96abc55aad4072fa729cad10f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/commits/b8ff7b15d4cbfca8007aa627d6094f405ed81559","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/b8ff7b15d4cbfca8007aa627d6094f405ed81559","node_id":"C_kwDORPBA8toAKGI4ZmY3YjE1ZDRjYmZjYTgwMDdhYTYyN2Q2MDk0ZjQwNWVkODE1NTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/c70a9391102ba7f79df5218201a7437fbef5d9a7","sha":"c70a9391102ba7f79df5218201a7437fbef5d9a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/c70a9391102ba7f79df5218201a7437fbef5d9a7"}],"sha":"b8ff7b15d4cbfca8007aa627d6094f405ed81559","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/b8ff7b15d4cbfca8007aa627d6094f405ed81559"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/c70a9391102ba7f79df5218201a7437fbef5d9a7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T20:59:27Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T20:59:27Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"message":"Keep point icons on the mixed Friends'' Projects layer when it restyles on zoom\n\nThe line-with-midpoint-markers restyle applied a line-only style to the\nwhole Data layer, so the layer''s point features fell back to Google''s\ndefault red marker after any zoom. Points now keep their icon (and the\nFriends-pin spacing) while lines keep their stroke.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9175eb76adfbd0d8ece50b43278aa045bf8084a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/trees/9175eb76adfbd0d8ece50b43278aa045bf8084a4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/commits/c70a9391102ba7f79df5218201a7437fbef5d9a7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/c70a9391102ba7f79df5218201a7437fbef5d9a7","node_id":"C_kwDORPBA8toAKGM3MGE5MzkxMTAyYmE3Zjc5ZGY1MjE4MjAxYTc0MzdmYmVmNWQ5YTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/694b77f2af39a323968c52b0a8968fa94c4641ab","sha":"694b77f2af39a323968c52b0a8968fa94c4641ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/694b77f2af39a323968c52b0a8968fa94c4641ab"}],"sha":"c70a9391102ba7f79df5218201a7437fbef5d9a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/c70a9391102ba7f79df5218201a7437fbef5d9a7"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/694b77f2af39a323968c52b0a8968fa94c4641ab/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T20:57:31Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T20:57:31Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"message":"Legend drawer with icon rail, marker spacing around Friends'' pins, clickable eelgrass pins\n\n- Legend: larger type; left-edge drawer that slides open on first load,\n  x to close, pull handle; collapses to an icon rail where each swatch\n  toggles its layer; no \"not in view\" wording\n- Turning a gated layer on below its minZoom lifts the gate; overrides\n  persist in the URL (zo=) and restore from shared links\n- Other marker layers keep clear of Friends'' Projects pins (34 px),\n  re-spaced on zoom and once the Friends layer loads\n- Midpoint markers (eelgrass) are clickable and open the line''s popup\n- Friends'' Projects markers at 1.5x\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"48015d59730f49a0dfedd16e504867ca35195927","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/trees/48015d59730f49a0dfedd16e504867ca35195927"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/commits/694b77f2af39a323968c52b0a8968fa94c4641ab","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/694b77f2af39a323968c52b0a8968fa94c4641ab","node_id":"C_kwDORPBA8toAKDY5NGI3N2YyYWYzOWEzMjM5NjhjNTJiMGE4OTY4ZmE5NGM0NjQxYWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/1204ade39eb95e6bb7e58b8ccf71c0dfc9562cff","sha":"1204ade39eb95e6bb7e58b8ccf71c0dfc9562cff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/1204ade39eb95e6bb7e58b8ccf71c0dfc9562cff"}],"sha":"694b77f2af39a323968c52b0a8968fa94c4641ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/694b77f2af39a323968c52b0a8968fa94c4641ab"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/1204ade39eb95e6bb7e58b8ccf71c0dfc9562cff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T20:33:30Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T20:33:30Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"message":"Friends'' Projects layer, Friends website content in popups, legend show/hide and zoom overrides\n\n- friends-projects: one always-on layer merging restoration, riparian,\n  in/over-water structure, and restoration-site files (owner names\n  dropped; scripts/build-friends-projects.py with corrected, checked\n  project links); target-over-water markers colored by type at 1.5x;\n  header placeholder globe removed\n- Friends website content: WordPress-API harvest + per-article\n  enrichment + index (public/data/friends-content.json); popups draw\n  photos, project summaries, and a From Friends article list from it\n- Legend: click a name to hide/show (row stays), x removes; the\n  \"zoom in\" hint forces a gated layer on at the current zoom\n- Eelgrass midpoint markers thin by a zoom-dependent grid\n- markerIconByProperty + markerScale on LayerConfig\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7687e9da2eabfe20bda712959433d5bf2863e891","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/trees/7687e9da2eabfe20bda712959433d5bf2863e891"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/commits/1204ade39eb95e6bb7e58b8ccf71c0dfc9562cff","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/1204ade39eb95e6bb7e58b8ccf71c0dfc9562cff","node_id":"C_kwDORPBA8toAKDEyMDRhZGUzOWViOTVlNmJiN2U1OGI4Y2NmNzFjMGRmYzk1NjJjZmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/c0a9af66ca12ac22e49d22e53c104269e043420f","sha":"c0a9af66ca12ac22e49d22e53c104269e043420f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/c0a9af66ca12ac22e49d22e53c104269e043420f"}],"sha":"1204ade39eb95e6bb7e58b8ccf71c0dfc9562cff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/1204ade39eb95e6bb7e58b8ccf71c0dfc9562cff"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/c0a9af66ca12ac22e49d22e53c104269e043420f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T17:12:39Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T17:12:39Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"message":"Parcels and buildings from vector tiles via deck.gl; drop the 150 MB downloads\n\n- DeckLayers.ts: GoogleMapsOverlay (classic mode) hosting MVTLayers styled\n  from the layer config; clicks re-broadcast as ssx-deck-click\n- tax-parcels / building-footprints: tiles on gs://salish-ndvi-tiles/tiles\n  (tippecanoe z13–16 / z14–16), no GeoJSON fetch\n- parcelDetail.ts: per-parcel JSON (full geometry + nearby buildings) and a\n  bbox index for point-in-parcel lookups and island percentiles\n- Radius report reads parcels/buildings from deck''s loaded tiles\n- scripts/build-parcel-files.py; README documents the tile pipeline\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"41aa10b177ae8f5612a49d7f5ce87a080275be03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/trees/41aa10b177ae8f5612a49d7f5ce87a080275be03"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/commits/c0a9af66ca12ac22e49d22e53c104269e043420f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/c0a9af66ca12ac22e49d22e53c104269e043420f","node_id":"C_kwDORPBA8toAKGMwYTlhZjY2Y2ExMmFjMjJlNDlkMjJlNTNjMTA0MjY5ZTA0MzQyMGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/02c0cd86f19654126decf5f6de0d7dbec610eb90","sha":"02c0cd86f19654126decf5f6de0d7dbec610eb90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/02c0cd86f19654126decf5f6de0d7dbec610eb90"}],"sha":"c0a9af66ca12ac22e49d22e53c104269e043420f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/c0a9af66ca12ac22e49d22e53c104269e043420f"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/02c0cd86f19654126decf5f6de0d7dbec610eb90/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T01:55:57Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T01:55:57Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"message":"Parcel report: seven tabs driven by the precompute\n\n- Tabs: Summary · Shoreline · Fish · Wildlife · Modifications · Vegetation · Property\n- Precompute adds Beamer & Fresh fish scores (segments within 200 ft) and\n  shoreline modifications (armor 50 ft, structures 100 ft, buoys 300 ft);\n  shoreform and forage distances widened to 200 ft\n- Fish tab works with no layer on; Wildlife adds an EarthAtlas whale-sightings\n  link at zoom 12 on the parcel; Modifications prints its search distances\n  and ends with the Friends site-visit CTA; Greenery moves to Vegetation;\n  Buildings and appraised value fold into Property (not featured)\n- Footer credit follows the active tab, source first\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"67c7e7f790ab26a724b3109caa039e5398a76fe9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/trees/67c7e7f790ab26a724b3109caa039e5398a76fe9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/commits/02c0cd86f19654126decf5f6de0d7dbec610eb90","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/02c0cd86f19654126decf5f6de0d7dbec610eb90","node_id":"C_kwDORPBA8toAKDAyYzBjZDg2ZjE5NjU0MTI2ZGVjZjVmNmRlMGQ3ZGJlYzYxMGViOTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jknauernever/salish-prop/commit/2ba6aadb8419cf364e8f813c0bf7606d7ce58267","sha":"2ba6aadb8419cf364e8f813c0bf7606d7ce58267","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/2ba6aadb8419cf364e8f813c0bf7606d7ce58267"}],"sha":"02c0cd86f19654126decf5f6de0d7dbec610eb90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/02c0cd86f19654126decf5f6de0d7dbec610eb90"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/commits/2ba6aadb8419cf364e8f813c0bf7606d7ce58267/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T00:01:59Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T00:01:59Z","email":"josh@knauernever.com","name":"Josh Knauer"},"message":"Spawning layers draw from zoom 12 instead of 14\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"03f87e430b3ce712c0327a61563cf706ca4a7fd9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/trees/03f87e430b3ce712c0327a61563cf706ca4a7fd9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jknauernever/salish-prop/git/commits/2ba6aadb8419cf364e8f813c0bf7